{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'C:\\\\Users\\\\dasbl\\\\.agents\\\\skills\\\\legion\\\\SKILL.md'\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: legion\ndescription: Bridge Codex requests to the Legion workflow installed at C:/Users/dasbl/.legion when the user references Legion or any legacy /legion:* command.\n---\n\n# Legion for Codex\n\nLegion's canonical Codex entry point is `/prompts:legion`. It accepts the same workflow language as the terminal CLI: `legion start`, `legion plan`, `legion build`, `legion review`, and related commands.\n\nCodex custom prompts are kept as compatibility aliases because current Codex guidance prefers skills for reusable workflows. This bridge skill keeps plain-language Legion requests and legacy `/legion:*` aliases routed to the same workflow contract.\n\n## Native Prompt Mapping\n\n- `legion <command>` -> `/prompts:legion` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion.md`\n- `legion start` -> `/prompts:legion-start` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-start.md`\n- `legion plan` -> `/prompts:legion-plan` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-plan.md`\n- `legion build` -> `/prompts:legion-build` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-build.md`\n- `legion review` -> `/prompts:legion-review` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-review.md`\n- `legion status` -> `/prompts:legion-status` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-status.md`\n- `legion quick` -> `/prompts:legion-quick` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-quick.md`\n- `legion advise` -> `/prompts:legion-advise` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-advise.md`\n- `legion portfolio` -> `/prompts:legion-portfolio` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-portfolio.md`\n- `legion milestone` -> `/prompts:legion-milestone` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-milestone.md`\n- `legion agent` -> `/prompts:legion-agent` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-agent.md`\n- `legion map` -> `/prompts:legion-map` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-map.md`\n- `legion explore` -> `/prompts:legion-explore` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-explore.md`\n- `legion board` -> `/prompts:legion-board` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-board.md`\n- `legion retro` -> `/prompts:legion-retro` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-retro.md`\n- `legion ship` -> `/prompts:legion-ship` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-ship.md`\n- `legion learn` -> `/prompts:legion-learn` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-learn.md`\n- `legion polish` -> `/prompts:legion-polish` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-polish.md`\n- `legion update` -> `/prompts:legion-update` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-update.md`\n- `legion validate` -> `/prompts:legion-validate` -> `C:/Users/dasbl/.codex/prompts/legion-validate.md`\n\n## How To Use\n\n1. Prefer the installed `legion` skill or `/prompts:legion` prompt when the user wants Legion.\n2. If the user types a legacy `/legion:*` alias and Codex reports it as unrecognized, map it to the matching command above.\n3. If the user mentions Legion in plain language, treat it as the same intent and follow the matching Legion workflow.\n4. Load only the matching Legion command markdown and only the files named in its `<execution_context>`.\n5. Use the current project's `.planning/PROJECT.md`, `.planning/ROADMAP.md`, and `.planning/STATE.md` when the Legion workflow expects project state.\n6. For install or update requests, check `C:/Users/dasbl/.legion/manifest.json` first and use `C:/Users/dasbl/.legion/commands/legion/update.md` as the workflow reference.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Do not claim that legacy `/legion:*` aliases are native Codex commands unless the runtime explicitly resolves them.\n- Prefer `/prompts:legion` and the `legion` skill before per-command prompt aliases.\n- Do not bulk-load all Legion skills. Follow the target command's execution context and keep context narrow.\n- Prefer the Codex adapter at `C:/Users/dasbl/.legion/adapters/codex-cli.md` when Legion behavior depends on runtime capabilities.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
