-1`; `cargo run -p xtask -- golden-path-2`; `cargo run -p xtask -- golden-path-3`; `cargo run -p xtask -- golden-path-4`; `cargo run -p xtask -- perf-harness`; `cargo run -p xtask -- verify-perf-harness`; `cargo run -p xtask -- update-drill`; local full phase-gate scripts run `cargo deny check` when cargo-deny is installed. GitHub Actions workflows: `.github/workflows/legion-gates.yml` runs the standing gate set (xtask gates, fmt/check/test/clippy, cargo-deny, report-only skeleton perf-harness, rust-analyzer smoke) on ubuntu/windows/macos for every push to main and every PR; `.github/workflows/legion-bench.yml` runs the weekly recorded-mode legion-bench with **synthetic budget-arithmetic scoring** (does not open fixture repos or run agents; `scoring_mode=synthetic_budget_arithmetic`; live provider calls are a future M13 scope); `.github/workflows/legion-smoke.yml` runs the GP-1/2/3/4 golden-path smokes and the update-drill (headless delegate mode flows: fixture edit/LSP/git for GP-1; scope/sandbox/kill-switch for GP-2; full delegate task loop with scope denial and evidence TOML for GP-3; automate multi-agent workflow evidence for GP-4; deterministic update/rollback with ephemeral key for the update-drill) on dispatch and weekly (Mondays 06:00 UTC) on the 3-OS matrix — it is an INDEPENDENT workflow and failures do NOT block PR merges. Promote smoke to merge-blocking only after the criteria in `docs/OPERATOR_RUNBOOK.md` (four consecutive green 3-OS scheduled runs + owner sign-off). Local gates remain the primary verification source until the hosted gate history is proven stable; the evals/training pytest suite is local-only for now.\r\n.\\AGENTS.md:17:- `cargo run -p legion-app -- <path>` opens the current directory as a trusted workspace and supports only `:w`/`:q`; it is a CLI shell proof, not the real renderer.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-ui\\src\\ui.rs:325:    /// Short icon label for renderers that do not have an icon set.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-ui\\src\\ui.rs:403:/// as 