onfiguration.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:93:/// Metadata-only Manual renderer performance report.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:189:            \"desktop egui projection render path stayed within Manual latency budgets\".to_string()\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:192:                \"Manual renderer measurement exceeded budget: keypress_p50={}us/{}us, keypress_p95={}us/{}us, scroll_p95={}us/{}us\",\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:240:/// Run the Manual renderer performance measurement and write its TOML report.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:246:            format!(\"Manual renderer measurement failed: {error}\"),\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:269:    let renderer = ManualPerfRenderer::default();\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:270:    renderer.render_once(&mut runtime)?;\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:282:        renderer.render_once(&mut runtime)?;\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:298:        renderer.render_once(&mut runtime)?;\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\manual_perf.rs:314:    context: egui::Context,\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\main.rs:1://! Legion IDE renderer-backed desktop entry point.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\lib.rs:1://! Renderer-backed desktop adapter for Legion IDE.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\lib.rs:3://! This crate owns native windowing, renderer resources, and adapter-local\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\harness.rs:1://! Headless test harness for the desktop adapter.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\harness.rs:3://! This module provides the documented seam between the headless egui/eframe\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\harness.rs:4://! test path and the production desktop adapter. It exists so that tests can\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\harness.rs:5://! exercise the real `DesktopEframeApp` / `egui::Context` input path without\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\harness.rs:6://! requiring a real `winit` window, while making it explicit that:\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\harness.rs:9://! * `legion-desktop` is a renderer/adapter; it may own adapter-local view\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\diagnostics.rs:26:    /// Crate version of the desktop adapter.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\src\\bridge.rs:58:/// Adapter-local renderer action before app routing.\r\n.\\crates\\legion-desktop\\Cargo.toml:27:egui = { workspace = true }\r\n.\\.planning\\codebase\\symbols.json:113:      \"summary\": \"Renderer-backed desktop adapter\",\r\n.\\.planning\\codebase\\symbols.json:291:      \"name\": \"eframe/egui\",\r\n.\\.planning\\codebase\\symbols.json:294:      \"summary\": \"Desktop renderer dependencies isolated to legion-desktop\",\r\n.\\.planning\\codebase\\symbols.json:317:      \"summary\": \"Desktop owns renderer/presentation only\",\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:16:  - There is no current GUI framework dependency in `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, or `crates/devil-ui/Cargo.toml` for GPUI, egui/eframe, winit, wgpu, Slint, Tauri, WRY, GTK, or similar GUI stacks.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:18:  - `plans/spikes/SPIKE-001A-result.md` accepts the native shell proof with renderer reservations: GPU/compositor frame variance, native IME, native clipboard, native focus, and accessibility tree validation remain renderer-integration follow-ups.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:20:  - Local architecture docs recommend a Rust-native GPU/editor shell direction, but current external primary sources make the renderer choice non-trivial: GPUI is still pre-1.0 and its README currently says macOS or Linux; egui/eframe supports native Windows/macOS/Linux and web/mobile targets but is immediate-mode and not native-looking; Tauri/WRY uses OS webviews and message passing; AccessKit is the current Rust accessibility infrastructure to plan around for custom UI toolkits.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:23:  - The next roadmap should be a productization track, not another platform-substrate track. The critical path is renderer-backed GUI integration, native input/accessibility/platform behavior, user-visible editor workflows, and packaging.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:25:  - Because the project has Windows-first evidence and GPUI's current public README does not claim Windows support, the renderer milestone must include a decision gate rather than assuming GPUI as the dependency.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:39:  - Convert the existing CLI/projection substrate into a renderer-backed desktop IDE that can be used for normal development workflows.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:44:  - Do not add a GUI framework as a drive-by dependency without a renderer ADR, proof spike, dependency-policy update, and platform evidence.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:50:Use a balanced productization track: add a new renderer-backed desktop adapter around the existing projection and intent boundary, then promote one user-visible workflow at a time until the IDE is daily-drivable.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:52:The key architectural move is to keep `devil-ui` as the projection model and command-intent layer, and add a separate renderer/application-shell integration crate or binary such as `devil-desktop` only after a renderer ADR is accepted. That GUI adapter consumes `ShellProjectionSnapshot` and emits `CommandDispatchIntent` values. `devil-app` remains the composition and authority layer for editor, workspace, proposal, AI, plugin, collaboration, remote, terminal, storage, policy, and observability.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:56:- Primary strategic target: Rust-native editor-grade renderer with strong control over text, GPU composition, key input, IME, clipboard, focus, accessibility, and multi-panel layout.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:57:- Fast fallback: egui/eframe if the goal is a Windows-first usable desktop GUI quickly and the immediate-mode tradeoffs are acceptable.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:59:- Accessibility requirement: plan an AccessKit tree or equivalent from the first renderer milestone, not after visual polish.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:61:This approach is recommended because the local codebase already has the hard safety substrate. The highest risk now is accidentally bypassing that substrate in the GUI, or choosing a renderer that cannot satisfy editor-grade input/accessibility/platform requirements.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:68:| Balanced: renderer-backed desktop adapter over existing projections | Preserves existing boundaries; creates real GUI milestones; allows renderer proof before commitment | Requires a new ADR, dependency policy, and platform evidence before implementation | Recommended |\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:69:| Ambitious: adopt a full native GPU/editor framework immediately | Fastest route to a Zed-like product shape if the framework fits | High framework/platform risk, especially Windows-first support and pre-1.0 churn | Use only after the renderer proof passes |\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:77:- [ ] Accept a renderer integration ADR that chooses the GUI stack and records fallback criteria.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:78:- [ ] Add a renderer-backed desktop adapter that opens a native window and renders layout, explorer, active buffer viewport, status, and proposal/trust summaries from projections.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:86:- [ ] Add renderer-backed performance evidence: p50/p95 input-to-paint, frame-time variance, large-file degraded mode, and non-blocking background work.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:92:- [ ] macOS and Linux parity with the same renderer/input/accessibility evidence.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:114:### M0: Baseline Reconciliation and Renderer Decision\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:116:**Goal**: Establish the exact current state and choose a GUI renderer path without weakening architecture gates.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:119:- Update or supersede the phase ledger so it agrees with the newer Phase 8 evidence, or explicitly mark the conflict as unresolved for this GUI track.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:120:- Add a renderer integration ADR that evaluates Rust-native GPU, egui/eframe, Slint, and Tauri/WRY against Windows-first GUI IDE requirements.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:122:- Update dependency policy and `xtask` checks before introducing renderer dependencies.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:246:  - Create the renderer crate/binary after M0 ADR/policy acceptance.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:249:- M1.2 Projection renderer:\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:267:  - Add a scripted smoke check if the renderer supports automation.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:274:- Stop if renderer latency cannot be measured.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:276:- Stop if dependency policy cannot express the renderer stack cleanly.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:283:- Add a renderer adapter crate only after M0. Candidate name: `devil-desktop`.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:284:- `devil-desktop` depends on `devil-app`, `devil-ui`, `devil-protocol`, and renderer-specific crates approved by policy.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:285:- Avoid renderer dependencies in `devil-editor`, `devil-project`, `devil-text`, `devil-index`, `devil-ai`, `devil-plugin`, `devil-collaboration`, `devil-remote`, `devil-terminal`, `devil-storage`, `devil-security`, and `devil-observability`.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:289:  - Side effects: none except renderer/window/platform UI side effects.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:323:- egui/eframe README, current public state: https://github.com/emilk/egui\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:330:- Which renderer stack should be approved for M1? Resolution path: M0 renderer ADR and spike.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:331:- Should the Phase 8 ledger/evidence conflict be fixed in `plans/phase-status-ledger.md`, or should the GUI track create its own baseline without editing historical phase status? Resolution path: M0 baseline reconciliation.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:342:- M0: Baseline reconciliation and renderer decision.\r\n.\\.planning\\explorations\\2026-05-26-gui-ide-roadmap-design.md:351:First build milestone should be M1 only after M0 is accepted. M1 delivers a native window, projection renderer, intent bridge, open/edit/save loop, conflict/rejection UI, and renderer evidence harness while preserving projection-only UI boundaries.\r\n.\\.planning\\config\\directory-mappings.yaml:40:    description: \"Renderer-backed desktop adapter, view, bridge, workflow, session, search, smoke, and metrics\"\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:19:Legion IDE is a Rust 2024 Cargo workspace for a local-first IDE. The current product track is GUI productization: the repo now contains both the legacy `legion-app` CLI shell proof and the newer `legion-desktop` renderer-backed adapter. Product authority remains outside the renderer.\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:26:- `legion-desktop` owns native windowing, egui/eframe rendering, adapter-local presentation state, session JSON read/write, input-to-intent translation, smoke harnesses, and display models derived from projections.\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:30:The high-risk implementation pattern is a deliberate anti-layering rule: renderer and UI code project and dispatch, while `legion-app` and lower authority crates perform stateful work and mutation mediation.\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:38:| Desktop renderer | `eframe`/`egui` 0.34.2 | Root workspace deps plus `crates/legion-desktop/Cargo.toml` |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:80:| `legion-desktop` | `crates/legion-desktop` | Renderer-backed desktop adapter | `legion-app`, `legion-protocol`, `legion-ui` |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:109:| Desktop launch/render | `legion-desktop` | Opens a native egui window, projects shell layout, explorer, tabs, active buffer, status, trust/proposal, search, language, terminal, assistant, plugin, and collaboration rows. |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:111:| CLI shell proof | `legion-app` binary | Still available as proof harness; not the primary GUI renderer. |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:121:| Dependency gates | `xtask`, `plans/dependency-policy.md`, `deny.toml` | Enforce crate boundary policy, renderer gate, and phase governance artifacts. |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:127:| `legion-desktop` | Native renderer, egui panels, adapter-local view/session state, action bridge, smoke harness | Editor buffers, workspace state, proposal lifecycle, terminal authority, provider/plugin/collab runtime authority |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:129:| `legion-app` | Composition, active document binding, command routing, save workflow, search, language and terminal workflow orchestration | Raw filesystem authority outside `legion-project`/`legion-platform`, renderer details |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:130:| `legion-project` | Workspace root/file authority, file preconditions, proposal-mediated mutations | Editor text transactions or renderer UI state |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:132:| `legion-protocol` | Wire contracts, projections, validation helpers, ports | Runtime state, storage side effects, renderer behavior |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:141:| UI/renderer authority creep | High | Desktop adapter now exists and can collect many actions | Preserve `legion-ui` projection-only invariant and route mutation through app/workspace/proposal services. |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:156:- `eframe`/`egui` are deliberate renderer dependencies and should remain isolated to `legion-desktop` by policy.\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:166:Local dependency risk is mostly architectural rather than version-based: keep renderer dependencies out of `legion-ui`, keep `legion-editor -> legion-project` forbidden, and keep network/secret/terminal dependencies behind authority crates and policy gates.\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:176:| `legion-desktop` | Depends only on `legion-app`, `legion-protocol`, and `legion-ui` internally; renderer deps are external. |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:240:| `Cargo.toml` | Workspace members, workspace deps, renderer deps, internal crate aliases |\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:277:cargo run -p legion-desktop -- --workspace . --smoke --duration-ms 1500 --evidence plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-smoke.md\r\n.\\.planning\\CODEBASE.md:325:- Keep `legion-desktop` renderer dependencies and state local to the adapter.\r\n.\\.superpowers\\sdd\\task-PKT-PLAN-M11-report.md:161:- `cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit`\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\getting-started.md:41:- projections and renderer adapters: [[projection-only-ui-and-desktop]]\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\projection-only-ui-and-desktop.md:13:    note: States the desktop adapter boundary and native-resource ownership.\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\projection-only-ui-and-desktop.md:21:    note: Records the accepted renderer direction and the non-authoritative UI rule.\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\projection-only-ui-and-desktop.md:25:`[[crates/legion-ui/src/lib.rs]]` re-exports projection structs, layout/view state, and `CommandDispatchIntent`. It does not expose editor engines, workspace actors, save authorities, or renderer dependencies [@ui-lib]. `[[crates/legion-desktop/src/lib.rs]]` explicitly says native windowing and renderer resources live in the desktop adapter while product state stays owned by `legion-app`, `legion-ui`, and `legion-protocol` [@desktop-lib].\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\projection-only-ui-and-desktop.md:29:`[[plans/adrs/ADR-0002-ui-editor-rendering.md]]` keeps the repository away from VS Code-style state splits. The accepted direction is a Rust-native renderer path, but the renderer is still an adapter. The ADR names the invariant directly: `legion-ui` consumes protocol projections and emits intents; it must not own editor text, workspace state, save decisions, provider state, telemetry storage, or persistence policy [@adr-0002].\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\projection-only-ui-and-desktop.md:31:## What the desktop adapter is allowed to do\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\projection-only-ui-and-desktop.md:35:- native windows and renderer resources\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\projection-only-ui-and-desktop.md:44:This boundary preserves the contracts in [[workspace-save-workflow]] and [[text-snapshots-and-degraded-mode]]. A renderer crash or UI bug must not imply a successful save, accepted proposal, AI dispatch, or workspace mutation. That is why save routing, proposal application, AI product modes, and workflow approval all terminate in app-owned code rather than in view code [@adr-0002].\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\projection-only-ui-and-desktop.md:46:The desktop crate is therefore a renderer-backed adapter, not a second application core.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:11:    provides: Workspace member and shared renderer dependency declarations for devil-desktop\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:14:    provides: Locked dependency graph after adding eframe and egui\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:20:    provides: Compile-safe public module boundary for desktop adapter\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:30:  - \"cargo test -p xtask renderer_dependency_gate_preserves_projection_boundary -- --exact\"\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:58:Add the `devil-desktop` adapter crate and renderer dependencies in the only policy-approved location, while keeping the crate compile-safe for later Phase 2 waves.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:64:- minimal diff: scaffold `devil-desktop` plus workspace/dependency wiring only; do not implement renderer workflows in this plan.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:65:- verify-before-report: run `xtask check-deps`, package check, and the exact renderer-gate regression test before reporting completion.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:70:- forbidden actions: editing `devil-ui`, moving app/editor/workspace logic, adding renderer dependencies to any non-adapter crate, or weakening `xtask`.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:71:- verification criteria: the new package exists, compiles by itself, and dependency gates still fail closed for non-adapter renderer dependencies.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:78:- BLOCKED if `plans/dependency-policy.md` no longer authorizes `devil-desktop` as the only renderer dependency host.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:80:- BLOCKED if `eframe`/`egui` cannot be added without placing renderer/windowing dependencies in `devil-ui` or core crates.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:88:- If cargo resolves additional renderer stack crates, confirm `xtask` allows them only through `devil-desktop`; do not add them to non-adapter manifests.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:102:- `devil-desktop` depends on `devil-app`, `devil-ui`, `devil-protocol`, `eframe`, and `egui`; no non-adapter crate gains renderer dependencies.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:109:Write `.planning/phases/02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode/02-01-RESULT.md` with scaffold summary, dependency list, verification results, and any cargo-deny warnings observed.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:135:2. Add shared workspace dependencies for `eframe` and `egui` using exact crate names authorized by Phase 1; use current compatible versions resolved by Cargo and no default-feature suppression unless required by compilation.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:136:   > verification: `rg -q \"eframe\" Cargo.toml` and `rg -q \"egui\" Cargo.toml`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:137:3. Create `crates/devil-desktop/Cargo.toml` with package metadata inherited from the workspace and dependencies on `anyhow`, `devil-app`, `devil-protocol`, `devil-ui`, `eframe`, `egui`, and `thiserror`.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:147:- Keep `devil-desktop` dependency declarations in the desktop crate manifest; do not add renderer dependencies to `devil-ui`.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-PLAN.md:152:- If `eframe` pulls `accesski