ptance Evidence.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\13-legion-workflow-orchestration\\13-01-PLAN.md:123:   > verification: `rg -q \"Approval-gated merge\" plans/adrs/ADR-0019-legion-workflow-orchestration.md`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\13-legion-workflow-orchestration\\13-01-PLAN.md:128:- If ADR numbering already has ADR-0019, use the next available ADR number and update this plan result with the exact path.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\13-legion-workflow-orchestration\\13-01-PLAN.md:134:rg -q \"Approval-gated merge\" plans/adrs/ADR-0019-legion-workflow-orchestration.md\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\13-legion-workflow-orchestration\\13-01-PLAN.md:189:- `plans/adrs/ADR-0019-legion-workflow-orchestration.md`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\13-legion-workflow-orchestration\\13-01-PLAN.md:224:- [ ] ADR-0019 exists and defines approval-gated merge.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-01-PLAN.md:8:requirements: [\"R-001\"]\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-01-PLAN.md:81:5. Preserve any historical caveats about renderer-backed latency, IME, clipboard, focus, and accessibility as GUI follow-up evidence, not as current substrate blockers.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-01-PLAN.md:130:2. Write the baseline document with sections for current runnable shell, projection boundary, save workflow, observability/storage constraints, renderer gap, dependency policy gap, and Phase 2 entry criteria.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-01-PLAN.md:148:- Do not infer a GUI crate name as implemented; use `planned desktop adapter` unless a crate exists.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-01-PLAN.md:162:- The document would need to assert a renderer implementation that does not exist.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-01-RESULT.md:20:- Treated GUI productization as a post-substrate track with renderer evidence still outstanding.\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\runtime-architecture.md:21:`[[crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs]]` is the authority layer for the product. It composes workspace, editor, protocol, security, storage, UI projection, indexing, AI, plugin, collaboration, remote, terminal, memory, tracker, and desktop-facing surfaces without pushing those authorities into the renderer layer [@app-root]. The workspace manifest shows this as a broad multi-crate Rust workspace rather than a monolith or a plugin host wrapped around one editor core [@workspace-manifest].\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\text-snapshots-and-degraded-mode.md:20:    path: plans/adrs/ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md\r\n.\\.almanac\\pages\\text-snapshots-and-degraded-mode.md:33:The accepted Phase 1 rule in `[[plans/adrs/ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md]]` is that UI gets full source only in explicitly bounded small-buffer mode. Large-file degraded mode must use viewport slices only, surface visible limitations, and avoid unbounded whole-file behavior [@viewport-adr].\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-SUMMARY.md:5:`devil-desktop` is now a workspace package with policy-approved `eframe`/`egui` renderer dependencies isolated to the adapter crate. The package compiles, `Cargo.lock` is refreshed, and `xtask` confirms renderer dependencies remain denied outside `devil-desktop`.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-SUMMARY.md:11:- `cargo test -p xtask renderer_dependency_gate_preserves_projection_boundary -- --exact`: passed\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-RESULT.md:9:- `Cargo.toml`: added `crates/devil-desktop` as a workspace member, added workspace `eframe`/`egui`, and exposed `devil-app`/`devil-desktop` workspace dependencies.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-RESULT.md:10:- `Cargo.lock`: refreshed by `cargo check -p devil-desktop --all-targets` after resolving `eframe = 0.34.2` and `egui = 0.34.2`.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-RESULT.md:11:- `plans/dependency-policy.md`: changed the renderer boundary wording from planned crate to active Phase 2 crate without widening non-adapter permissions.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-RESULT.md:12:- `crates/devil-desktop/Cargo.toml`: created the desktop adapter manifest with dependencies on `anyhow`, `devil-app`, `devil-protocol`, `devil-ui`, `eframe`, `egui`, and `thiserror`.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-RESULT.md:24:| `cargo test -p xtask renderer_dependency_gate_preserves_projection_boundary -- --exact` | passed; 1 passed |\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-01-RESULT.md:28:Cargo resolved the renderer stack through `devil-desktop` only. The dependency policy and `xtask` renderer gate still reject renderer/windowing crates in `devil-ui` and other core crates.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-02-PLAN.md:11:    provides: egui projection renderer and display view model\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-02-PLAN.md:39:Render the current `ShellProjectionSnapshot` in `devil-desktop` using egui panels without moving projection state or business authority into UI.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-02-PLAN.md:45:- minimal diff: edit only the renderer view module and its tests.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-02-PLAN.md:48:- task: turn protocol/UI projection DTOs into egui-visible panels and a testable view model.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-02-PLAN.md:50:- allowed tools/actions: create pure view-model helpers, egui rendering functions, and renderer tests.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-02-PLAN.md:60:- BLOCKED if egui rendering requires modifyin