-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-04-PLAN.md:55:- forbidden actions: direct filesystem saves from desktop, direct editor mutation outside `dispatch_ui_intent`, app code edits, or renderer dependencies outside `devil-desktop`.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-04-PLAN.md:65:- BLOCKED if eframe requires renderer callbacks that would own editor text or save state.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode\\02-04-PLAN.md:93:Write `.planning/phases/02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode/02-04-RESULT.md` with run command, tested workflows, and rejection evidence.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\03-daily-editing-mvp\\03-04-PLAN.md:195:- `plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-foundation.md`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\04-language-and-terminal-ide-loop\\04-04-PLAN.md:61:- allowed tools/actions: focused Rust/egui edits, desktop unit/integration tests, cargo check/test, and source-boundary greps.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\06-packaging-platform-integration-and-accessibility\\06-04-PLAN.md:57:Make crash-safe session restore and metadata-only diagnostics export available through the desktop adapter.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\06-packaging-platform-integration-and-accessibility\\06-06-PLAN.md:59:- read-before-write: read `06-CONTEXT.md`, `06-01-RESULT.md` through `06-05-RESULT.md`, all Phase 6 GUI evidence stubs/runbooks, `plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-smoke.md`, `phase-3-session-and-large-file.md`, `phase-5-control-trust-safety.md`, and `AGENTS.md` before writing evidence.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\06-packaging-platform-integration-and-accessibility\\06-06-PLAN.md:209:- `plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-smoke.md`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\08-advanced-platform-gui-ga\\08-01-PLAN.md:146:- Do not loosen renderer dependency gates or existing Phase 8 runtime substrate gates.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\06-packaging-platform-integration-and-accessibility\\06-CRITIQUE.md:55:- Real OS accessibility inspection may still be limited by egui/eframe and the local environment. The plan requires a deterministic accessibility tree model and honest OS-observed labels, not unsupported claims.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\08-advanced-platform-gui-ga\\08-CONTEXT.md:63:- `devil-desktop` may own renderer resources, adapter-local presentation state, smoke harnesses, metadata-only diagnostics, and native platform observations. It must not own app/editor/workspace/proposal/security/storage/runtime authority.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\06-packaging-platform-integration-and-accessibility\\06-CONTEXT.md:28:Turn the renderer-backed GUI into an installable Windows desktop application with credible platform behavior.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\06-packaging-platform-integration-and-accessibility\\06-CONTEXT.md:51:- `devil-ui` remains projection-only and must not gain renderer, app, editor, project, storage, terminal, provider, plugin, collaboration, or remote authority.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\06-packaging-platform-integration-and-accessibility\\06-CONTEXT.md:52:- `devil-desktop` may own packaging scripts, native window setup, renderer resources, adapter-local platform observations, diagnostics export formatting, and metadata-only session persistence. It must not own editor text, workspace mutation, proposal lifecycle authority, terminal runtime authority, provider routing, storage authority, or security policy.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\08-advanced-platform-gui-ga\\08-07-RESULT.md:17:- Phase 8 GUI GA remains renderer/projection-only for `devil-ui` and `devil-desktop`.\r\n.\\README.md:36:- `legion-desktop` is the eframe/egui renderer edge and must not own product state.\r\n.\\README.md:49:cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit\r\n.\\README.md:98:This is not the full renderer-backed desktop product.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:1:# Phase 1 Review: Baseline Reconciliation and Renderer Decision\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:14:- `plans/evidence/gui-productization/renderer-decision-matrix.md`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:19:- `plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-1-renderer-readiness.md`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:21:- Phase 1 planning artifacts under `.planning/phases/01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision/`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:28:- **Line/Section**: pre-review `run_check_deps` renderer gate call and `validate_renderer_dependency_gate`\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:30:- **Issue**: The renderer dependency gate enforced the deny list only for `devil-ui`, while the Phase 1 spec and policy require renderer crates to stay out of `devil-ui` and core/non-adapter workspace crates.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:31:- **Details**: Plan 01-04 explicitly required enforcement so renderer dependencies cannot enter `devil-ui` or core crates. The policy also says renderer crates are adapter-only and must not appear in core substrate crates, but the runtime check passed only `devil-ui` dependency names into the gate. A package like `devil-app` could have declared `eframe` without `cargo run -p xtask -- check-deps` catching it.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:32:- **Suggested Fix**: Build a dependency-name map for all workspace packages, skip only the planned `devil-desktop` adapter, and report renderer/windowing dependencies from any other package.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:53:The renderer decision matrix remains consistent with current primary sources checked during review:\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:55:- egui's official README states that `eframe` supports native Windows and that official integrations include `egui-winit` plus `egui-wgpu` or `egui_glow`: https://github.com/emilk/egui\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:56:- eframe docs list default `accesskit`, `winit`, and `wgpu` feature paths: https://docs.rs/crate/eframe/latest/features\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:57:- AccessKit docs list egui and Slint integrations and recommend the AccessKit winit adapter for winit-based Rust toolkits: https://accesskit.dev/\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:63:| `cargo test -p xtask renderer_dependency_gate_preserves_projection_boundary -- --exact` | passed, 1 passed |\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:77:- Phase 2 still needs real renderer evidence for input-to-paint, IME, clipboard, focus, high-DPI, file dialogs, and accessibility before GUI acceptance can be claimed.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-REVIEW.md:81:No separate behavior-preserving code-polish pass was needed beyond the review fix. Cleanup was limited to the renderer gate scope, evidence wording, and trailing blank lines in Phase 1 planning files. The full verification set passed afterward.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-CONTEXT.md:1:# Phase 1 Context: Baseline Reconciliation and Renderer Decision\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-CONTEXT.md:7:- Phase source: `.planning/ROADMAP.md`, phase 1, \"Baseline Reconciliation and Renderer Decision\".\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-CONTEXT.md:19:- `plans/adrs/ADR-0002-ui-editor-rendering.md` is accepted with reservations and identifies the native Rus