an authority layer.\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision\\01-03-RESULT.md:21:- Restricted desktop adapter ownership to window, renderer, native input, accessibility, diagnostics, and app-command routing.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-02-large-files-workspace-scale.md:1249:The exact egui code depends on the existing rendering pattern. The engineer must follow the existing code style in `view.rs`.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-02-large-files-workspace-scale.md:1295:cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:5:**Goal:** Complete WS-MANUAL-01 from `plans/legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md` by turning Manual mode into a measurable, renderer-backed, input-safe native IDE path with latency budgets, keyboard/IME/clipboard/focus coverage, font and wrapping policy, large-file capability messaging, deterministic renderer evidence, and zero-egress smoke.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:7:**Architecture:** Keep the existing authority split: `legion-ui` remains projection-only and emits typed `CommandDispatchIntent`; `legion-app` owns editor/workspace commands and Manual-mode policy; `legion-editor` and `legion-text` own buffer, viewport, cursor, selection, degraded-mode, and line-slice behavior; `legion-desktop` owns egui/eframe rendering, native adapter observations, and renderer evidence. `xtask` must not take a direct dependency on `legion-desktop`; it should launch a desktop-owned manual perf command as a subprocess and fold the metadata-only result into the existing perf report shape.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:9:**Tech Stack:** Rust 2024 workspace, `legion-app`, `legion-desktop`, `legion-editor`, `legion-text`, `legion-ui`, `legion-protocol`, `xtask`, eframe/egui 0.34.2, Markdown evidence under `plans/evidence/production/WS-MANUAL-01/`, targeted Rust integration tests, `cargo run -p xtask -- perf-harness`, `cargo run -p xtask -- verify-perf-harness`, `cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit`, and the repo-standard Rust gates.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:16:- `crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs` already renders Manual mode through `render_editor_canvas`, `render_code_lines`, `DesktopProjectionViewModel`, `DesktopCodeLineViewModel`, and cached egui galleys.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:19:- `crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs` already writes metadata-only renderer/platform smoke evidence and records first input-to-paint timing.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:21:- `xtask/Cargo.toml` currently has no internal crate dependencies. Preserve that by spawning `cargo run -p legion-desktop` for renderer-backed Manual measurements instead of importing desktop code into `xtask`.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:22:- `xtask/no-egui-textedit.toml` and `xtask/src/no_egui_textedit.rs` already guard the custom editor render path against `egui::TextEdit`.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:26:- `plans/product-readiness-ledger.md` currently keeps `PR-UI-001` at substrate validated. WS-MANUAL-01 evidence may support movement toward product-workflow validation only after real renderer-backed input, focus, accessibility, and platform evidence is recorded.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:36:- `crates/legion-desktop/tests/manual_renderer_evidence.rs`\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-manual-01-editor-feel-rendering-input.md:62:- Do not replace the custom code-canvas path with `egui::TextEdit`.\r\n.\\docs\\superpowers\\plans\\2026-06-19-ws-man