inal_workflow, save_all_conflict, beta_acceptance_e2e) plus the new tests/common/mod.rs is CLEAN (no warnings). test: the boundary/temp-dir changes I made all pass -- platform_smoke 6/6, intent_bridge 17/17, and the converted boundary tests desktop_control_trust_bridge_preserves_projection_only_boundary, desktop_phase4_dispatch_stays_projection_only, and save_all_conflict_desktop_save_paths_dispatch_ui_intent are all green. The remaining test failures are PRE-EXISTING/ENVIRONMENTAL and not caused by my changes: DesktopRuntime::open returns 'path read denied by policy' for workspaces under this machine's system temp dir, which fails every runtime-opening test (control_trust_bridge 4, language_terminal_workflow 2, save_all_conflict 4) and blocks run_beta_workflow (beta_acceptance_e2e panics at line 213 before my added section-12 assertion is reached). NOTE on environment: an initial sandboxed build had corrupted the dependency rlib artifacts; recovering required `cargo clean -p legion-desktop -p legion-protocol -p legion-ui -p legion-app` and rebuilding with reduced parallelism (-j 2) to avoid a Windows paging-file/OOM error (os error 1455).\"}], \"verification\": [{\"work_key\": \"legion-protocol\", \"build\": \"PASS\", \"clippy\": \"PASS\", \"test\": \"PASS\", \"details\": \"clean. cargo build -p legion-protocol: Finished. cargo clippy -p legion-protocol --all-targets -- -D warnings: Finished, no warnings. cargo test -p legion-protocol: 111 passed (lib 20 incl. 3 new + integration 91), 0 failed. Note: pre-existing test compile drift in crates/legion-protocol/tests/dto_contracts.rs (missing ViewportProjection.cursors and ProposalAuditRecord.checkpoint_rollback_projection/risk_rule_ids fields, plus two golden JSON literals missing cursors) was fixed in-scope to get a green test build; the crate did not compile at all before these fixes due to the dangling module declarations (E0583).\"}, {\"work_key\": \"legion-collaboration\", \"build\": \"PASS\", \"clippy\": \"PASS\