 lib unit test fails: tests::open_and_resolve_path_stays_inside_root panics with 'SecurityDenied { ... reason: \\\"path read denied by policy\\\" }' when resolving cwd/Cargo.toml via root_workspace(), which uses DenyByDefaultBroker::default() from legion-security. legion-security has concurrent uncommitted changes from a parallel agent (new src/policy.rs and src/risk.rs) that altered the default policy; this is outside legion-project scope and untouched by my edits (I changed none of resolve_file, root_workspace, or the security policy). cargo build -p legion-project and cargo clippy -p legion-project --all-targets -- -D warnings both pass clean.\"}, {\"work_key\": \"legion-tracker\", \"build\": \"PASS\", \"clippy\": \"PASS\", \"test\": \"PASS\", \"details\": \"clean; cargo build, clippy --all-targets -D warnings, and test all pass; 8 unit tests pass including new regression test\"}, {\"work_key\": \"legion-agent\", \"build\": \"PASS\", \"clippy\": \"PASS\", \"test\": \"PASS\", \"details\": \"clean - cargo build, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, and cargo test all pass (23 tests, 0 failures).\"}, {\"work_key\": \"legion-app__src\", \"build\": \"PASS\", \"clippy\": \"PASS\", \"test\": \"PASS\", \"details\": \"cargo build -p legion-app: clean. cargo build -p legion-app --no-default-features --all-targets: clean (confirms Finding 2). cargo clippy -p legion-app --all-targets -- -D warnings: clean. cargo test -p legion-app --lib: 35 passed (incl. 4 new terminal OSC tests). cargo test -p legion-app --no-default-features --lib offline: 3 passed. NOTE: a PRE-EXISTING build break unrelated to the findings blocked compilation -- PluginContributionProjection initializer at lib.rs load_plugin_manifest was missing the `permission_review_rows` field (added by legion-protocol). I fixed it by populating permission_review_rows from manifest.requested_capabilities in the existing 'permission review N: capability=...' format, since the build had to be green to verify the findings.\"}, {\"work_key\": \"legion-app__tests\", \"build\": \"PASS\", \"clippy\": \"PASS\", \"test\": \"SKIPPED\", \"details\": \"cargo build -p legion-app --tests: PASS. cargo clippy -p legion-app --all-targets -- -D warnings: clean. cargo test: NOT GREEN on this Windows host due to two PRE-EXISTING, environmental failures unrelated to my changes (both reproduced on the stashed/original tree): (1) legion-security path_policy denies reads under the system temp dir -> every test that open_file()s a temp path panics with Workspace(SecurityDenied{reason:'path read denied by policy'}); this hits tests I never modified, e.g. daily_editing_search_active_file_returns_bounded_rows, confirmed failing on the unmodified baseline. (2) plugin_grammar parse assertion expects parser_version 'legion-index-tree-sitter-v1' but gets 'legion-index-lexical-v1' because native tree-sitter grammars are not built in this environment (assertion unchanged by my rename). Root causes live in crates/legion-security/src and the tree-sitter build config (outside the tests/ scope restriction). Tests that do not touch the temp-dir security policy or native tree-sitter compile and pass.\"}, {\"work_key\": \"legion-desktop__src\", \"build\": \"PASS\", \"clippy\": \"FAIL\", \"test\": \"FAIL\", \"details\": \"cargo build -p legion-desktop: PASS. cargo clippy -p legion-desktop --lib -- -D warnings: PASS (clean - all my source changes are warning-free). cargo clippy -p legion-desktop --all-targets and cargo test -p legion-desktop: FAIL, but exclusively due to PRE-EXISTING breakage from parallel agents concurrently modifying legion-protocol/legion-ui/legion-security in the same working tree (evidenced by untracked legion-security/src/policy.rs & risk.rs and dozens of modified crates). Specifically, in tests/ (out of my scope): projection_rendering.rs references removed legion_ui::ActiveBufferProjectionState / ActiveBufferProjection.state and ViewportProjection now requires line_wrapping_policy/wrap_column/cursors; plugin_management.rs missing PluginContributionProjection.permission_review_rows; headless_input.rs calls a nonexistent DesktopEframeApp::handle_action; assistant_rail.rs imports the orphaned (uncompiled) module. I DID fix the two in-scope (src/workflow.rs inline test module) protocol-drift compile errors (added permission_review_rows and cursors). Test targets that compile and are not blocked by the parallel legion-security path-read policy PASS and validate my changes: packaging (4/4 pass - package.rs target-triple), platform_smoke (6/6 pass - platform.rs/smoke.rs), session_restore store-level tests pass (session_store_save_publishes_validated_temp_and_cleans_intermediates validates Finding 2; session_restore_store_rejects_raw_source_markers confirms the Finding 3 test conflict), operational_health_empty_projection passes. The remaining test failures (operational_health/session_restore runtime tests, beta_workflow) fail at runtime workspace-open with 'path read denied by policy' from the parallel security work, or expect projection shapes changed by parallel work - all reproduced identically with original sources (verified for beta.rs).\"}, {\"work_key\": \"legion-desktop__tests\", \"build\": \"PASS\", \"clippy\": \"FAIL\", \"test\": \"FAIL\", \"details\": \"build: `cargo build -p legion-desktop` PASSES (lib clean). `cargo build -p legion-desktop --tests` fails ONLY on the pre-existing projection_rendering.rs API drift (legion_ui::ActiveBufferProjectionState / ActiveBufferProjection.state removed; ViewportProjection now requires line_wrapping_policy & wrap_column) -- unrelated to my changes. clippy: `cargo clippy -p legion-desktop --all-targets -- -D warnings` cannot complete because of that same pre-existing projection_rendering.rs compile error; however clippy with -D warnings on all 6 targets I touched (platform_smoke, control_trust_bridge, intent_bridge, language_terminal_workflow, save_all_conflict, beta_acceptance_e2e) plus the new tests/common/mod.rs is CLEAN (no warnings). test: the boundary/temp-dir changes I made all pass -- platform_smoke 6/6, intent_bridge 17/17, and the converted boundary tests desktop_control_trust_bridge_preserves_projection_only_boundary, desktop_phase4_dispatch_stays_projection_only, and save_all_conflict_desktop_save_paths_dispatch_ui_intent are all green. The remaining test failures are PRE-EXISTING/ENVIRONMENTAL and not caused by my changes: DesktopRuntime::open returns 'path read denied by policy' for workspaces under this machine's system temp dir, which fails every runtime-opening test (control_trust_bridge 4, language_terminal_workflow 2, save_all_conflict 4) and blocks run_beta_workflow (beta_acceptance_e2e panics at line 213 before my added section-12 assertion is reached). NOTE on environment: an initial sandboxed build had corrupted the dependency rlib artifacts; recovering required `cargo clean -p legion-desktop -p legion-protocol -p legion-ui -p legion-app` and rebuilding with reduced parallelism (-j 2) to avoid a Windows paging-file/OOM error (os error 1455).\"}], \"results\": [{\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Reworked TimestampMillis::now() to use u64::try_from(d.as_millis()).unwrap_or(u64::MAX) (no silent u128->u64 wrap) and added fallible try_now() -> Result<Self, SystemTimeError> that surfaces the duration_since error; now() delegates to try_now and saturates to 0 only on pre-epoch clocks. Added unit test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Imported std::time::SystemTimeError.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced raw substring protected-path gate in evaluate_delegated_task_runtime_readiness with delegated_target_matches_protected_pattern, which normalizes both / and \\\\ separators into lowercased components and matches the protected pattern as a contiguous component-window run (boundary-aware). Patterns with no usable path components fall back to a case-insensitive substring check so opaque labels still fail closed. Added unit tests covering boundary match and cross-boundary rejection (e.g. .gitignore vs .git).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Component-aware matching done in-memory (no filesystem canonicalize) since target_path_labels are display-safe labels, not real paths.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"capability.rs module never existed (not in working tree or git history). AssistedAiCapabilityMatrix / has_explicit_declaration are defined nowhere in the package and referenced by no other crate. Removed the dangling `pub mod capability;` and `pub use capability::AssistedAiCapabilityMatrix;` that broke compilation.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Planned-but-unimplemented module; nothing to restore. Build was broken (E0583) before this removal.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"manifest.rs module never existed. ContextManifestAssembly/ContextManifestSources/into_record defined nowhere in the package and unused elsewhere. Removed the dangling `pub mod manifest;` and its re-export that broke compilation.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Planned-but-unimplemented module; nothing to restore.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"plan.rs module never existed. EditablePlanArtifact and related types/EditablePlanArtifact::validate defined nowhere in the package and unused elsewhere. Removed the dangling `pub mod plan;` and its re-export.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Planned-but-unimplemented module; nothing to restore.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"risk.rs module never existed. RiskAssessment/is_allow/RiskRuleId defined nowhere in the package and unused elsewhere. Removed the dangling `pub mod risk;`. The vacuous-truth is_allow concern cannot apply to nonexistent code.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Planned-but-unimplemented module; nothing to restore. Note: the unrelated, real delegated-task gate in lib.rs already fails closed.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"scope.rs module never existed. DelegatedTaskScope/target_is_within_scope/forbidden_paths defined nowhere in the package and unused elsewhere. Removed the dangling `pub mod scope;` and its re-export.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Planned-but-unimplemented module; nothing to restore.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"tools.rs module never existed. LegionToolCallFeedback/LegionToolKind defined nowhere in the package and unused elsewhere. Removed the dangling `pub mod tools;` and its re-exports.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Planned-but-unimplemented module; nothing to restore.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"tools.rs module / validate_tool_schema_definition never existed in the working tree or git history; function body cannot be inspected or fixed. Covered by removal of the dangling tools module declaration.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Planned-but-unimplemented module; nothing to restore.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"The read/edit-as-proposal tool JSON schemas live in the nonexistent tools.rs; no start_line/end_line schema text exists anywhere in the package. Covered by removal of the dangling tools module declaration.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Planned-but-unimplemented module; nothing to restore.\", \"package\": \"legion-protocol\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Cited file crates/legion-ui/src/projection.rs and function legion_workflow_fleet_card_projections do not exist in this package; the described proposal-card verification projection behavior lives in the UI/desktop crates (render_proposal_cards in legion-desktop), not legion-collaboration. No collaboration-side symbol matches.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Real location (if implemented later) would be legion-desktop/src/view.rs proposal-card rendering; out of scope for this package.\", \"package\": \"legion-collaboration\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"In handle_transport_envelope, added authorization checks: Operation payloads require envelope.sender_participant_id == operation.author_participant_id and Presence payloads require envelope.sender_participant_id == projection.participant_id, returning InvalidOperation on mismatch before dispatch. Added negative tests for operation- and presence-sender spoofing plus a positive matching-sender test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-collaboration\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"In the participant roster loop, the insert into participant_map is now checked with .is_some() and returns InvalidParticipant on a duplicate id, preventing silent overwrite of principal/permissions. Added duplicate_participant_id_is_rejected test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"With duplicates rejected, the deduplicated map equals submitted count so the existing max_participants bound remains correct.\", \"package\": \"legion-collaboration\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"submit_operation now iterates operation.preconditions.base_vector.entries before acceptance and, for any entry where participant_sequences.get(entry.participant_id) < entry.sequence, emits a CollaborationCausalGap and a GapDetected acknowledgement instead of replaying. Added base_vector_dependency_on_unseen_sequence_emits_gap test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-collaboration\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"Implemented conservative fail-closed: a destructive (Delete/Replace) operation that is concurrent with an already-accepted operation it did not observe (via has_concurrent_accepted_operation, the negation of depends_on) is now rejected with a ResyncRequired acknowledgement instead of applying a raw, possibly-wrong-but-in-bounds byte range. Inserts remain accepted (non-destructive, convergent under the deterministic total order; out-of-bounds/non-boundary cases already fail-closed via replace_range). Updated the existing delete_replace test to declare its real causal dependency and added concurrent_destructive_operation_is_fail_closed.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Remaining work: a real OT/CRDT inclusion-transformation step that adjusts byte ranges of concurrent operations during replay (so concurrent destructive edits can be safely applied rather than rejected), and positional transform of concurrent inserts so they target correct offsets rather than relying on deterministic total-order convergence. The exploit (silent document corruption from concurrent destructive ops) is closed.\", \"package\": \"legion-collaboration\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced DefaultHasher in metadata_hash with a self-contained, deterministic SHA-256 (pure-Rust FIPS 180-4 impl, since no sha2/blake3 dep is available and Cargo.toml is out of scope) emitting the full 64-char hex digest. metadata_fingerprint now sets algorithm to 'sha256:<domain>' and domain-separates the hashed input so identical bytes under different domains never collide. Added golden/stability tests (empty/abc/hello vectors) and a fingerprint domain-separation test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Used a vendored pure-Rust SHA-256 because adding sha2/blake3 would require editing Cargo.toml (forbidden). Output verified against published SHA-256 test vectors.\", \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Converted the MetadataOnly/None redaction branch to allowlist-based via new redact_metadata_value/is_safe_metadata_key helpers (replacing is_metadata_value). Non-string scalars pass through; free-form strings are collapsed to 'hash=<digest>;len=<n>' unless the key is an allowlisted classifier/id/hash key AND the value contains no forbidden marker (contains_forbidden_assisted_ai_marker). Arrays/objects become '<metadata-only>'. Added two tests covering free-form hashing and forbidden-marker rejection on an allowlisted key.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"assert_core_ids remains in place; it is already fail-closed (panics on nil causality / zero correlation / zero sequence, preventing emission of invalid events). Did NOT convert the ~16 public envelope helpers to Result.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Converting the helpers to Result would ripple to legion-app (imports proposal_applied_event, proposal_approved_event, save_denied_event, proposal_audit_recorded_event, etc.; call site e.g. crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs:10480) which is out of scope per the edit-only-legion-observability restriction. Per the rules I preferred leaving the existing fail-closed behavior over a cross-crate-breaking signature change.\", \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"Added a fail-closed invariant guard at the top of proposal_audit_record: assert_eq!(transition.proposal_id, proposal.proposal_id), so a mismatched proposal/transition pairing can no longer silently produce a corrupted audit record. Added accept-matching and should_panic mismatch tests.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"The recipe's Result<ProposalAuditRecord, ObservabilityError> signature change would ripple to legion-app (proposal_audit_record call at crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs:10337), which is out of scope. Used an assert (consistent with the module's existing assert_core_ids invariant style) for fail-closed rejection without changing the public signature.\", \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"event_metadata_record now sets schema_version: envelope.schema_version instead of the literal 1, so a bumped envelope schema propagates. Added a test bumping envelope.schema_version to 7 and asserting propagation.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/telemetry.rs does not exist (package has only lib.rs) and suggestion_metadata_summary appears nowhere in this package's source. Behavior not present to fix.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"src/minidump.rs does not exist and no crash_reports_enabled/symbol_upload/symbolicated consent-gating code exists anywhere in legion-observability. Nothing to fix in this package.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"No minidump.rs and no crash-summary envelope code (crash_id/metadata_summary/symbol_upload_target) present in this package.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"No minidump.rs and no symbolicated/symbol_upload_state assignment present in this package.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"src/training.rs does not exist and consented_training_candidate_from_records appears nowhere in this package's source.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"No training.rs and no AssistedAiConsentState::NotRequired training-gate logic in this package.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"No training.rs and no ProposalLifecycleState::Approved->Accepted training-label mapping in this package.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"The legion-debug crate does not exist in the workspace (no crates/legion-debug directory, not referenced in any Cargo.toml). debug_adapter_audit_evidence/test_run_summary_evidence are absent. Out of scope for legion-observability and the target crate does not exist.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Cited code would live in a non-existent legion-debug crate, not legion-observability.\", \"package\": \"legion-observability\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Rewrote NativeProcessService::execute to spawn with piped stdin/stdout/stderr instead of blocking command.output(). stdout/stderr are drained on dedicated reader threads (avoids pipe-buffer deadlock); when request.timeout is set, the call polls child.try_wait() against started.elapsed() and on overrun calls terminate_timed_out_process (SIGKILL to the child's process group on Unix via a new setpgid pre_exec, then child.kill()/wait()) and returns PlatformError::Timeout. Added test process_execution_enforces_timeout_while_child_runs asserting a 10s child is aborted within 5s with a Timeout error.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Unix-cfg portions (setpgid pre_exec, group SIGKILL) not compiled on this Windows host; cross-platform timeout path and test verified on Windows.\", \"package\": \"legion-platform\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"PtyRequest (crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs:698-706) has only command/args/cwd fields - there is no request.env to forward, so child_environment_vars(&[]) is not actually dropping per-request env. Forwarding env would require adding a public env field to PtyRequest, which ripples to its struct-literal construction in crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs:555 (out of scope; cannot add a required field without editing that crate).\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"To truly fix, add `env: Vec<(String,String)>` to PtyRequest and forward it, plus update the legion-terminal construction site - a cross-crate change.\", \"package\": \"legion-platform\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"In kill_pty (Unix branch) added PtyKillMode::Terminate to the negative-PID (process-group) target set so close_pty's SIGTERM reaches the whole group (child is session leader via setsid), not just the leader. After the 500ms wait, if the child has not exited, escalate with SIGKILL to the process group and wait/reap again before removing the session entry; the error message now reflects the SIGKILL escalation.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Unix-cfg code; not compiled on this Windows host. Follows the existing wait_unix_child_exit/nix patterns in the file.\", \"package\": \"legion-platform\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced list_directory's filter_map(|entry| entry.ok()) with an explicit loop that propagates per-entry errors via PlatformError::from_io_error(\\\"list directory\\\", path, err), so failed read_dir entries surface instead of being silently dropped. Added test list_directory_lists_entries_sorted.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-platform\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"handle_filesystem_operation and handle_process_descriptor now reject when the payload's embedded operation_id != envelope.operation_id (added `|| operation.operation_id != operation_id` and `|| descriptor.operation_id != operation_id`), returning RemoteRuntimeError::InvalidOperation. session_id was already checked; these are the only payload fields carrying an embedded operation_id, so no other consistency fields apply.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-remote\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"validate_mutation_gate now calls validate_capability(&preconditions.capability_decision, \\\"remote.fs.write\\\") (denies on error) and compares preconditions.principal_id against self.descriptor.authority.principal_id (denies on mismatch) before proceeding.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Correlation/causality binding to the envelope is implicitly covered: write_preconditions travel inside the RemoteFilesystemOperation payload which is itself the envelope unit, and Finding 7 now binds operation.operation_id == envelope.operation_id so preconditions cannot be replayed under a different envelope. The two concretely exploitable gaps named in the evidence (missing capability-name validation and missing principal match) are closed.\", \"package\": \"legion-remote\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"create_file now computes fingerprint: metadata_fingerprint(&content) from the actual built content instead of the constant string, matching seed_file/write_file.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-remote\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added derived_snapshot_id(path, content_version, operation_id) = SnapshotId(stable_hash_u128(path:cv:op) | 1). write_file, create_file, and rename_file now assign a fresh post-mutation snapshot id (instead of reusing preconditions.snapshot_id or leaving the renamed entry unchanged), returned via snapshot_for_path.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-remote\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"common_headers now returns Result<HeaderMap, RemoteRuntimeError>; invalid AUTHORIZATION or X-Legion-Client-Identity HeaderValue::from_str errors map to RemoteRuntimeError::InvalidOperation and propagate via send_with_body (self.common_headers()?) instead of being silently dropped.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-remote\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added encode_path_segment (RFC 3986 pchar allowlist) applied to task_id.0 in all four HTTP URL builders (events/cancel/proposal/evidence) so `/ ? #` and control bytes are percent-encoded and cannot alter the path/query. Also tightened validate_cloud_task_id to reject ids containing control chars or `/ \\\\ ? #`.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"pchar set (unreserved + sub-delims + ':' + '@') is passed through so legitimate colon-delimited ids like cloud-task:http:1 remain unchanged; no percent_encoding crate dependency was added (would require Cargo.toml edit, out of scope).\", \"package\": \"legion-remote\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"serve_one now reads via read_full_http_request: accumulates until the \\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n header terminator, parses Content-Length, then reads the full body, with a 5s read timeout set on the accepted stream. Replaces the single fixed 4096-byte read that could truncate segmented/large requests.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote/tests/cloud_lane_http_transport.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-remote\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"The three before-network rejection tests (disabled_policy, forbidden_upload, cost_cap) no longer spawn a listener; they use unreachable_base_url() (http://127.0.0.1:1) so no accept() thread is leaked and any accidental network attempt fails fast. Added a read timeout to serve_one's accepted stream for genuine-listener tests.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote/tests/cloud_lane_http_transport.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Genuine-listener tests self-terminate after serving one request, so a join/shutdown handle was not added; the leak source (listeners that were never contacted) is fully removed.\", \"package\": \"legion-remote\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Changed accepted_sequences from VecDeque<EventSequence> to VecDeque<(EventSequence, RemoteOperationId)> in try_accept_frame so that when the replay window slides (pop_front), the evicted operation id is also removed from seen_operations. This bounds seen_operations to replay_window_size, so replay_window().accepted_operation_count (which reports seen_operations.len()) and audit_summary are no longer unbounded. inflight_operations remains separate (removed on ack). Updated replay_window front() access for the new tuple type. Added test remote_transport_state_machine_bounds_seen_operations_to_replay_window.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote-transport/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Out-of-window operations are now caught by the contiguous forward-only frame_sequence check (ReplayRejected) rather than reported as Duplicate, which is the expected behavior for a bounded replay window.\", \"package\": \"legion-remote-transport\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added two validation guards in checkpoint() before assigning self.last_checkpoint: reject with ReplayRejected when checkpoint.event_sequence.0 > self.last_sequence.0 (ahead of accepted frames), and reject when it is below the lowest retained accepted_sequence (outside the replay window). Added test remote_transport_state_machine_rejects_out_of_window_checkpoint_sequence covering ahead, stale, and valid-in-window cases.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-remote-transport/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Used a let-chain to satisfy clippy::collapsible_if.\", \"package\": \"legion-remote-transport\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Lease expiry was set to TimestampMillis(policy.ttl_ms), treating a duration as an absolute epoch. Now computed in both capture_descriptor and capture_bundle as TimestampMillis(now_ms.saturating_add(policy.ttl_ms).min(grant.expires_at.0)) using TimestampMillis::now(), so it is an absolute timestamp clamped to the consent grant.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Existing purge_expired test still passes: grant.expires_at (60_000) clamps the lease, keeping its recorded value, while real captures now use wall-clock TTL.\", \"package\": \"legion-retention\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"pack_files now accumulates raw file byte total and returns RawSourceVaultError::Denied once it exceeds request.max_bytes, enforcing the consent-bound budget instead of only the vault config limit. Added test file_backed_vault_rejects_capture_exceeding_consent_byte_budget.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-retention\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"flush_index now writes to index.json.tmp, fsyncs the file, renames over index.json, and best-effort fsyncs the parent dir (ignored where unsupported, e.g. Windows). open() now quarantines a corrupt index to index.json.corrupt-<ts> and fails closed instead of erroring without preservation or silently starting empty.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-retention\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"capture_bundle now writes ciphertext to a temp .vault.tmp file, stages index mutations in memory, persists the index via flush_index, and only then renames temp->bundle_path. On flush failure it reverts the staged index entries (new revert_bundle_index helper) and removes the temp file; on rename failure it reverts, re-flushes, and removes the temp file, so no orphaned or dangling files remain.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-retention\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"delete_bundle now treats NotFound from fs::remove_file as recoverable (proceeds to drop index entries and record the tombstone) and only errors on other IO failures. purge_expired now continues on per-bundle delete failures (counting only successes) instead of aborting on the first failure. Updated the prior test to assert delete now succeeds and removes the descriptor when ciphertext is missing.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Renamed test file_backed_vault_delete_fails_when_ciphertext_is_missing -> file_backed_vault_delete_tolerates_missing_ciphertext to match the corrected fail-safe behavior.\", \"package\": \"legion-retention\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Targets crates/legion-sandbox/src/landlock.rs (LandlockProfile). That symbol does not exist anywhere in legion-security; it belongs to legion-sandbox, a different (non-workspace-member) package outside my scope.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Real location is legion-sandbox, which has no Cargo.toml and is not compiled; not editable from this package.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Targets crates/legion-sandbox/src/seatbelt.rs (SeatbeltProfile). Symbol absent from legion-security; belongs to legion-sandbox.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Different package, out of scope.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Targets crates/legion-sandbox/src/windows.rs (WindowsProfile). Symbol absent from legion-security; belongs to legion-sandbox.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Different package, out of scope.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Targets windows.rs `documented_fallback` in legion-sandbox. No such field/file in legion-security.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Different package, out of scope.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Reworked NormalizedPolicyPath::starts_with to require symmetric prefix equality (self.prefix != root.prefix => false). The default \\\"./\\\" roots (prefix None, no segments) no longer match absolute candidates, so can_access(\\\"/tmp/file\\\", Read) now returns false while workspace-relative access still works. Added regression test default_path_policy_does_not_allow_absolute_paths.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Chose symmetric-prefix check over the recipe's empty-root guard because the latter would deny all relative workspace access (breaking the intended default); symmetric check fixes the absolute-path bypass without that regression and matches the recipe's stated intent.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Rewrote the fs.* arm: fs.write with no target_path now denies (was allow); fs.read/fs.list now require a path and run PathPolicy::can_access (Read/List); unknown fs.* subcommands deny-by-default. Added tests fs_read_requires_path_and_honors_path_policy and fs_write_without_path_fails_closed.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Only fs.read/fs.write are used in the codebase; list handled defensively, all other fs.* denied.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"remote.fs.read/remote.fs.write now require a target path and enforce PathPolicy::can_access (Read/Write, including blocked-root checks); missing path fails closed. Threaded `path` into remote_capability_decision. Updated remote_policy_allows_filesystem_without_execution test and added a missing-path deny assertion.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"CapabilityRequestContext has no dedicated remote-path field, so the request target_path (already plumbed as `path`) is used as the canonical remote path.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"CommandTaxonomy::classify now parses git subcommands (push/fetch/pull/clone/remote=>Network; clean/checkout/reset/commit/etc=>Mutate; else Read) instead of keying only on the first token. terminal.launch now denies Network/Mutate/Unknown launch binaries (kept Terminal/LanguageServer/Read). cmd.* arm and requires_trusted_workspace_for_request now treat Unknown as deny/trusted-required for untrusted workspaces. Added tests git_subcommands_are_classified_by_verb and cmd_git_push_is_denied_for_untrusted_workspace.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Deviated from the recipe's literal 'deny Terminal at terminal.launch': launching a shell (Terminal class) is the terminal's legitimate purpose and an existing test asserts bash=>Allow, so Terminal stays allowed while the real bypass (git push as Read, unknown/mutate/network launch binaries) is closed.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"lsp.launch now requires context.lsp_server_binary, rejects binaries not in lsp_policy.allowed_binaries, denies network-refresh launches when deny_network_refresh is set, and the catch-all now denies unknown lsp.* subcommands instead of allowing them. Added test lsp_launch_requires_allowlisted_binary.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Used the actual context field lsp_server_binary (recipe said command_binary, which is the terminal field).\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"CapabilityBrokerPort::handle no longer echoes caller-supplied Grant/Deny envelopes as authoritative Granted/Denied responses; both now return Err(ProtocolError::validation(..)). Only Request envelopes go through the policy engine. Added test broker_rejects_grant_and_deny_envelopes.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Fail-closed: external Grant/Deny rejected rather than trusted.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Moved the decision counter to AtomicU64 with a manual Clone impl and a next_decision_id() helper. handle() no longer clones the broker; it increments the real instance's counter via &self, so generated CapabilityDecisionIds are monotonic across repeated calls. Added test handle_generates_monotonic_decision_ids (asserts ids 1,2,3).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Public decide/decide_with_request_context kept as &mut self to avoid unused_mut churn across ~30 existing tests; atomic works fine under &mut self.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"policy.rs was missing from disk/git (crate did not compile). Recreated it with ProposalAutoApprovalPolicy::allows_rule_ids implemented fail-closed: returns false when disabled or when rule_ids is empty, and requires every id to be non-empty and present in allowed_rule_ids. Also provided BatchRuntimeApplyPolicy and ProposalApplyGate (fail-closed defaults) required by the lib.rs re-export. Added unit tests including empty_rule_ids_are_never_auto_approved.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/policy.rs\", \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Module was referenced by lib.rs:24-25 but never existed; recreating it was required to make the package compile and directly implements the requested !rule_ids.is_empty() guard.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"risk.rs was missing from disk/git. Recreated it with is_dependency_or_lockfile covering Rust (Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock), npm/yarn/pnpm/deno/bun, Go, Python, Ruby, PHP, and JVM manifests + lockfiles, name-compared case-insensitively across / and \\\\\\\\ separators. Added unit test manifests_and_lockfiles_are_detected.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/risk.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Module referenced by lib.rs:26 but never existed; recreated to compile and to implement the requested manifest coverage. Self-contained (no current consumers in the crate).\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"In the recreated risk.rs, path_scope_risk treats an absent/blank workspace_root as RiskLevel::Deny (never low-risk), and returns Elevated for paths escaping the root or containing '..'. Added unit test missing_workspace_root_is_not_low_risk.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-security/src/risk.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Missing scope metadata is no longer treated as low-risk evidence, per the finding.\", \"package\": \"legion-security\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added a fail-closed equality check at the start of FileBackedTelemetrySpool::pending_batch that rejects with TelemetrySpoolError::InvalidMetadata when the passed endpoint != consent.endpoint (full struct equality, stricter than the recipe's field list). Since export_once delegates to pending_batch, both upload paths are now covered. Added test pending_batch_rejects_endpoint_not_matching_consent.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-telemetry/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"HostedTelemetryEndpointDescriptor derives PartialEq/Eq in legion-protocol, so direct != comparison is valid and includes endpoint_id, label, region, allowlisted, schema_version.\", \"package\": \"legion-telemetry\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added SUPPORTED_SPOOL_SCHEMA_VERSION const and a validate_persisted_spool helper invoked in FileBackedTelemetrySpool::open after JSON decode. It rejects unsupported schema_version, records.len() > config.max_records, and runs validate_hosted_telemetry_spool_record on every decoded record, returning a clear TelemetrySpoolError::InvalidMetadata for corrupt/oversized/invalid files. Added tests file_backed_spool_open_rejects_unsupported_schema_version and file_backed_spool_open_rejects_oversized_persisted_file.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-telemetry/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Validation runs only when an existing file is loaded; the freshly-initialized default state is constructed with the supported schema version.\", \"package\": \"legion-telemetry\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"LineIndex::visible_line_slices now validates end_line_exclusive <= self.line_count() and returns TextError::LineOutOfBounds BEFORE the Vec::with_capacity, so a huge end_line_exclusive can no longer force a massive allocation ahead of the per-line bounds check. Added test visible_line_slices_reject_out_of_bounds_range_before_allocating.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Fix is in the LineIndex method; TextSnapshot/TextBuffer visible_line_slices both forward to it.\", \"package\": \"legion-text\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"rebuild_from_simple_edit now returns None when the shifted edited chunk's byte_len exceeds DEFAULT_CHUNK_FORCE_MAX_BYTES, so try_replace_range falls back to refresh_cache_and_index(rebuild_chunk_index), restoring the bounded-chunk invariant instead of growing a chunk past 96 KiB on the simple-edit fast path. Added test simple_edit_growing_chunk_past_bound_falls_back_to_bounded_rebuild.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-text\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"TextSnapshot::text() no longer panics: it returns the bounded cache when present, otherwise lazily materializes the full text from the rope once via a new OnceLock<Arc<String>> field. Added test snapshot_text_does_not_panic_for_degraded_cache. TextBuffer::text() still panics (documented) because it is the mutable editing surface where a materialized fallback would risk staleness across edits and silently reintroduce unbounded retention.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Could not make TextBuffer::text() non-panicking without either changing the public -> &str signature (would ripple to dependent crates; the safe fallible try_full_text() already exists) or adding interior-mutability with invalidation on every mutation (staleness risk not worth it for a low finding). Snapshot path (the immutable read surface the recipe targets) is fully fixed.\", \"package\": \"legion-text\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added sanitize_terminal_text helper (escapes C0 controls except newline/tab, DEL 0x7f, and C1 controls 0x80-0x9f as visible \\\\xNN) and routed every untrusted Display-rendered projection string in Shell::render through it: layout title, tab titles, close-dirty prompt, small-buffer text, viewport visible_text, file path, command id/scope, proposal lifecycle label/title, artifact id/state, verification run id/class, manifest id/item id/selected, inspector exposure id, budget id, assist provider/route/preview ids, prediction labels, workflow artifact ids/labels, hover label/summary, operation id, terminal denial/payload, and debug config/breakpoint/frame/variable/watch/console labels. {:?}-formatted fields left as-is (escape_debug already neutralizes control chars).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Added unit test sanitize_terminal_text_escapes_control_and_ansi_sequences covering ESC/ANSI, C0, DEL, C1, and preservation of newline/tab and multibyte text.\", \"package\": \"legion-ui\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"parse_pos viewport branch now computes absolute offset slice.byte_range.start + (byte_offset - current_offset), validates it lies within the slice (<= byte_range.end), and rejects offsets outside every visible slice with ShellCommandError::InvalidPosition instead of falling through to (0,0).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Added tests parse_pos_viewport_returns_absolute_byte_offset (asserts Some(1024)/Some(1029)) and parse_pos_viewport_rejects_offset_outside_visible_slices.\", \"package\": \"legion-ui\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"parse_pos small-buffer branch now validates byte_offset <= text.len() and text.is_char_boundary(byte_offset), and the viewport branch guards relative char boundary; both return new ShellCommandError::InvalidPosition rather than coercing to (0,0,0). parse_pos and command_position changed to Result<TextCoordinate, ShellCommandError> and propagated with ? at all call sites (:assist-predict, :hover, :completion, :definition, :references, :rename, :d, :r, :code-action). Non-numeric command_position payloads now rejected instead of coercing to start.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Signature change is internal to legion-ui (parse_pos/command_position are private methods). Added tests parse_pos_rejects_out_of_bounds_offset, parse_pos_rejects_mid_codepoint_offset, parse_pos_accepts_in_bounds_char_boundary_offsets.\", \"package\": \"legion-ui\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added .filter(|value| *value != 0) to parse_proposal_id between parse and map(ProposalId), mirroring parse_buffer_id, so :proposal-approve 0 (and other proposal commands) no longer emit a sentinel-id intent and fall through to Noop.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Added test parse_proposal_id_rejects_zero_sentinel asserting 0/blank yield None, 42 yields Some, and :proposal-approve 0 yields Noop (no ApproveProposal intent).\", \"package\": \"legion-ui\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Threaded a per-message index discriminator from from_status_messages_with_verbosity (via .enumerate() before filtering) into from_status_message and folded it into toast_id, so two identical status messages now produce distinct toast ids; dismissing one no longer collapses duplicates.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\"], \"notes\": \"index enumerated over the original messages slice for stability across verbosity filtering. Added test toast_ids_distinguish_identical_status_messages. from_status_message is pub but only used within legion-ui (legion-desktop uses from_status_messages_with_verbosity), so the added parameter does not ripple.\", \"package\": \"legion-ui\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added has_executable_entrypoint() that detects non-empty main/browser fields in package.json. manifest_from_package_json now threads this flag into required_tier (floors tier to Tier2ExtensionHostSidecar) and requested_capabilities (inserts vscode.extension.activate). An extension with executable main and only declarative contributions/no activation events now resolves to Tier2/SupportedWithPolicy and a NodeSidecar host session instead of Tier0/Supported/NoneRequired. aggregate_status already returns SupportedWithPolicy for non-Tier0, so no change needed there. Added two tests (executable_entrypoint_requires_host_policy_without_activation_events, blank_executable_entrypoint_stays_declarative).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-vscode-compat/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-vscode-compat\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"required_string now maps to s.trim().to_string() before the non-empty filter so publisher/name/version identity fields are normalized before building VsCodeExtensionId, preventing malformed ids from whitespace. Added test identity_fields_are_trimmed_before_building_extension_id asserting padded inputs yield 'legion.trim-fixture'.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-vscode-compat/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-vscode-compat\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"In ProviderRouter::route_completion, after obtaining `completion` I added a guard that returns a refused_response with reason_code `provider.identity_mismatch` when `completion.provider != request.provider_id || completion.model != request.model_label`, so a provider cannot silently substitute a different provider/model. Added unit test `router_refuses_when_provider_returns_mismatched_identity` with a `MismatchedIdentityProvider` mock.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Kept the response echoing request provider/model on the success path (now guaranteed equal to completion's), matching existing API shape.\", \"package\": \"legion-ai\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Changed `allowed_route_decision()` to `allowed_route_decision(schema_version: u16)` and used the parameter for the nested AssistedAiRouteDecision.schema_version; call site now passes `request.schema_version`. Added unit test `route_decision_propagates_request_schema_version` asserting the nested decision's schema_version tracks the request (=2).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-ai\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"No telemetry code exists in package legion-ai. Grep for telemetry/TelemetrySpool/HostedTelemetry across crates/legion-ai/src returns nothing; package contains only lib.rs, redaction.rs, streaming.rs. The described Option<HostedTelemetrySpoolRecord> helper is not present here.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"If the helper exists at all it would live in a different package (e.g. legion-telemetry/legion-observability), which is out of scope for this agent.\", \"package\": \"legion-ai\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added #[ignore = \\\"performance suite: 100MB report-only measurement\\\"] to large_file_100mb_degraded_mode_measurement so the 100 MiB allocation no longer runs on default `cargo test`. A smaller deterministic degraded-mode default test (ci_large_file_degraded_open_and_viewport_are_bounded) already exists.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-editor\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"The same 100MB test is now #[ignore], i.e. a dedicated report-only measurement excluded from the default pass/fail suite (the recipe's accepted resolution); its eprintln! latency report still runs under `cargo test -- --ignored`.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-editor\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added small deterministic non-ignored default-run companions: undo_redo_round_trips_content_for_default_runs (asserts undo/redo content round-trip) and snapshot_retention_and_release_for_default_runs (asserts pin counts before/after save+ack). Heavy benchmark variants remain #[ignore].\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-editor\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"In apply_edits, deltas are now recomputed against the final staged buffer. Edits still apply descending (no offset drift during mutation), then a second ascending pass carries a cumulative length shift so each ChangedDelta byte_range/utf16_range reflects the higher edit's post-edit position instead of the original offset. Added regression test batch_edit_deltas_track_cumulative_shift_from_lower_edits.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\", \"crates/legion-editor/tests/atomicity_and_retention.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-editor\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"set_cursors now validates every Cursor.position via buffer.try_byte_offset before storing; set_selections validates both range endpoints and start<=end (returning EditorError::InvalidEdit on inversion). Invalid editor state can no longer be persisted, so viewport_projection's protocol_range/try_byte_offset calls cannot fail on stored state.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-editor\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"EditorRequest::ApplyTransaction no longer returns a false EditorResponse::Transaction success. A TextTransactionDescriptor carries only changed-range metadata (no replacement text), so mutation is impossible from it; the handler now validates buffer identity then returns ProtocolError::unsupported directing callers to ApplyEdit (fail-closed). Identity-mismatch error path preserved.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-editor\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"EditorRequest::Overlay no longer returns a false OverlayApplied success. The DiagnosticOverlay request carries no buffer/workspace identity to resolve a target, and engine.set_overlays results are never projected anywhere (state.overlays is write-only). Handler now returns ProtocolError::unsupported (fail-closed) until overlay routing is implemented.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-editor\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Resolved the contract contradiction by aligning the viewport message with the implemented-and-tested behavior. request_save already assembles degraded-file text from chunks, and large_file_save_assembles_from_chunks + large_file_undo_redo_round_trips_content assert this success path. The misleading LargeFileStatus message claiming 'Phase 1 saves fail closed' was updated to state saves assemble the full file from chunks on request.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Chose the 'support degraded saves' contract over fail-closed because existing passing tests enforce that degraded saves succeed via chunk assembly; failing closed would have regressed working, tested functionality. EditorError::DegradedSaveUnavailable remains a public (unused) variant \\u2014 no new warning since it is a pub enum variant. Separately fixed a pre-existing/parallel build break: legion_protocol::ViewportProjection gained a required `cursors: Vec<TextCoordinate>` field; the editor constructor now populates it from buffer cursor state (lib.rs ~1046).\", \"package\": \"legion-editor\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Split bundled-Rust support from plugin registration. Added private helper tree_sitter_language_is_bundled_rust (rust/rs only). highlight_captures_from_text and code_chunk_descriptors_from_text now gate on the bundled-Rust check (return empty for plugin/unsupported languages instead of running the Rust query). TreeSitterParser::parse now only runs the Rust tree-sitter path for rust/rs; plugin-registered languages route to LexicalFallbackParser and push an 'index.tree_sitter.plugin_grammar_unsupported' Warning diagnostic to both file_index.diagnostics and outcome.diagnostics. tree_sitter_supports_language still reports plugin grammars as supported but they no longer parse as Rust.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs\", \"crates/legion-index/tests/plugin_grammar.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Updated the existing test (which codified the buggy as-Rust behavior) to assert lexical fallback + diagnostic, and added bundled_rust_still_parses_via_tree_sitter to lock in the positive path. Real loaded-grammar worker for plugin grammars remains future work; fail-soft fallback is in place.\", \"package\": \"legion-index\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced all three .lock().expect(...) calls on PLUGIN_TREE_SITTER_GRAMMAR_REGISTRY (register_plugin_tree_sitter_grammars, plugin_tree_sitter_grammar_is_registered, reset_plugin_tree_sitter_grammar_registry_for_tests) with .unwrap_or_else(PoisonError::into_inner) so a poisoned lock recovers instead of panicking the indexing process. Added PoisonError to the std::sync import.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-index\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"In build_rename_preview_payload, changed coverage_kind from Complete to Partial because a single SymbolFileMapRecord only carries this file's shallow declaration/reference ranges and cannot prove cross-file references were searched. Also replaced the empty diagnostics vec with an 'index.rename.single_file_coverage' Warning explaining cross-file references were not searched.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs\", \"crates/legion-index/tests/index_workflows.rs\"], \"notes\": \"SymbolFileMapRecord carries no workspace-complete/freshness proof (reference_ranges are documented as 'known from the shallow map'), so Partial is always correct here. Updated the workflow test that asserted Complete.\", \"package\": \"legion-index\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"read_until_correlated_response no longer drops responses carrying a different json_rpc_id. Added a response_stash: HashMap<u64, LspCorrelatedResponse> to LspStdioSession; out-of-order responses are now correlated and stashed by json_rpc_id, and read_response_for drains the stash before reading new frames. Unknown/already-resolved ids (e.g. late responses for cancelled requests) are still skipped.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Existing session contract tests (cancel/late-response, multi-request reuse) still pass.\", \"package\": \"legion-lsp\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"Added a deadline derived from pending.timeout_ms around the read loop in read_until_correlated_response (Instant-based, checked between frames). On expiry it calls self.client.resolve_timeout(expected_request_id, elapsed_ms) and returns the Timeout-status LspCorrelatedResponse instead of blocking until EOF. read_response_for now threads pending.timeout_ms through.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Bounds the wait whenever the server keeps emitting frames (notifications / other responses). A fully SILENT server is still bounded only by the future async read pump the type docs describe: std pipe reads have no portable timeout, so the deadline can only be observed between frames without a dedicated reader thread. The type is documented as intentionally synchronous (WS03.T1), so the async pump/$/cancelRequest emission remains as the follow-up; no insecure silent-proceed path was left in place.\", \"package\": \"legion-lsp\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"prepare_request now uses checked_add(1) and returns LspRuntimeResult<LspPendingRequest>, surfacing a new LspRuntimeError::JsonRpcIdExhausted instead of saturating at u64::MAX and reusing the id (which corrupted the correlation tables). send_request propagates with `?`; the 5 in-package test call sites in lifecycle_contract.rs were updated with .unwrap().\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs\", \"crates/legion-lsp/tests/lifecycle_contract.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Signature change is confined to this package (only callers are send_request and in-crate tests; legion-protocol has an unrelated prepare_request of its own).\", \"package\": \"legion-lsp\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"completion_projection_for_item now computes score_basis_points in u32: penalty = (index as u32).saturating_mul(100); 10_000u32.saturating_sub(penalty) as u16. The result is always <= 10_000 so the final u16 cast is lossless, and large indices can no longer wrap to a top score.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-lsp\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"mock_lsp_server read_frame now rejects Content-Length greater than a new MAX_FRAME_PAYLOAD_BYTES (64 MiB, mirroring LspFramer::MAX_FRAME_PAYLOAD_BYTES) with MockIoError::Protocol before allocating the payload buffer, matching the production read_lsp_frame bound.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-lsp/src/bin/mock_lsp_server.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-lsp\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"The unknown-method (`other`) arm now uses id.map(...) so unknown NOTIFICATIONS (id absent) get no response, while unknown REQUESTS still receive the -32601 error. This stops the mock emitting `\\\"id\\\": null` responses to notifications.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-lsp/src/bin/mock_lsp_server.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-lsp\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"rust_analyzer_initializes_against_legion_repo_when_opted_in is now an #[ignore]-gated live-smoke target. The two silent early returns were converted to hard failures: it asserts LEGION_RUN_RUST_ANALYZER_SMOKE=1 and asserts the rust-analyzer binary is available (panic instead of eprintln+return), so the real-server launch path cannot silently rot. Run via `cargo test -- --ignored` in a dedicated CI job.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-lsp/tests/stdio_transport_contract.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Verified it now reports as `ignored` in the default test run.\", \"package\": \"legion-lsp\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the unused underscore bindings in the rust-analyzer smoke with real assertions on the deterministic surfaces: completion contains an `Alpha` entry; hover label is non-empty and mentions `add`; definition/declaration/references resolve at least one location; signatureHelp has a non-empty `signatures` array; document outline and workspace symbols include `add`; folding ranges and semantic-token `data` are non-empty. Per the fix recipe's narrowing option, implementation/typeDefinition/inlayHint/codeLens remain smoke-exercised only (legitimately empty/config-dependent for a free function) with explanatory comments rather than flaky assertions.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-lsp/tests/stdio_transport_contract.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Assertions run only under the #[ignore] live job; could not execute them here (no rust-analyzer in this environment), but they compile under clippy --all-targets.\", \"package\": \"legion-lsp\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added protocol_workspace_configs/protocol_file_metadata/protocol_sessions (#[serde(default)] maps) and protocol_trust (#[serde(default)] Vec, because its (WorkspaceId,PrincipalId) tuple key cannot be a JSON map key) to PersistedState; copied them in From<&InMemoryStorage>; restored them in From<PersistedState> (rebuilding the trust map from the record list) instead of HashMap::new(). Added flush/reopen regression test file_backed_storage_roundtrips_protocol_workspace_metadata_session_and_trust exercising SaveWorkspaceConfig/SaveFileMetadata/SaveSessionRecord/SaveTrustRecord.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"protocol_trust persisted as a flat Vec<TrustRecord> and rebuilt on load because serde_json rejects tuple map keys; all other three persist as native maps with integer/string keys.\", \"package\": \"legion-storage\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Reordered record_event to persist+validate event metadata first (self.handle(SaveEventMetadata)? ) and only then emit. If emit fails after a successful store it now returns an explicit partial-failure ProtocolError (code storage_event_emit_failed_after_store) while keeping the persisted record, instead of emitting before storing. Added test record_event_persists_before_emitting_and_fails_closed_on_store_error verifying no event is emitted when the store fails and exactly one is emitted on success.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-storage\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the integrity verification with a SHA-256 digest (new storage_checksum + inline pure-Rust sha256_digest, no new crate dependency since sha2 is not a dep of legion-storage and Cargo.toml must not be edited). STORAGE_CHECKSUM_ALGORITHM is now legion-storage-sha256-v1; backup_file uses storage_checksum; recover_from_backup verifies sha256 for new markers and keeps a legacy branch (LEGACY_STORAGE_CHECKSUM_ALGORITHM via stable_storage_sum) for old sum:len markers, returning algorithm-mismatch otherwise. Added test storage_checksum_is_collision_resistant_and_order_sensitive (known SHA-256 vectors + permutation that fools the legacy sum now differs).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Implemented SHA-256 inline rather than via the sha2 crate because adding a dependency requires editing Cargo.toml, which is out of scope; legacy checksum retained read-only for backward compatibility.\", \"package\": \"legion-storage\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"In FileBackedStorage::open the corrupt-parse branch now captures fs::rename's Result: on Ok it returns StorageError::Corrupt with the quarantine_path (move actually happened); on Err it returns StorageError::Failed describing the quarantine failure, so a failed rename no longer reports the file as quarantined while leaving the corrupt primary in place.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"No new unit test: simulating a rename failure portably (held handle / read-only dir) is platform-dependent; existing file_backed_storage_corrupt_file_is_quarantined covers the success path.\", \"package\": \"legion-storage\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/secrets.rs does not exist; InMemorySecretStore/SecretStoreError appear nowhere in this package (only lib.rs is present). The described behavior is not implemented here.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"No secret-store implementation exists in legion-storage.\", \"package\": \"legion-storage\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"provider_secret_reference and the format!(\\\"{provider_id}:{secret_name}\\\") keyring-account construction do not exist anywhere in legion-storage (no secrets.rs).\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-storage\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"The string-matching keyring 'not found' classification does not exist in legion-storage. The only keyring usage in the repo is legion-retention's keyring_error, which lives in a different package and must not be edited from here.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Real location is legion-retention (keyring_error), outside this package's scope.\", \"package\": \"legion-storage\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the inert placeholder_docs_hygiene_test_file_compiles test with docs_hygiene_passes_for_clean_minimal_repo, which actually calls run_docs_hygiene on a clean fixture and asserts it passes.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/tests/docs_hygiene.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Distinct from the release_pipeline 'Finding 17' (xtask.md).\", \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"docs_hygiene_checks_untracked_markdown_in_git_repo now captures the `git init` and `git add` outputs and asserts output.status.success(), printing stdout/stderr on failure, so a failed git fixture no longer silently degrades the test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/tests/docs_hygiene.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 19\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Extracted a pure classify_skeleton_status(total, budget) in perf_harness.rs (now the single source of truth used by plan_perf_harness) and replaced the two stub tests with perf_harness_classifies_status_failed_when_total_exceeds_budget (deterministically asserts Failed/Passed/Skipped) plus a zero-budget Skipped test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/perf_harness.rs\", \"xtask/tests/perf_harness.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 20\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added pub apply_fail_on_budget_value(&mut, &str) that takes an injected value; apply_fail_on_budget_override now delegates to it. The test was rewritten to call apply_fail_on_budget_value with literal strings, removing all process-global env mutation (no more unsafe set_var/remove_var race).\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/perf_harness.rs\", \"xtask/tests/perf_harness.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 21\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"release_pipeline TempRepo::new now includes std::process::id() and a static AtomicU64 counter in the temp dir name, matching the docs_hygiene/perf fixtures, guaranteeing uniqueness under coarse clock granularity.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/tests/release_pipeline.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added a `#[arg(long = \\\"no-strict\\\")] no_strict: bool` negation flag to all four subcommands (PerfHarness, VerifyPerfHarness, LegionBench, VerifyLegionBench) and resolve effective strict as `strict && !no_strict` in the main dispatch, so --no-strict now actually disables strict mode as the docs claim.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/main.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Existing default-true behavior preserved; --no-strict now works as documented.\", \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added a `--config` arg to the VerifyReleasePipeline variant (matching ReleasePipeline) and threaded it into run_verify_release_pipeline_command, so a custom config used for release-pipeline can be verified instead of always loading the default example config.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/main.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Rewrote markdown_section to iterate lines via a new parse_atx_heading helper: it now requires a real ATX heading line whose level and label match (no more substring matches in prose/code blocks) and terminates at the next heading whose level <= the matched level. Added three unit tests.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/main.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"check_markdown_links now resolves normal relative links only against file.parent(); dropped the root.join(&normalized) fallback so a nested broken link (e.g. README.md) no longer passes just because the repo root has a same-named file. Leading-`/` root-relative handling is unchanged.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"run_docs_hygiene no longer silently `continue`s on read error; it pushes a new DocsHygieneViolationKind::UnreadableFile violation so an unreadable tracked markdown file causes a non-zero exit (fail-closed).\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"is_allowlisted now matches on path-segment boundaries via a new path_has_prefix helper (rel == prefix or rel starts with prefix+'/'), so allowlist `docs/foo` no longer matches sibling `docs/foo-old.md`.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Changed BacklogCard.dependencies to Option<Vec<String>> (removed #[serde(default)]) so an omitted field deserializes to None vs. `[]` being Some([]); check_required_fields now requires dependencies.is_some(), and validation iterates dependencies.iter().flatten(). Updated existing literals and added two tests (omitted rejected, present-empty accepted). Verified the real backlog declares dependencies for all 146 tasks.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/kanban_backlog.rs\", \"xtask/tests/kanban_backlog.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"verify_legion_bench_report now does full task equality (expected != &result.task) in the zip loop and recomputes the summary from report.tasks via a shared recompute_summary helper (also used by plan_legion_bench_report), rejecting any mismatch. This catches tampered task fields, tampered scores (via average_score), and tampered summary counts. Added two tamper-rejection tests.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/legion_bench.rs\", \"xtask/tests/legion_bench.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"score_task no longer conflates tests_passed with require_tests_pass: it now sets tests_passed=true (synthetic baseline run passes) and gates with tests_gate = !require_tests_pass || tests_passed, so a task with require_tests_pass=false can pass. Default-suite behavior (all require_tests_pass=true) is unchanged.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/legion_bench.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"run_no_egui_textedit no longer `continue`s on read error; it pushes a new NoEguiTextEditViolationKind::UnreadableFile violation so an unreadable scanned file causes a non-zero exit (fail-closed).\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/no_egui_textedit.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"is_scanned and is_allowlisted now match on path-segment boundaries via a new path_has_prefix helper, so a configured prefix no longer matches sibling paths that merely share the byte prefix.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/no_egui_textedit.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"plan_release_pipeline now passes the channel-adjusted `&version` (not `&workspace_version`) into build_version_stamp, so version_stamp.package_version matches each descriptor's version (e.g. `0.1.0-preview` for the preview channel).\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/release_pipeline.rs\"], \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"write_descriptors now pre-collects descriptor_file_stem values into a HashSet and returns an explicit collision error before writing anything, so two installer-target names normalizing to the same `<stem>.toml` no longer silently overwrite. Added a collision test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"xtask/src/release_pipeline.rs\", \"xtask/tests/release_pipeline.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Distinct from the docs_hygiene-test 'Finding 17' (tests---remaining-crates.md).\", \"package\": \"xtask\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added shared_blocking_client() (OnceLock) built via reqwest::blocking::Client::builder().connect_timeout(10s).timeout(120s) and reused it at all four blocking HTTP sites (ReqwestProviderHttpTransport::post_json, Anthropic post_json/post_text, StreamableHttpMcpTransport::send). Timeout/connect failures map to ProviderError::RequestFailed / McpClientError::Transport as before. Also fixed a latent panic: the provider HTTP path built a rustls client without installing a crypto provider; shared_blocking_client now installs it eagerly. Added test shared_blocking_client_builds_with_timeouts.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"A true network-hang timeout test would require a deliberately slow server; the added test verifies the timeout-configured client builds. Real elapsed-timeout behavior is enforced by reqwest's connect_timeout/timeout.\", \"package\": \"legion-ai-providers\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"OpenAiCompatibleProvider::complete now builds the chat/completions payload incrementally and only sets max_tokens/temperature when Some(..), mirroring OpenAiResponsesProvider::request_payload, so unset options are omitted instead of serialized as JSON null. Added test openai_compatible_provider_omits_unset_sampling_options.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-ai-providers\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Introduced AnthropicCredentialKind (ApiKey|AuthToken) and AnthropicCredential; transport post_json/post_text now send x-api-key for API keys and Authorization: Bearer only for auth tokens via apply_anthropic_credential. from_env detects the kind per matched env var (preserving precedence); added credential_kind field, with_transport_kind constructor, and credential() helper. Updated the AnthropicMessagesTransport trait signature (package-internal; no external impls). Added test anthropic_api_key_uses_x_api_key_and_auth_token_uses_bearer.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Trait signature change is confined to this package (grep found no external implementors/callers). Existing with_transport keeps its public signature and defaults to ApiKey kind.\", \"package\": \"legion-ai-providers\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Changed OpenAiResponsesProvider::request_payload store default from true to false so provider-side response storage requires explicit openai.responses.store=true opt-in. Added test openai_responses_store_defaults_to_false_without_metadata.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-ai-providers\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Reworked StdioMcpSession to read stdout on a dedicated thread that pushes lines over an mpsc channel; send_on_session now enforces a per-request deadline (STDIO_MCP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=30s) via recv_timeout, returning McpClientError::Transport on timeout, channel error, or disconnect. This bounds the time the session mutex is held and prevents a wedged/silent or notification-flooding server from hanging the caller indefinitely. Drop joins the reader thread after killing the child (pipe closes -> EOF).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Full fix: the reader-thread + recv_timeout design gives a real wall-clock deadline even for a silent server, not just a flood bound.\", \"package\": \"legion-ai-providers\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Hardened spawn_http_fixture: listener set non-blocking with an accept loop bounded by HTTP_FIXTURE_DEADLINE (20s), per-stream read/write timeouts (10s), and a while handled<4 loop that self-terminates at the deadline. Because the fixture thread now always exits, the test's handle.join() is bounded; an early client failure surfaces as the existing requests.len()==4 assertion instead of an indefinite hang.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/mcp_ga_conformance.rs\"], \"notes\": \"\", \"package\": \"legion-ai-providers\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the hard-coded python3 stdio fixtures with a Cargo-built Rust fixture binary at src/bin/mcp_stdio_fixture.rs (auto-discovered, so no Cargo.toml edit), referenced from tests via env!(\\\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_mcp_stdio_fixture\\\"). The binary reimplements both the conformance and pid JSON-RPC fixture behaviors (mode arg). Removed the python script helpers; stdio_transport/stdio_pid_transport now invoke the binary. External python3 runtime dependency eliminated.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/mcp_ga_conformance.rs\", \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/bin/mcp_stdio_fixture.rs\"], \"notes\": \"New binary is a normal package target using serde_json (already a non-dev dependency); builds and passes clippy under --all-targets -D warnings.\", \"package\": \"legion-ai-providers\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added MemoryError::UnsupportedSnapshotVersion variant and a SUPPORTED_SNAPSHOT_SCHEMA_VERSION=1 constant; from_snapshot now rejects schema_version 0 and any version above the supported max before constructing Self. Added test from_snapshot_rejects_unsupported_schema_versions.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-memory\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added an explicit candidate_id.trim().is_empty() guard at the start of validate_memory_candidate returning InvalidProposalMetadata, mirroring validate_legion_workflow_candidate. Added test memory_candidate_rejects_empty_candidate_id.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-memory\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Converted retain, retain_legion_workflow_candidate, and retain_trace_record to upsert: replace an existing entry with the same candidate_id/trace_id instead of blindly pushing, so duplicates can no longer accumulate. Delete semantics (filter-by-id) remain consistent with the now-unique keys. Added test repeated_retain_does_not_duplicate_records covering all three paths.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-memory\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the hard-coded EventSequence(13) in from_session_metadata with EventSequence(session.generated_at.0), deriving a distinct sequence from session metadata. Kept the public signature unchanged (avoiding ripple to legion-app which calls this), per the internal-fix preference. Added test workflow_candidate_sequence_is_derived_from_session_metadata.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"from_session_metadata is also called from crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs, so the signature was preserved and the sequence is derived internally instead of adding a parameter.\", \"package\": \"legion-memory\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"dispatch_host_call now computes next_output_bytes = output_bytes_used.saturating_add(label.len()) and denies with QuotaExceeded when the cumulative total exceeds max_output_bytes; only commits the accumulated value on accept. Added test plugin_runtime_accumulates_output_bytes_across_calls.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-plugin\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added explicit begin_invocation/end_invocation methods on PluginRuntimeHost; begin_invocation resets host_calls_used and output_bytes_used to 0 (sets Running), end_invocation returns to Idle, making the per-invocation quota docs accurate. Added test plugin_runtime_resets_quota_counters_on_invocation_boundary.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-plugin\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"CommandDescriptor and Contribution arms of PluginRuntimePort::handle now verify the item against loaded state. register_command requires a loaded/activated plugin that declares the required capability AND has a matching Command contribution in its manifest, else returns ProtocolError plugin_command_not_registered. register_contribution requires the descriptor's plugin_id to resolve to a loaded/activated plugin, else plugin_not_loaded/plugin_not_active. Added two tests.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"PluginCommandDescriptor carries no PluginId (in legion-protocol, out of scope to change), so the command arm matches across loaded plugins by command_id + required_capability instead of a direct plugin lookup. ContributionDescriptor has no required_capability/contribution-name mapping into the manifest's heterogeneous contribution enum, so the contribution arm enforces the plugin-loaded/activated check (the reliably verifiable part) rather than a fragile name match that could reject valid contributions.\", \"package\": \"legion-plugin\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the DefaultHasher body of stable_hash with a fixed 128-bit FNV-1a implementation (full-width, deterministic across compiler/std versions) and mixed in a STABLE_HASH_VERSION tag so persisted/protocol-facing ids (WorkspaceId, git hunk ids, content-version digest) are namespaced by algorithm version. Added a unit test asserting determinism, no-collision, and 128-bit width.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"All three consumers (WorkspaceId@~455, hunk id@~1790 via {:032x}, content digest@~3447 via `as u64`) now benefit from a stable algorithm with no API change.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Removed the gix Debug-format scraping (git_status_entries_gix now delegates to the authoritative CLI porcelain parser, mirroring git_blame_lines_gix) and deleted the fragile extract_gix_status_path/extract_gix_status_code helpers. Extracted the porcelain parsing into a pure parse_git_porcelain_status fn and added a rename/copy/delete/untracked/modified unit test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Preserved the existing CLI parser's rename/copy keying behavior exactly (keys on trailing source field) to avoid introducing new behavior. The gix dependency is now unused in source but Cargo.toml is out of scope; no unused-dependency lint is enabled so build/clippy stay clean.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"WorkspaceSearchHit::line_number is user-facing; changed both search sites to (line_number as u32).saturating_add(1) so the first line reports 1, matching the one-based blame convention, and documented the field as one-based.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"No existing tests asserted specific search-hit line numbers.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Cited file crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/smoke.rs does not exist and the described hosted-Anthropic smoke test is in a different package (legion-ai-providers), outside legion-project scope.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Real location would be legion-ai-providers if reintroduced; not editable here.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Cited file crates/legion-plugin/tests/hostile.rs does not exist; legion-plugin has no tests/ dir. This is a different package, outside legion-project scope.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Real location would be legion-plugin if reintroduced; not editable here.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Cited file crates/legion-plugin/tests/quotas.rs does not exist; legion-plugin has no tests/ dir. Different package, outside legion-project scope.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Real location would be legion-plugin if reintroduced; not editable here.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the fixed 120ms sleep in indexed_workspace_search_refreshes_after_file_changes with a bounded retry loop (5s deadline, 20ms backoff) that drains poll_watcher_events and re-runs the indexed search until the invalidation is observed (hit_count==0).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-project/tests/search_workspace.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Test verified passing.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added a non-ignored test indexed_workspace_search_matches_live_scan_for_dozens_of_files (32 files) validating indexed-vs-live equivalence for larger fixtures, complementing the still-#[ignore]d 500-file benchmark so default runs cover multi-file indexed search.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-project/tests/search_workspace.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Test verified passing.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the fixed 80ms sleep in watcher_recovery_overflow_then_rescan_emits_recovery_event with a bounded poll loop (5s deadline, 20ms backoff) retrying poll_watcher_events until the Modified recovery event appears.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-project/tests/watcher_recovery.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Recovery is NOT synchronous (gated behind the 64ms WATCHER_RENAME_DEBOUNCE_MILLIS debounce), so a plain sleep removal failed; the bounded poll loop is the correct robust fix per the recipe. Verified passing.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Introduced an RAII TempWorkspace struct (Deref<Target=Path>, Drop removes the root via remove_dir_all and any tracked outside fixtures via remove_file). create_temp_workspace now returns it; removed all manual `let _ = remove_dir_all(root);` cleanup lines and the symlink test's outside-file cleanup, which is now tracked via track_outside.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-project/tests/path_boundary.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Deref coercion keeps all existing &root/root.join call sites unchanged. track_outside is cfg-allowed dead on non-unix (only the unix symlink test uses it). All path_boundary tests verified passing.\", \"package\": \"legion-project\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added `|| self.failed_verification_count > 0` to the Ready-state validation guard in LegionWorkflowTrackerRecord::validate so a merge-ready record with failed/blocked verification gates is now rejected. Added regression test legion_workflow_tracker_rejects_failed_verification_ready_state.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-tracker/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Defect re-confirmed at the renamed/current location (validate fn, Ready guard). failed_verification_count was previously never validated.\", \"package\": \"legion-tracker\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"initialize() now passes sandbox_path to `git worktree add` via .arg(&self.sandbox_path) (OsStr) instead of .to_str().unwrap(), removing the non-UTF-8 path panic.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-agent\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"validate_containment now returns the normalized sandbox-relative PathBuf and rejects residual ParentDir/RootDir/Prefix components; generate_proposal builds the CanonicalPath from that normalized path (joined with '/'), so `..` segments no longer persist in the emitted payload.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"validate_containment signature changed from Result<(),_> to Result<PathBuf,_>; it is only used within this crate (one call site + tests), so no cross-crate ripple.\", \"package\": \"legion-agent\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"generate_proposal now reads the target's on-disk state (new base_target_preconditions helper) and populates expected_file_length/expected_modified_at/expected_fingerprint as a concurrency guard; misleading 'compares with HEAD' doc corrected. Added a test asserting preconditions populate when the target exists and stay None for a genuine create.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Payload still ProposalPayload::CreateFile even when a base file exists, because emitting a TextEditProposal requires a FileId/EditBatch that the generator's inputs do not provide. The security-relevant defect (no concurrency guard) is resolved; the create-vs-edit payload distinction remains. Fingerprint uses std DefaultHasher (algorithm label 'std-default-hasher-v1') since no crypto-hash crate is available in this package's deps.\", \"package\": \"legion-agent\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"record_proposal_output now fails closed with AgentError::InvalidLegionWorkflow when an evidence_id/result_id for the worker already exists, preventing colliding ids and duplicate worker_results/evidence_records. Added a duplicate-record test.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-agent\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"provider_route_request_from_worker now derives cancellation_token and event_sequence per-worker via new derive_cancellation_token/derive_event_sequence helpers (deterministic DefaultHasher over worker_id + correlation_id) instead of the constant 13. Added a test asserting two provider workers get distinct audit identities.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Identities are deterministic per (worker_id, correlation_id) rather than a true monotonic session-supplied sequence; a session-threaded monotonic counter would require a signature/state change beyond this static helper. The core defect (all routes sharing one cancellation/audit identity) is resolved.\", \"package\": \"legion-agent\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"main() now tracks whether a path arg was explicitly supplied. When the scratch.txt default is used and the file does not exist, it opens via open_new_file (CreateNew intent) instead of open_file (Existing intent), so startup no longer aborts on a missing scratch file. Explicit user-supplied paths still use open_file.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/src/main.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added `prompt_prefix: String::new()` to the AssistedAiProviderRouteRequest literal in the #[cfg(test)] route_request() helper. Verified with `cargo build -p legion-app --no-default-features --all-targets` (offline_ai compiled) which now succeeds, and the offline_ai tests pass.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/src/offline_ai.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"validate_containment no longer panics: both std::env::current_dir().unwrap() calls now propagate via a closure returning OfflineAiError::InvalidMetadata (fn already returns Result). Added canonicalize_existing_prefix() which canonicalizes the longest existing ancestor of the candidate (resolving symlinks in the on-disk portion) and re-appends the non-existent tail, then compares canonical paths so a symlink placed inside the sandbox can no longer escape via lexical-only normalization.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/src/offline_ai.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Confirmed proposal.rs does not exist in legion-app/src and no accepted-target/filtered-batch code (filtered_batch, for_accepted, build_filtered, accepted_targets, filter_proposal) matches anywhere in the package. The described defect has no location in the current tree.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Planned split-module layout never landed; the described filtered-batch edge-dropping behavior does not exist in this package.\", \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Eliminated the disk-vs-buffer inconsistency on post-commit audit failure. SaveWorkflowFailure gained a `committed: Option<SaveWorkflowOutput>` field; only the Ok(applied) branch's observe_proposal_response failure sets it (the on-disk write already committed). save_buffer's Err arm now, when `committed` is present, acknowledges the save and calls bind_saved_buffer + clear_dirty_prompt_for to reconcile editor state with the persisted bytes before surfacing the audit failure as Rejected, so disk and editor state stay consistent. All other failure paths set committed: None (no disk mutation).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Implemented recipe option 3 (commit saved metadata while surfacing the audit failure) rather than a pre-save rollback, because SaveWorkflowService is a free function without the &mut self checkpoint machinery; this fully resolves the dirty-buffer-over-saved-disk inconsistency.\", \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"The post-initialize ACP block's two early returns now run orchestrator.cleanup(&permission) before returning. acp_host_command.run(...) and std::fs::read_to_string(...) were converted from `?` to match arms that, on Err, run cleanup and surface cleanup failures alongside the original error message before returning AppCompositionError::AiRuntime. The sandbox is no longer leaked on these failure paths.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"Confirmed no filtered/partial delegated-apply path exists: filtered_batch, build_filtered, filter_proposal, filtered_apply_required, accepted_targets match nowhere in legion-app/src. The described projection-vs-apply divergence cannot be located.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"No subset/partial-apply code in this package; described behavior does not exist.\", \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"parse_terminal_shell_output now tracks whether the OSC sequence was terminated (BEL/ST). On an unterminated sequence it pushes the raw bytes from the ESC] introducer onward into visible_output and breaks, instead of silently dropping the trailing remainder. Added unit tests parse_terminal_keeps_unterminated_osc_bytes and parse_terminal_handles_terminated_osc.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"terminal_shell_cwd_from_osc now URL-aware: splits host from path (file:/// => empty host, localhost treated as empty), percent-decodes each path segment via a new percent_decode helper, special-cases Windows drive-letter paths (file:///C:/Users -> C:/Users via is_windows_drive_prefix) and UNC paths (file://server/share -> //server/share). Added tests osc7_cwd_decodes_windows_drive_and_percent and osc7_cwd_handles_localhost_and_unc.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the per-token comment predicate with a proper overlap rejection over the full delimiter span. Rust: reject Comment tokens where start_col < rust_slashes+2 && end_col > rust_slashes; TOML: reject where start_col <= toml_hash && end_col > toml_hash. A comment token starting at the second slash inside a string is now correctly flagged as a failure.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_contracts.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Introduced a Drop-guarded TempWorkspace (Deref+AsRef<Path>) returned by create_root(); Drop does a prefix/location-checked remove_dir_all (temp_dir + 'legion-app-daily-editing-'). Removed all 11 manual `let _ = remove_dir_all(&root)` calls so panics no longer leak temp roots.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_contracts.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Bound the git init Output and assert status.success(), including status code, stdout and stderr in the failure message, so a failed `git init` no longer lets the gitignore test continue in a non-repo.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_search.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Made temp_workspace return a Drop-guarded TempWorkspace (Deref+AsRef<Path>) with a prefix/location-checked remove_dir_all on drop ('legion_app_delegated_'); removed the three ad-hoc remove_dir_all calls so all tests (waiting-plan, approved-plan, acp-host, hunk, chat) clean up uniformly even on panic.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/delegated_task_integration.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added a once-checked git_available() helper (OnceLock running `git --version`) and a fail-fast assert at the top of TempGitRepo::new() with an explicit environment diagnostic, so a missing git binary surfaces as a clear environment error rather than a confusing product-test failure inside run_git.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/git_workflow.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added merge_feature_expecting_conflict() which captures the merge Output, asserts !status.success() and that `git diff --name-only --diff-filter=U` is non-empty (with stdout/stderr in messages), then replaced all five discarded-ExitStatus `git merge feature` blocks with this helper.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/git_workflow.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the single TerminalInput+OutputPoll+Search sequence with: send input, then a bounded poll loop (10s deadline, 25ms backoff) re-dispatching TerminalOutputPoll until output_rows is non-empty, then search; final assert reports the projection on failure. Removes the one-poll race on slow hosts with the real PTY fixture.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/language_terminal_integration.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Re-rooted temp_workspace in std::env::temp_dir() (was current_dir/target) with a pid+timestamp+counter unique suffix and returned a Drop-guarded TempWorkspace (Deref+AsRef<Path>) doing a prefix/location-checked remove_dir_all ('legion-workflow-integration-'); removed the three manual remove_dir_all calls.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/legion_workflow_integration.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Removed the hard-coded /13.0 denominator (now cases.len()) and added a catalog-drift guard: enumerate the live registered command catalog via an OpenPalette '>' projection, assert every case title exists in the catalog (no stale cases), and assert catalog == case-titles UNION an explicit git-mutation allowlist so any new command added without a case/allowlist entry fails with a catalog-vs-cases diff. Also changed the loop to borrow `&cases` so the table is reusable after the loop.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/palette.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Renamed app_plugin_manifest_registers_tree_sitter_grammar_through_phase_five_channel to ..._metadata_through_phase_five_channel and added a doc comment making explicit that it validates metadata registration only and deliberately does not create/validate/load the .wasm artifact (artifact_uri is a placeholder). Chose the recipe's second option because the loader does not enforce artifact existence and that enforcement lives in src/ (out of scope for tests/).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/plugin_grammar.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Artifact existence/loadability is still not validated; enforcing it requires a loader change in crates/legion-app/src (and a real fixture artifact), which is outside the tests/ scope restriction.\", \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Extracted poll_terminal_until(app, session_id, condition) with a generous 10s deadline that re-dispatches TerminalOutputPoll until the exact condition holds and panics with the last projection on timeout; replaced the fixed `for _ in 0..20 { sleep 25ms }` loop (~500ms ceiling) with it.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/terminal_workflow.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Wrapped create_root() output in a Drop-guarded TempWorkspace (Deref+AsRef<Path>) whose Drop performs a prefix-checked remove_dir_all using 'legion-terminal-workflow-{pid}-'; removed the manual `remove_dir_all(&root).ok()` cleanup calls in all three tests.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/terminal_workflow.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added a Drop-guarded OutsideFixture that builds the off-workspace path in root.parent() with a fresh Uuid::now_v7() suffix (eliminating the colliding TEMP_ROOT_COUNTER.load name with no pid/timestamp) and removes the file on drop with a prefix/location check. Used it for both the legion-escape and legion-outside fixtures; for the traversal test the unique file_name is reused to build the ../../ path so outside_normalized still matches. Removed the manual remove_file calls.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/workspace_vfs_integration.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Same fix as the app-&-agent Finding 12 (the cited legion-desktop palette_coverage.rs does not exist; the coverage test is in legion-app/tests/palette.rs). Removed the hard-coded /13.0 denominator (now cases.len()) and added a registered-command-catalog drift guard derived from the live palette projection.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-app/tests/palette.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Finding's source_file path (legion-desktop) is wrong; the real test lives in crates/legion-app/tests/palette.rs. Resolved by the same edit as the app-&-agent Finding 12.\", \"package\": \"legion-app\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"platform.rs high_dpi_status now reports any positive finite scale (including exactly 1.0) as os-observed; NOT_OBSERVED reserved for None/non-finite/<=0.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/platform.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"temporary_session_path now appends a static AtomicU64 nonce alongside process::id(), so concurrent same-path saves get unique temp files; the pre-write remove_file is now scoped to that unique path. Validated by session_store_save_publishes_validated_temp_and_cleans_intermediates (passes).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/session.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"DEFERRED\", \"summary\": \"Whole-document substring scan in reject_raw_source_markers is a genuine false-positive risk, but tests/session_restore.rs:338 (session_restore_store_rejects_raw_source_markers) explicitly asserts that a session_id of 'source_body' is rejected, enshrining the whole-document scan as intended defense-in-depth. Narrowing to field-scoped checks would break that test, which is out of scope (tests/). Left behavior unchanged.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Blocked by out-of-scope test that depends on the current behavior; fix requires editing tests/session_restore.rs.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added DesktopBridgeError::MissingRemoteDefaultBranch; OpenGitPullRequestUrl now returns that typed error when remote_default_branch is None/empty/whitespace instead of falling back to the current branch (which produced branch...branch self-compare URLs).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/bridge.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"OpenWorkspace Ok branch now assigns self.workspace_root = root.clone() and clears explorer_expansion so workspace-scoped state rebases to the newly opened root.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added DesktopRuntime::dispatch_ui_action which captures the handle_action Result, sets an Error status and refreshes the projection on failure. Replaced all four discard sites (handle_keyboard loop, palette query change, palette row click delta+dispatch, eframe ui output loop).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"editor_text_input_actions now tracks a running insertion coordinate: `at` is mutable and advanced via new advance_text_coordinate helper after each Text/Paste/ImeCommit action, so multiple text events in one frame target sequential positions instead of the original cursor offset.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Windows URL opener no longer goes through `cmd /C start`; new open_url_windows calls ShellExecuteW (linked from shell32, mirroring the existing MoveFileExW pattern) passing the URL as the single lpFile, so `&` and other metacharacters are not reinterpreted by cmd. Command import gated to non-windows.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added normalize_inline (control chars -> space) and normalize_markdown (control chars -> space plus backslash-escaping of markdown-sensitive chars) and applied them to workspace_label and each unsupported surface in rows() and to_markdown(). Verified operational_health/diagnostics tests use .contains() substrings that still match.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/health.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"FrameTimingRecorder now bounds both input_paint_samples and frame_durations_ms to MAX_RETAINED_SAMPLES (4096), evicting the oldest entry on push so a long-running session cannot grow them or summary()'s work unbounded.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/metrics.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Search result rows now pass row.snippet through a normalize_snippet helper (control chars -> spaces) before interpolation, preserving the one-line path:line:col snippet format.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/search.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"WindowsPackageConfig gained an optional target_triple (plus with_target_triple builder; new() defaults to None preserving the 3-arg API). plan_windows_package appends --target <triple> to cargo_args and builds executable_source as target/<triple>/<profile>/legion-desktop.exe when set, and fails closed (MissingWindowsTargetTriple) when packaging from a non-Windows host without a triple. Validated by packaging tests (4 pass).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/package.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"prepare_beta_workspace now takes real_workspace_root and resolves relative beta workspace paths (and the target/ root boundary) against the configured real_workspace_root instead of std::env::current_dir(). Call site updated to pass config.real_workspace_root.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/beta.rs\"], \"notes\": \"beta_workflow integration tests fail at runtime open due to parallel legion-security policy changes (path read denied) - confirmed pre-existing by reproducing identically with the original beta.rs.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"beta_smoke_command now shell-quotes each path argument via new shell_quote/shell_quote_path helpers (POSIX single-quote, simple args left bare) so paths with spaces/metacharacters yield a re-runnable command.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/beta.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Renderer smoke status now gates Passed on more than frame_count: added fail-closed gate checks via push_adapter_gate for clipboard/ime/file_dialog adapter paths (Some(false)/None -> error) and for unobserved focus and invalid/unobserved high-DPI scale. Status is Passed only when no gate errors. Validated platform_smoke tests still pass (they construct reports directly).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"SmokeObservations::high_dpi_status now accepts any positive finite scale (including 1.0) for the os-observed branch, matching the platform.rs fix.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"smoke_command now shell-quotes workspace/file/evidence/session-state/diagnostics-export arguments via local shell_quote/shell_quote_path helpers, so paths with spaces/metacharacters round-trip.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Added normalized_text_range helper and applied it at the drag SetSelection emit site (view.rs ~1930) so backwards drags no longer store an inverted range. drag_selection_range itself was left unchanged because tests/projection_rendering.rs:1532 asserts its raw (un-normalized) fallback output, which is out of scope to edit.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Normalization applied at the emit site rather than inside drag_selection_range to avoid breaking an out-of-scope unit test that asserts the raw range.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"render_fleet_canvas: the unbound 'Pause Workflow' and 'Add Constraint' buttons are now rendered disabled (add_enabled_ui(false) with on_disabled_hover_text) instead of live buttons whose clicks are dropped, and the hard-coded 'confidence 87%' literal was removed (no projected confidence field exists).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"render_delegated_hunk_review_controls now wraps all reviews and all hunks in a bounded vertical ScrollArea (max 280px) with no take() caps, so every review/hunk is reachable for accept/reject/pending instead of being silently truncated at 4 reviews / 6 hunks.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"git_relative_path now requires a component boundary after strip_prefix (remainder empty, starts with a separator, or root ends with a separator) before accepting, so root /repo no longer matches /repo2/src/lib.rs.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Privacy inspector record rendering now stably partitions records so denied/fully-redacted/external-egress/high-risk records sort first before take(10), and pushes an explicit 'privacy records omitted from preview: N' row when records exceed the cap, so sensitive records beyond index 10 are no longer invisible.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (assistant_rail.rs)\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"Fixed the gating logic in assistant_rail.rs: apply_as_proposal_available now requires `proposal_id.is_some() && complete`, and render_code_block only renders the Apply-as-proposal button when complete && apply_as_proposal_available (else shows 'proposal unavailable'). Could NOT wire the module: it is orphaned (view.rs declares only mod code_canvas_painter) and depends on legion_ai which is not a dependency of legion-desktop, so adding `pub mod assistant_rail` requires editing Cargo.toml (out of scope). The module is therefore not compiled and the fix cannot be verified by build/clippy.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/assistant_rail.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Source defect fixed for if/when the module is wired. Wiring needs a legion_ai dependency (Cargo.toml) which is out of scope; tests/assistant_rail.rs is pre-existing non-compiling because the module is not exported. The in-module #[cfg(test)] assertion (complete=true) remains satisfied.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (cloud_lane.rs)\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/cloud_lane.rs does not exist and no cloud-task cancellation-row rendering exists in view.rs. The cited string and panel are absent from current source.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (fleet_card.rs)\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"render_proposal_cards (live equivalent of fleet_card) now gates Approve/Reject on lifecycle: only Created/Validated/Previewed proposals expose enabled Approve/Reject (others render disabled via add_enabled_ui), and the lifecycle state label is surfaced on each card so terminal/applied/denied proposals no longer present active controls.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2 (fleet_card.rs)\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"render_proposal_cards now renders an explicit '{N} more proposals' overflow label after the take(4) loop, counting both rows beyond the cap and the projection's omitted_row_count.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (manifest_panel.rs)\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/manifest_panel.rs does not exist and the cited 'no context items projected before invocation' misreport is nowhere in source. The live trust_rows code simply omits the line when items are empty (no misreport), so the specific described defect is not present.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (provider_setup.rs)\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/provider_setup.rs and provider_policy_rows do not exist. The live provider rendering already uses authoritative projection fields (availability/class/risk/privacy/refusal reason_code) and does not re-derive policy labels from hard-coded class strings, so the described defect is absent.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (worker_panel.rs)\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/worker_panel.rs does not exist; no code parses display_safe_labels for a 'signoff:' prefix or constructs sign-off recovery actions from label text. display_safe_labels is only joined into a display string.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2 (worker_panel.rs)\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/worker_panel.rs does not exist; no view code constructs LegionWorkflowVerificationGateId/LegionWorkflowConflictId from display label text. Those typed IDs appear only in bridge.rs action variants and validation guards, so the described view-side ID-from-label transport defect is absent.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"DEFERRED\", \"summary\": \"Adding production-path coverage that drives the VSIX manifest through the plugin/install runtime, opens proposal context manifest + diff via the bridge from a real proposal, and records a verification run is a large workflow-test addition. It also cannot execute in this environment because DesktopRuntime::open fails (the runtime security policy denies reading temp workspaces). Left the fixture-shape asserts intact; did not add the runtime-driven coverage.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Distinct from Finding 2. Requires runtime install/proposal/verification entry points and a runtime that can open a workspace; in this env open() is denied by policy for temp paths.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"Added a structured no-autonomous-apply assertion in beta_acceptance_e2e.rs section 12: drive StartAiProposal/OpenProposalDetails/PreviewProposal through the production runtime, then assert every projected proposal_ledger_projection row's typed lifecycle.state is never ProposalLifecycleState::Applied or ::Approved, instead of relying only on substring scans of report.proposal_status. Imported ProposalLifecycleState.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/tests/beta_acceptance_e2e.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Adds a structured assertion on the projected proposal model. Cannot be exercised here: the test panics earlier at line 213 because run_beta_workflow returns 'blocked' (DesktopRuntime cannot open temp workspaces under this machine's security policy). A fully structured BetaWorkflowReport (lifecycle/allowed-action enum) would require editing src/beta.rs, which is outside this agent's tests-only scope.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"DEFERRED\", \"summary\": \"The proper fix (typed enums/fields on BetaWorkflowReport plus typed error variants for blocked/failed) lives in src/beta.rs and the error types, which are outside this agent's tests-only scope. The beta_workflow.rs test only holds the string-valued report (no runtime handle), so a projection-based assertion like the one added for Finding 2 is not available there.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Requires src/beta.rs structured fields; tests-only change cannot replace the substring checks meaningfully without them.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"DEFERRED\", \"summary\": \"A protocol-level fake-DAP integration test (launch request, breakpoint binding, stopped event, frames, variables from real protocol events) is a large harness addition that also needs production injection seams; the existing fixture/projection test is retained. No insecure production path exists to fail-close.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Needs a fake DAP server or real adapter plus a runtime that can launch; runtime open is also blocked by the temp-path security policy in this environment.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"DEFERRED\", \"summary\": \"A loopback/fake collaboration transport test feeding remote presence/conflict/proposal events through the production ingestion path is a substantial new harness requiring src injection points; the existing local-runtime projection test remains.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"No production injection seam available from tests-only scope; runtime open also denied for temp paths here.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the raw `source.contains(...)` boundary scan in desktop_control_trust_bridge_preserves_projection_only_boundary with a shared comment/string-stripped, whole-identifier matcher (common::assert_source_excludes) so the projection-only boundary fails only on a real source reference, not on prose or substrings. Test passes.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/tests/control_trust_bridge.rs\", \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/common/mod.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"DEFERRED\", \"summary\": \"A real-or-fake-DAP integration test validating launch/breakpoint/stopped/step/evaluate/error from the protocol layer is a large harness addition; the existing projection smoke test is kept. No insecure production path to fail-close.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Same constraints as Finding 4: needs fake DAP + openable runtime; temp-path policy blocks open here.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"NOT_APPLICABLE\", \"summary\": \"The cited tests/diagnostics_harness.rs does not exist (confirmed via Glob/ls). Diagnostics ingestion/validation lives in src/diagnostics.rs, which is outside this agent's tests-only scope; no buffer_id/URI diagnostics happy-path harness exists under tests/ to extend with negative cases.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Real behavior is in src/diagnostics.rs (unit-test territory). diagnostics_export.rs exists but is an export test, not the ingestion harness the finding describes.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the raw substring scan in intent_bridge_preserves_app_boundary with common::assert_source_excludes (whole-identifier, comment/string-aware). Test binary passes (17/17).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/tests/intent_bridge.rs\", \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/common/mod.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the bridge/view raw substring scan in desktop_phase4_dispatch_stays_projection_only with common::assert_source_excludes for AppComposition/legion_terminal/TerminalRuntime (whole identifiers, comment/string-stripped). That test passes; verified the forbidden identifiers are genuinely absent from src/bridge.rs and src/view.rs.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/tests/language_terminal_workflow.rs\", \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/common/mod.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Reworked platform_smoke_report_writes_evidence_file to use a new TempEvidenceDir helper with the workspace's nanos+atomic-counter+process-id naming pattern and a Drop guard that removes the dir under temp_dir even on panic, replacing the process-id-only name and manual end-of-test cleanup. Test passes (platform_smoke 6/6).\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/tests/platform_smoke.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the brittle raw substrings (\\\"pub payload\\\", \\\"pub text\\\", \\\"String,\\\") in platform_smoke_adapter_paths_route_without_metrics_payloads with a structural metadata-only check: common::assert_source_excludes forbids the whole identifiers String/payload/text in comment/string-stripped src/metrics.rs, so the metrics public API is asserted to carry only numeric aggregates. Test passes.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/tests/platform_smoke.rs\", \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/common/mod.rs\"], \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"FIXED\", \"summary\": \"Replaced the raw substring scan in projection_rendering_tests_preserve_app_boundary with common::assert_source_excludes for legion_app/AppComposition (whole identifiers, comment/string-aware). The change is the same pattern proven green in 5 other compiling test binaries.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/tests/projection_rendering.rs\", \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/common/mod.rs\"], \"notes\": \"PRE-EXISTING, unrelated: projection_rendering.rs does not compile against the current API (references legion_ui::ActiveBufferProjectionState and a `state` field that no longer exist; ActiveBufferProjection now exposes `degraded`, and ViewportProjection now requires line_wrapping_policy/wrap_column). This API drift is not part of this finding and not introduced by my change, but it prevents the binary from building; migrating ~11 call sites is a separate task needing src API semantics.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"DEFERRED\", \"summary\": \"A loopback/fake remote backend test driving connect/reconnect/offline/terminal+LSP descriptor/remote-proposal events through the production ingestion path is a large harness addition; the existing local-runtime projection test remains. No insecure production path to fail-close.\", \"files_changed\": [], \"notes\": \"Needs production injection seam + openable runtime; temp-path security policy blocks runtime open in this environment.\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\", \"action\": \"PARTIAL\", \"summary\": \"Hardened save_all_conflict_desktop_save_paths_dispatch_ui_intent: replaced raw include_str! substring checks with common::assert_source_includes(\\\"dispatch_ui_intent\\\") and common::assert_source_excludes(\\\"save_file_with_proposal\\\") (whole-identifier, comment/string-stripped) so the no-proposal-apply-save boundary is not satisfied/violated by prose. Test passes.\", \"files_changed\": [\"crates/legion-desktop/tests/save_all_conflict.rs\", \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/common/mod.rs\"], \"notes\": \"Improves the structural source check but does not add the fuller spy/mock app-authority behavior test the recipe also suggested (that needs an openable runtime / injectable authority; runtime open is blocked by the temp-path policy here).\", \"package\": \"legion-desktop\"}]}\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-implementation-plan-v0.1.md:190:1. After ADR-0011 acceptance, create [`crates/legion-lsp/Cargo.toml`](../crates/legion-lsp/Cargo.toml) and [`crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs`](../crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs) with dependencies only on protocol, platform, security, observability, and allowed runtime/serialization crates.\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-implementation-plan-v0.1.md:232:1. After ADR-0012 acceptance, create [`crates/legion-plugin/Cargo.toml`](../crates/legion-plugin/Cargo.toml) and [`crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs`](../crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs) for first-party/trusted plugins only.\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-implementation-plan-v0.1.md:316:- [`plans/adrs/ADR-0011-lsp-architecture.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0011-lsp-architecture.md)\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-implementation-plan-v0.1.md:317:- [`plans/adrs/ADR-0012-plugin-runtime.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0012-plugin-runtime.md)\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-implementation-plan-v0.1.md:318:- [`plans/adrs/ADR-0013-filesystem-vfs-policy.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0013-filesystem-vfs-policy.md)\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-implementation-plan-v0.1.md:319:- [`plans/adrs/ADR-0014-workspace-state-watcher-policy.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0014-workspace-state-watcher-policy.md)\r\n.\\.planning\\phases\\07-fully-functional-local-ide-beta\\07-CONTEXT.md:61:- `devil-desktop` may own renderer resources, adapter-local presentation state, smoke harnesses, metadata-only diagnostics, and native platform observations. It must not own app/editor/workspace/proposal/security/storage/runtime authority.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-headless-input-evidence.md:80:1. Open a workspace file through the real egui context.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-headless-input-evidence.md:82:3. Save the dirty file through the real egui context with Cmd+S.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-headless-input-evidence.md:83:4. Run search through the real egui context with Cmd+F.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-headless-input-evidence.md:84:5. Switch product mode through the real egui context with Cmd+Alt+M.\r\n.\\.legion-review\\_validated.json:1:{\"total_validated\": 274, \"files_processed\": 20, \"by_verdict\": {\"CONFIRMED\": 190, \"FALSE_POSITIVE\": 34, \"ALREADY_FIXED\": 11, \"UNCERTAIN\": 39}, \"by_severity\": {\"low\": 54, \"high\": 76, \"medium\": 138, \"critical\": 6}, \"confirmed_by_effort\": {\"S\": 83, \"M\": 99, \"L\": 8}, \"findings\": [{\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs:237\", \"evidence\": \"In DelegatedTaskSandboxOrchestrator::initialize the worktree path is passed as `self.sandbox_path.to_str().unwrap()` inside the `git worktree add` args; a non-UTF-8 PathBuf panics the process.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the `.args([... self.sandbox_path.to_str().unwrap(), \\\"HEAD\\\"])` call with `Command::new(\\\"git\\\").arg(\\\"worktree\\\").arg(\\\"add\\\").arg(&self.sandbox_path).arg(\\\"HEAD\\\")` so the OsStr path is passed directly, or convert via `to_str().ok_or_else(|| io::Error::new(InvalidInput, ...))?`.\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs:247-251\", \"evidence\": \"There is no copy-based fallback: when `git worktree add` fails the fallback arm simply calls `std::fs::create_dir_all(&self.sandbox_path)` creating an empty dir. `git log -S \\\"fs::copy\\\"` shows fs::copy has never existed in this file, so the described symlink-following copy walk does not apply.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs:314-361 (validate_containment) and 413-433 (generate_proposal)\", \"evidence\": \"validate_containment normalizes ParentDir components only for its internal starts_with check and returns `Result<(), AgentError>` (no path); generate_proposal then derives the proposal path from the raw original via `input.target_path.strip_prefix(&self.sandbox_base).unwrap_or(input.target_path)` and wraps it in `CanonicalPath(...)`, so `..` segments persist in the emitted payload.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change validate_containment to return the normalized contained PathBuf (the `clean_path`), and in generate_proposal use that normalized path for strip_prefix and the CanonicalPath payload. Reject any resulting relative path whose components include ParentDir/RootDir/Prefix before constructing CreateFileProposal.\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs:406-458\", \"evidence\": \"generate_proposal's doc says 'Compares sandbox directory state with HEAD checkout' but the body never reads HEAD/diffs; it unconditionally returns `ProposalPayload::CreateFile` and sets every field of ProposalVersionPreconditions to None (file_version, expected_fingerprint, etc.).\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In generate_proposal, stat/read the base (HEAD or sandbox-base) target: if it exists emit an edit/patch payload, else CreateFile. Populate ProposalVersionPreconditions (expected_fingerprint, expected_file_length, expected_modified_at, file_content_version) from the base/sandbox file metadata to provide a concurrency guard.\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs:854-919\", \"evidence\": \"record_proposal_output builds evidence_id `format!(\\\"legion-evidence:{}\\\", worker_id.0)` and result_id `format!(\\\"legion-result:{}\\\", worker_id.0)` and unconditionally pushes to proposal_outputs/evidence_records/worker_results with no duplicate check, so repeated calls per worker create colliding ids and duplicate results.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Before pushing, check whether an evidence/result with that id (or the worker_id/proposal_id pair) already exists and return a structured AgentError on duplicate, or make ids unique by including output.proposal_id/output_id in the format string and dedupe proposal_outputs by proposal id.\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/lib.rs:1137 and 1144\", \"evidence\": \"provider_route_request_from_worker hardcodes `cancellation_token: CancellationTokenId(uuid::Uuid::from_u128(13))` and `event_sequence: EventSequence(13)` for every worker, so all provider routes share the same cancellation/audit identity.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Derive cancellation_token and event_sequence from per-worker/session data (e.g. hash worker_id/correlation_id into the Uuid, and use a monotonically increasing session-supplied sequence) rather than the constant 13, or require these as parameters from the caller/worker metadata.\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/dag.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-agent/src/dag.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"The legion-agent crate contains only src/lib.rs; dag.rs and the function `workflow_dag_from_approved_plan` exist nowhere in the workspace. `git log -S workflow_dag_from_approved_plan` shows the name appears only in the review doc commit 87c9789, never in source.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/evidence.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-agent/src/evidence.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"No evidence.rs file and no `external_log_evidence_record`/`record_external_log_evidence` functions exist in the workspace; git pickaxe shows these identifiers only in review doc commit 87c9789, never in any .rs source.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/external.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-agent/src/external.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"No external.rs file and no `validate_workspace_edit_conversion` function exist anywhere; git pickaxe shows the name only in review doc commit 87c9789. The described code was never part of the codebase.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/external.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-agent/src/external.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"Same nonexistent external.rs / validate_workspace_edit_conversion as Finding 9; the `let _ = principal` validation logic described is not present anywhere in the workspace source.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/plan.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-agent/src/plan.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"No plan.rs file and no `task_entries` function exist in the workspace; git pickaxe shows `task_entries` only in review doc commit 87c9789, never in source code.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/src/scope.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-agent/src/scope.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"No scope.rs file and no `target_is_within_scope`/`forbids_path` functions exist in the workspace; git pickaxe shows both names only in review doc commit 87c9789, never in source. (Note: real path-containment logic does exist as validate_containment in lib.rs, but it is unrelated to the cited scope.rs functions.)\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"agent-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/lib.rs:607-633 (ProviderRouter::route_completion)\", \"evidence\": \"After `let completion = provider.complete(...)?;` the success response sets `provider_id: request.provider_id.clone()` and `model_label: request.model_label.clone()` (lines 624-625) with no comparison against `completion.provider`/`completion.model`, which exist on ChatCompletionResponse (lib.rs:104-106).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In route_completion, after obtaining `completion`, add `if completion.provider != request.provider_id || completion.model != request.model_label { return Ok(self.refused_response(&request, \\\"provider.identity_mismatch\\\", \\\"provider returned a different provider/model than requested\\\")); }` (or return a ProviderError). Optionally also record the actual provider/model from `completion` in the response instead of echoing the request.\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/lib.rs:684-693 (allowed_route_decision) and call site 623/632\", \"evidence\": \"`allowed_route_decision()` hard-codes `schema_version: 1` (line 691) while the enclosing route response sets `schema_version: request.schema_version` (line 632); the nested AssistedAiRouteDecision can therefore be stale.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change signature to `fn allowed_route_decision(schema_version: u16) -> AssistedAiRouteDecision` and use that parameter for the nested `schema_version`; at the call site (line 623) pass `request.schema_version`.\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/lib.rs:404-459; crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs:10774,11613\", \"evidence\": \"deterministic_inline_prediction validates request metadata first (lib.rs:404) and validate_inline_prediction_request_metadata rejects `max_prediction_bytes == 0` (protocol:10774); the built result is then validated (lib.rs:457) and validate_inline_prediction_ghost_text rejects empty text (protocol:11613), so an Available result with empty ghost text can never be returned (the function returns Err instead).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/redaction.rs\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/redaction.rs:17-58\", \"evidence\": \"redaction_patterns now use regexes matching the entire secret (e.g. `authorization:\\\\s*bearer\\\\s+\\\\S+`, `(?:openai_api_key|...|api_key)\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\S+`, `(?:sk-|...)\\\\S+`) and replace_all collapses marker+value; tests assert the full value (`sk-test-mock-value`, `mock-bearer-value`) is gone (lines 99-102).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/redaction.rs\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/redaction.rs:20-29\", \"evidence\": \"Every redaction regex spec is prefixed with the case-insensitive flag `(?i)` (lines 22,24,26,28), so mixed/upper/lowercase markers are all replaced rather than merely flagged.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/streaming.rs\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/streaming.rs:42-58\", \"evidence\": \"flush_code no longer guards on empty code_lines; it always pushes a `MarkdownStreamSegment::CodeBlock` preserving language and complete flag (lines 52-56), with a comment documenting empty blocks are intentionally preserved, and dedicated tests cover empty complete and incomplete fences (lines 117-148).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai/src/telemetry.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (crates/legion-ai/src/telemetry.rs does not exist)\", \"evidence\": \"The cited file crates/legion-ai/src/telemetry.rs does not exist and has no git history; legion-ai contains only lib.rs, redaction.rs, streaming.rs and no telemetry code (grep for `telemetry` in lib.rs returns nothing). The described Option<HostedTelemetrySpoolRecord> helper collapsing validation/consent into None could not be located in current code.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Locate the actual telemetry helper (possibly relocated to legion-telemetry/legion-observability) before acting; if it exists, return Result<Option<...>, _> so validation/construction errors are distinguishable from consent-policy None.\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs:303, 1102, 1139, 2059\", \"evidence\": \"All four blocking transports call `reqwest::blocking::Client::new().post(...)` with no `.timeout()`/`.connect_timeout()` (ReqwestProviderHttpTransport:303, Anthropic post_json:1102, post_text:1139, StreamableHttpMcpTransport:2059), so a hung endpoint blocks the calling thread indefinitely.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Construct a shared `reqwest::blocking::Client` via `Client::builder().connect_timeout(Duration::from_secs(...)).timeout(Duration::from_secs(...)).build()` (stored once per transport or in a OnceLock) and reuse it at all four sites; map elapsed timeouts to ProviderError::RequestFailed/McpClientError::Transport; add a test with a delayed/injected transport.\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs:845-855 (OpenAiCompatibleProvider::complete)\", \"evidence\": \"The chat/completions payload serializes `\\\"max_tokens\\\": request.max_tokens` and `\\\"temperature\\\": request.temperature` directly inside `json!` (lines 853-854), so when the options are None they are sent as JSON null rather than omitted.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Build the payload as a mutable `json!({...})` without max_tokens/temperature, then `if let Some(v) = request.max_tokens { payload[\\\"max_tokens\\\"] = json!(v); }` and likewise for temperature, mirroring the incremental pattern already used in OpenAiResponsesProvider::request_payload (lines 571-576).\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs:1109-1111, 1146-1148 (Anthropic transport); from_env 1179-1186; bearer_token 1220-1230\", \"evidence\": \"Both Anthropic transport methods send the credential via `request.bearer_auth(token)` (lines 1110, 1147), and from_env collapses ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN into a single `api_key` field (1179-1186); API keys are therefore sent as a bearer header instead of the required `x-api-key`.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Track credential kind (ApiKey vs AuthToken) when reading env in from_env, plumb it through with_transport/AnthropicMessagesClient, and in post_json/post_text set `request.header(\\\"x-api-key\\\", key)` for API keys and `request.bearer_auth(token)` only for auth tokens; add tests asserting the header chosen per credential type.\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs:569 (OpenAiResponsesProvider::request_payload), metadata_flag 527-536\", \"evidence\": \"`\\\"store\\\": Self::metadata_flag(&request.metadata, \\\"openai.responses.store\\\", true)` defaults the Responses-API `store` flag to true (line 569; metadata_flag returns the default when the key is absent), opting into provider-side response storage unless callers override it.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change the default argument at line 569 from `true` to `false` so provider-side storage requires an explicit `openai.responses.store=true` metadata opt-in; update/add a test asserting `store` defaults to false and document retention behavior.\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/src/lib.rs:1977-1998 (StdioMcpTransport::send_on_session), lock held at 2006-2019\", \"evidence\": \"send_on_session loops on `read_line` until `response.get(\\\"id\\\") == expected_id` with no timeout, deadline, or max-iteration bound (lines 1977-1998); the session mutex is locked in `send` (line 2008) and held across this unbounded blocking read, so a wedged or notification-only server hangs the caller forever.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a per-request deadline (e.g. Instant::now()+timeout) to the loop and return McpClientError::Transport on expiry; set a read timeout on the underlying stdout/child pipe or bound the number of unrelated messages; handle JSON-RPC error responses/notifications explicitly; consider not holding the session mutex across the blocking read.\", \"review_file\": \"ai-stack.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/main.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/src/main.rs:11-22 (open_file -> lib.rs:13205-13207)\", \"evidence\": \"main() defaults `path` to \\\"scratch.txt\\\" then calls `app.open_file(path)?`; `open_file` forwards `OpenFileIntent::Existing` (lib.rs:13206), and the Existing arm calls `open_existing_file_text_with_causality` (lib.rs:8183) which reads metadata, so a missing scratch.txt aborts startup with `?`.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In main(), when the path argument is absent (the scratch.txt default) and the file does not exist, call `app.open_new_file(path)` (CreateNew intent) instead of `open_file`; or detect NotFound from open_file and retry via open_new_file, or require the user to pass an existing path.\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"error\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/offline_ai.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/src/offline_ai.rs:1283-1320\", \"evidence\": \"The `#[cfg(test)]` helper `route_request()` builds `AssistedAiProviderRouteRequest { route_id: ..., ... schema_version: 1 }` with no `prompt_prefix`, while the field is required (legion-protocol/src/lib.rs:6657 `pub prompt_prefix: String`) and the non-test builder sets it (offline_ai.rs:1105). offline_ai is `#[cfg(not(feature=\\\"ai\\\"))]` (lib.rs:26) and default=[\\\"ai\\\"], so `--no-default-features --all-targets` compiles this test and fails with E0063.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add `prompt_prefix: String::new(),` (or a deterministic prefix) to the struct literal in `route_request()` at offline_ai.rs:1283, and keep `--no-default-features --all-targets` in CI.\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/offline_ai.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/src/offline_ai.rs:410-441 (validate_containment)\", \"evidence\": \"validate_containment canonicalizes base via `std::fs::canonicalize(base)` but only lexically normalizes the candidate (the `clean_components` loop strips ParentDir/CurDir without resolving symlinks) before `clean_stripped.starts_with(&base_stripped)`; it also calls `std::env::current_dir().unwrap()` at lines 412 and 417, panicking when the cwd is unavailable instead of returning OfflineAiError.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace both `std::env::current_dir().unwrap()` calls with `std::env::current_dir().map_err(|e| OfflineAiError::InvalidMetadata(...))?` (change the fn to propagate). Resolve the candidate's existing parent directory with `canonicalize` and join the final component, or reject any symlink components, so a symlink inside the sandbox cannot escape; then compare canonical paths.\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/proposal.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file and function absent)\", \"evidence\": \"`crates/legion-app/src/proposal.rs` does not exist (src/ contains only lib.rs, main.rs, offline_ai.rs) and has no git history; `filtered_batch_proposal_for_accepted_targets` / `filtered_batch` / `for_accepted` match nowhere in crates/. The current batch code (apply_batch_proposal, preflight at lib.rs:22921-22939, batch_has_dependency_cycle at 23341) validates dependency edges but contains no accepted-target filtering that drops edges, so the described defect cannot be located in the current tree.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs:10270-10300 (SaveWorkflowService::save_active_buffer) and 17663-17693 (AppComposition::save_buffer)\", \"evidence\": \"After `workspace.save_file_with_proposal` returns Ok(applied) (lib.rs:10270), an `observe_proposal_response` audit failure returns `SaveWorkflowFailure` (lib.rs:10279-10282) with no rollback of the on-disk write; save_buffer's Err arm reports `AppSaveOutcome::Rejected` and never calls `bind_saved_buffer` (only the Ok arm does, line 17678), so disk is mutated while the buffer stays dirty. The generic apply path instead calls `rollback_audit_failed_mutation` on audit failure (lib.rs:21275).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In SaveWorkflowService::save_active_buffer Ok-branch, when observe_proposal_response returns Err, roll back the just-written file using a pre-save checkpoint (mirror `rollback_audit_failed_mutation`/`rollback_snapshot_for_proposal`) before returning the failure; alternatively persist the audit before committing the workspace save, or commit saved metadata while surfacing the audit failure separately so disk and editor state stay consistent.\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs:15280-15368 (execute_delegated_task ACP block)\", \"evidence\": \"After `orchestrator.initialize(&permission)?` (lib.rs:15280) allocates the sandbox, the ACP path's `acp_host_command.run(...).map_err(...)?` (15325-15329) and `std::fs::read_to_string(&target_file_absolute)?` (15365-15367) return early without `orchestrator.cleanup`, whereas the unsuccessful-exit branch (15356) and the post-generation path (15391) do clean up, confirming the inconsistency.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Wrap the post-initialize ACP block so every early return runs `orchestrator.cleanup(&permission)` (a scope-guard/RAII drop wrapper around the orchestrator, or explicit cleanup before the `run(...)?` and `read_to_string(...)?` error returns), and surface cleanup errors alongside the original error.\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (partial-apply/filtered-batch path absent)\", \"evidence\": \"No filtered/partial delegated-apply code exists: `filtered_batch`/`build_filtered`/`filter_proposal` match nowhere in crates/, and `filtered_apply_required` appears only as a projection flag computed by `from_hunks` (lib.rs:828). `review_delegate_proposal_hunk` (lib.rs:18759-18794) merely records dispositions into `hunk_decisions` and returns a projection; lib.rs:21700-21763 is workspace-reopen/save-commit code, not a filtered apply. proposal_ledger_projection does render from `self.proposals` (lib.rs:2163), but with no subset-apply path the described divergence cannot be located.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"app-entry-&-proposals.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Cargo.toml Finding 1\", \"title\": \"No workspace rust-version (MSRV) declared for edition 2024\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"Cargo.toml\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"Cargo.toml:34-38\", \"evidence\": \"[workspace.package] declares version, edition=\\\"2024\\\", license, publish=false but no rust-version; grep for 'rust-version' across Cargo.toml returns no matches.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add `rust-version = \\\"1.85\\\"` (or the chosen MSRV that supports edition 2024 and current deps) to [workspace.package] in Cargo.toml, have member crates inherit via `rust-version.workspace = true`, and add a CI lane pinning that toolchain to enforce the floor.\", \"review_file\": \"build-&-config.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Cargo.lock Finding 1\", \"title\": \"Lockfile contains many duplicate crate versions\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"Cargo.lock\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"Cargo.lock (whole file)\", \"evidence\": \"`grep '^name = ' Cargo.lock | sort | uniq -d | wc -l` reports 44 duplicated crate names; windows-sys resolves to 0.45.0/0.52.0/0.59.0/0.60.2/0.61.2 and bitflags/thiserror each appear twice (some specifics like toml now resolve to a single 0.8.23, so the review's exact list has drifted).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Run `cargo tree -d` to enumerate duplicates, align direct dependency versions in [workspace.dependencies] where possible, document unavoidable transitive duplicates with `[bans] skip`/`skip-tree` entries in deny.toml, then promote multiple-versions to deny once the baseline is minimized.\", \"review_file\": \"build-&-config.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"deny.toml Finding 1\", \"title\": \"Yanked/unknown-registry/unknown-git set to warn instead of deny\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"deny.toml\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"deny.toml:10,52-53\", \"evidence\": \"deny.toml has `yanked = \\\"warn\\\"` (line 10), `unknown-registry = \\\"warn\\\"` (line 52), and `unknown-git = \\\"warn\\\"` (line 53), so the cargo-deny gate passes even with yanked or off-policy sources.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change `yanked`, `unknown-registry`, and `unknown-git` to \\\"deny\\\" in deny.toml; add `allow-registry`/`allow-git` allowlists for the known-good sources, and use narrow documented ignore entries (with owner/removal note) for any temporary exceptions. Note: CI workflow currently does not run cargo-deny since the workflow was removed (see CI findings), so enforcement also depends on restoring a gate.\", \"review_file\": \"build-&-config.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"deny.toml Finding 2\", \"title\": \"multiple-versions = warn with no skip/exception list\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"deny.toml\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"deny.toml:14-16\", \"evidence\": \"[bans] block has `multiple-versions = \\\"warn\\\"` and `wildcards = \\\"allow\\\"` with no `skip`/`skip-tree` entries, while the lockfile holds ~44 duplicate crate names.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add `[[bans.skip]]`/`[[bans.skip-tree]]` entries with rationale comments for each unavoidable duplicate in deny.toml, resolve avoidable duplicates by aligning versions, then set `multiple-versions = \\\"deny\\\"` once the baseline is clean.\", \"review_file\": \"build-&-config.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml Finding 1\", \"title\": \"CI workflow missing least-privilege permissions block\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file deleted)\", \"evidence\": \"`.github/workflows/ci.yml` no longer exists; git history shows commit d397f5e \\\"chore: remove hosted CI workflow\\\" deleted the workflow, so the missing-permissions defect no longer applies to any current file.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"build-&-config.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml Finding 2\", \"title\": \"Third-party actions pinned to mutable tags\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file deleted)\", \"evidence\": \"The reviewed workflow was removed (commit d397f5e \\\"chore: remove hosted CI workflow\\\"); no .github/workflows/*.yml exist in the repo, so there are no action references to pin.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"build-&-config.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml Finding 3\", \"title\": \"Floating stable toolchain not pinned to rust-toolchain.toml/MSRV\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file deleted)\", \"evidence\": \"The workflow installing the floating toolchain was deleted (commit d397f5e), and no rust-toolchain.toml exists; the time-dependent CI behavior described no longer applies to any present file. (Related MSRV gap is captured separately under Cargo.toml Finding 1.)\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"build-&-config.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs:194-200\", \"evidence\": \"`TimestampMillis::now()` does `SystemTime::now().duration_since(UNIX_EPOCH).map_or(0, |d| d.as_millis() as u64)` \\u2014 pre-epoch clocks collapse to 0 and the u128->u64 cast can wrap silently.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In TimestampMillis::now(), replace `d.as_millis() as u64` with `u64::try_from(d.as_millis()).unwrap_or(u64::MAX)`; optionally add a fallible `try_now() -> Result<Self,_>` that surfaces the `duration_since` error instead of `map_or(0, ...)`.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs:9515-9522 (evaluate_delegated_task_runtime_readiness)\", \"evidence\": \"Protected-path gate uses substring match: `.any(|protected| !protected.is_empty() && target.contains(protected))` over `protected_path_patterns`, which is not path-aware (separators/case/canonicalization/globs ignored).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In evaluate_delegated_task_runtime_readiness, normalize each target label to a canonical Path and compare protected patterns with component/boundary-aware matching (or compiled globs), e.g. `Path::starts_with` on canonicalized components, keeping a conservative fallback for non-path labels rather than raw `contains`.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/capability.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A \\u2014 crates/legion-protocol/src/capability.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"lib.rs:18 declares `pub mod capability;` and lib.rs:27 re-exports `AssistedAiCapabilityMatrix`, but no capability.rs/capability/mod.rs exists in the repo or git history; `cargo check -p legion-protocol` fails with E0583 'file not found for module `capability`', and `has_explicit_declaration` is not defined anywhere in lib.rs.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: locate/restore the missing capability module, then in `has_explicit_declaration` use `field.trim().is_empty()` for provider/display identifier fields.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/manifest.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A \\u2014 crates/legion-protocol/src/manifest.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"lib.rs:14 declares `pub mod manifest;` and lib.rs:15 re-exports `ContextManifestAssembly`, but no manifest.rs exists (not tracked in git, absent from working tree); `cargo check` fails E0583 for `manifest`, and `ContextManifestAssembly`/`into_record` have no definition in lib.rs.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: locate/restore the manifest module, then change `into_record()` to return `Result<ContextManifestRecord, AssistedAiContractError>` validating manifest_id, schema_version, identifiers, and recomputing omitted/freshness counts.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/plan.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A \\u2014 crates/legion-protocol/src/plan.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"lib.rs:20 declares `pub mod plan;` and lib.rs:28-32 re-exports `EditablePlanArtifact`, but no plan.rs exists in repo or git history; `cargo check` fails E0583 for `plan`, and `EditablePlanArtifact::validate` is not defined in lib.rs.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: locate/restore the plan module, then in `validate()` assert each section's index equals `section.kind.order()` (canonical requirements->design->tasks) and reject out-of-order deserialized artifacts.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/risk.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A \\u2014 crates/legion-protocol/src/risk.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"lib.rs:22 declares `pub mod risk;` but no risk.rs exists (untracked, absent from working tree); `cargo check` fails E0583 for `risk`, and `is_allow`/`RiskAssessment` are not defined in lib.rs, so the vacuous-truth claim cannot be evaluated against current code.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: locate/restore the risk module, then make `is_allow()` fail closed by returning false when `findings` is empty or when any id in `RiskRuleId::all()` is missing, before the `Iterator::all()` check.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/scope.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A \\u2014 crates/legion-protocol/src/scope.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"lib.rs:24 declares `pub mod scope;` and lib.rs:33 re-exports `DelegatedTaskScope`, but no scope.rs exists in repo or git history; `cargo check` fails E0583 for `scope`, and `target_is_within_scope`/`forbidden_paths` are not defined in lib.rs.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: locate/restore the scope module, then add an `allows_target_path()` predicate combining workspace boundary, target kind, and `forbidden_paths`, or have `target_is_within_scope()` call `forbids_path()` and return false on a forbidden match.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/tools.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A \\u2014 crates/legion-protocol/src/tools.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"lib.rs:26 declares `pub mod tools;` and lib.rs:34-38 re-exports `LegionToolCallFeedback`/`LegionToolKind`, but no tools.rs exists (untracked, absent); `cargo check` fails E0583 for `tools`, and these types have no definition in lib.rs.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: locate/restore the tools module, then add `attempted_tool_name: Option<String>` to `LegionToolCallFeedback` (or make its tool field an enum `Known(LegionToolKind)|Unknown(String)`) to represent unknown tool names.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/tools.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A \\u2014 crates/legion-protocol/src/tools.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"lib.rs:34-38 re-exports `validate_tool_schema_definition`, but no tools.rs exists in repo or git history and `cargo check` fails E0583 for `tools`; the function body cannot be inspected to confirm it omits tool_name/label consistency checks.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: locate/restore the tools module, then in `validate_tool_schema_definition()` assert `tool.tool_name == tool.kind.tool_name()` and `description_label == tool.kind` canonical label, rejecting mismatches.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-protocol/src/tools.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A \\u2014 crates/legion-protocol/src/tools.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"The read/edit-as-proposal JSON schemas live in the missing tools.rs (lib.rs:26 `pub mod tools;` references a nonexistent file; `cargo check` fails E0583); the schema text constraining start_line/end_line cannot be located in current source.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: locate/restore the tools module, then add post-schema runtime validation rejecting `start_line > end_line` and returning structured `InvalidArguments` feedback for inverted ranges.\", \"review_file\": \"core-protocol.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/platform.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/platform.rs:194-198\", \"evidence\": \"high_dpi_status matches `Some(scale) if scale > 1.0 => format!(\\\"os-observed scale {scale:.3}\\\")` and falls through `Some(_) | None => NOT_OBSERVED`, so an observed scale of exactly 1.0 is reported as 'not observed'.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In high_dpi_status, split the match: `Some(scale) if scale.is_finite() && scale > 0.0 => format!(\\\"os-observed scale {scale:.3}\\\")` for any positive finite scale (including 1.0), and reserve NOT_OBSERVED for `None` and non-finite/<=0 values.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/session.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/session.rs:177-184 (temporary_session_path) and 126-127 (save_crash_safe)\", \"evidence\": \"temporary_session_path builds `.{file_name}.{process::id()}.{suffix}` using only the PID, and save_crash_safe does `let _ = fs::remove_file(&temp_path)` before writing, so two concurrent saves of the same path in one process collide and can delete each other's temp.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a per-save uniqueness component to temporary_session_path: append an atomic counter (static AtomicU64::fetch_add) and/or a random nonce in addition to process::id(), or switch to a tempfile crate NamedTempFile in the destination dir. Remove the blind remove_file or scope it to the unique nonce only.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/session.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/session.rs:106-113 (reject_raw_source_markers), markers at 12-15\", \"evidence\": \"reject_raw_source_markers does `json.contains(**marker)` over the whole serialized document for markers like `source_body`/`small_buffer_preview`, so any metadata field, path, or label containing those substrings fails the save/load.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Deserialize to the record and inspect only the known raw-payload-carrying fields (e.g. preview/body fields) rather than substring-scanning the entire JSON, or use a dedicated schema-level redaction marker that cannot collide with user content.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/bridge.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/bridge.rs:1215-1220 (OpenGitPullRequestUrl handler)\", \"evidence\": \"`let base_branch = snapshot.git_projection.remote_default_branch.as_deref().unwrap_or(branch_label);` falls back to the current branch when the default branch is missing, producing a branch...branch self-compare URL.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the unwrap_or(branch_label) fallback: if remote_default_branch is None/empty, return a typed error (e.g. add DesktopBridgeError::MissingRemoteDefaultBranch) instead of defaulting to the current branch; only use a configured validated fallback when the projection explicitly provides one.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs:931-945 (OpenWorkspace request handler)\", \"evidence\": \"On Ok the handler only calls `self.set_status(...Opened...)` and returns WorkspaceOpened; it never assigns `self.workspace_root = root`, so diagnostics/health/session paths keep the original root (field defined at line 530/605).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In the OpenWorkspace Ok branch, set `self.workspace_root = root.clone();` and reset workspace-scoped adapter-local explorer/expansion state; ensure session_state/diagnostics paths derived from workspace_root are rebased or explicitly retained per launch policy.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs:2201, 2259-2261, 2323-2325, 2327-2329, 2348\", \"evidence\": \"Multiple UI paths discard the Result: `let _ = self.runtime.handle_action(action)` (2201, 2348), `let _ = self.runtime.handle_action(DesktopAction::UpdatePaletteQuery...)` (2259-2261), and palette selection actions (2323-2329).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Capture each handle_action Result; on Err set an error status (self.set_status(StatusSeverity::Error, ...)) and request a projection refresh/repaint. For headless/test harness paths, store or propagate the error so failures are assertable.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs:2527 (`let at = projected_cursor(snapshot)`) used inside loop 2535-2578\", \"evidence\": \"editor_text_input_actions computes `at` once before iterating events, and every Text/Paste/ImeCommit action pushed in the loop reuses the same stale `at`, so multiple text events in one frame all target the original cursor offset.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Either concatenate consecutive Text/Paste payloads into one InsertText at `at` preserving order, or track a running insertion offset locally (advance `at` by the inserted length after each generated action) so batched actions target sequential positions; ideally refresh the projection cursor between dispatches.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/workflow.rs:2771-2779 (open_url_in_system_browser, Windows branch)\", \"evidence\": \"On Windows it builds `cmd /C start \\\"\\\"` then `command.arg(url)`, passing the URL as a raw cmd argument; `&` and other metacharacters in forge/GitLab MR URLs are reinterpreted by cmd.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Avoid cmd /C start for URLs: use the `open` crate (open::that) or call ShellExecuteW directly via windows-sys, or at minimum escape cmd metacharacters (^& etc.) in the URL before passing to cmd. Prefer a ShellExecute-based opener that does not go through the cmd parser.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/health.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/health.rs:173 and 226-232 (rows), 240 and 304-310 (to_markdown)\", \"evidence\": \"`format!(\\\"workspace: {}\\\", self.workspace_label)` and `format!(\\\"unsupported: {surface}\\\")` (and markdown equivalents `workspace_label:`/`- {surface}`) interpolate labels with no newline/control-char normalization or markdown escaping.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a normalization helper that replaces \\\\r\\\\n\\\\t and other control chars (and escapes markdown-sensitive chars for to_markdown) and apply it to workspace_label and each unsupported surface before formatting rows/markdown.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/diagnostics.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/diagnostics.rs:49-98 (to_markdown)\", \"evidence\": \"to_markdown emits only metadata/count fields and ends with a Privacy section stating diagnostics exclude raw bodies; there is no triple-backtick fence or opt-in raw snapshot appendix anywhere in the file (grep for ``` and {:#?}/raw appendix found none). The cited lines 109-118 are now inside write_to_path (create_dir_all).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/metrics.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/metrics.rs:88-92 (record_paint push) and 102 (record_frame_duration push); fields 51-52\", \"evidence\": \"FrameTimingRecorder stores input_paint_samples and frame_durations_ms as plain Vecs with unconditional `.push(...)` and no eviction, so a long-running session grows them unbounded and summary() sorts/iterates ever-larger vectors.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Bound retention: use a fixed-capacity ring buffer (e.g. VecDeque with pop_front when len exceeds a cap) for both vectors, or maintain windowed running aggregates for summary(); expose the cap/retention policy in the recorder API.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/search.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/search.rs:61-68 (result_rows mapping)\", \"evidence\": \"The result row `format!(\\\"{}:{}:{}{} {}\\\", path, line, char, truncated, row.snippet)` interpolates row.snippet directly, so newlines/tabs/control chars in the snippet break the one-line row format.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Normalize row.snippet before interpolation (replace \\\\r\\\\n\\\\t and other control chars with spaces/escapes) via a small helper; keep raw snippet in a structured field if needed elsewhere.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/package.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/package.rs:35-41 (cargo_args) and 116-120 (executable_source)\", \"evidence\": \"cargo_args returns `[\\\"build\\\",\\\"-p\\\",\\\"legion-desktop\\\"]` with no --target triple, and executable_source = workspace_root/target/<profile>/WINDOWS_EXECUTABLE_NAME; on a non-Windows host this builds the host binary and points at a path that has no .exe.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add an optional target triple to WindowsPackageConfig; when set, append `--target <triple>` to cargo_args and build executable_source as target/<triple>/<profile>/legion-desktop.exe. Default to requiring the windows triple when host OS is not windows.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/beta.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/beta.rs:345-360 (prepare_beta_workspace)\", \"evidence\": \"prepare_beta_workspace resolves workspace_root from `std::env::current_dir()` (346-349) and joins relative beta paths against it (`workspace_root.join(path)` 359), ignoring BetaWorkflowConfig.real_workspace_root.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Pass the configured real_workspace_root into prepare_beta_workspace and resolve relative beta workspace paths against it instead of current_dir(); or assert/enforce that current_dir equals the configured root before proceeding.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/beta.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/beta.rs:647-660 (beta_smoke_command)\", \"evidence\": \"beta_smoke_command builds `format!(\\\"--workspace {}\\\", config.real_workspace_root.display())` etc. and `.join(\\\" \\\")` with no quoting, so paths with spaces/metacharacters produce a non-rerunnable command.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Shell-quote each path argument (or render the command as a structured argv Vec<String>) using a quoting helper for the documented shell before joining.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs:315-323\", \"evidence\": \"Only `if observations.frame_count == 0 { errors.push(...) }` gates status; adapter checks, focus/high-DPI, accessibility projection, and guardrail statuses can be 'not observed'/failed while status stays RendererSmokeStatus::Passed.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Before selecting status, add explicit gate checks: push errors when required adapter checks (clipboard/ime/file_dialog) are Some(false)/None, when high_dpi/focus are unobserved-but-required, and when guardrail statuses fail; only set Passed when all required signals pass.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs:437-442 (SmokeObservations::high_dpi_status)\", \"evidence\": \"`match self.pixels_per_point { Some(scale) if scale > 1.0 => ..., Some(_) | None => NOT_OBSERVED }` reports an observed scale of exactly 1.0 as 'not observed', same false-negative as platform.rs.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change the guard to accept any positive finite scale (`Some(scale) if scale.is_finite() && scale > 0.0`) for the os-observed branch and reserve NOT_OBSERVED for None/invalid; keep consistent with the platform.rs fix.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/smoke.rs:351-368 (smoke_command)\", \"evidence\": \"smoke_command pushes `format!(\\\"--workspace {}\\\", config.workspace_root.display())`, `--file {file}`, `--evidence {}` etc. and `parts.join(\\\" \\\")` without quoting, so paths with spaces/metacharacters don't round-trip.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Shell-quote each path/file argument or return a structured argv list; reuse the same quoting helper recommended for beta_smoke_command (Finding 15).\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-core.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:4242-4251 (drag_selection_range), emitted at 1930-1933\", \"evidence\": \"drag_selection_range builds `ProtocolTextRange { start: drag_anchor.unwrap_or(current_cursor), end: coordinate }` with no ordering normalization; the emitted range flows through set_buffer_selection -> editor_range -> set_selections (legion-editor lib.rs:1880-1891) which stores `state.selections = selections` verbatim, so a backwards drag yields an inverted range. (The review's named paint fn `selection_span_for_line` does not exist, but the inverted-range defect is real.)\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In drag_selection_range, after picking start=anchor/cursor and end=coordinate, compare the two TextCoordinates (by line then character) and swap so start<=end before constructing ProtocolTextRange; alternatively add a `normalized()` helper on ProtocolTextRange and call it at all SetSelection emit sites (1909-1918, 1930-1933) and in set_buffer_selection.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:2641-2642 (buttons) and 2656-2659 (confidence) in render_fleet_canvas\", \"evidence\": \"`let _ = soft_button(ui, \\\"Pause Workflow\\\");` and `let _ = soft_button(ui, \\\"Add Constraint\\\");` discard the responses (no DesktopAction pushed), and the strip renders `theme::accent(\\\"confidence 87%\\\", ...)` as a hard-coded literal not derived from any projection field.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Either bind the two buttons' `.clicked()` to real DesktopAction variants (e.g. a workflow pause / add-constraint action) and replace the literal with a value read from legion_workflow_projection (e.g. risk_monitors/confidence field), or render them with a disabled style and an explicit 'unavailable' label and drop the hard-coded percentage until projected confidence exists.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:3159-3188 (render_delegation_console)\", \"evidence\": \"No scope-picker is rendered in the command center; `git grep DesktopScopePickerViewModel` and `ScopePicker` over the whole repo/history return only the review docs, never source. render_delegation_console shows a 'Delegate' button and approval queue, no scope view model, so the described `DesktopScopePickerViewModel::default()` render never existed in legion-desktop.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:3305-3353 (render_delegated_hunk_review_controls), caps at 3315 and 3324\", \"evidence\": \"`for review in reviews.iter().take(4)` and `for hunk in review.hunks.iter().take(6)` silently truncate with no overflow count, navigation, or proposal-level action; hidden reviews/hunks cannot be accepted/rejected/marked pending from this surface. (The 'file groups to 6' detail does not match -- there is no file grouping -- but the silent reviews=4/hunks=6 caps defect holds.)\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In render_delegated_hunk_review_controls add omitted-count labels (reviews.len().saturating_sub(4), review.hunks.len().saturating_sub(6)) and wrap the lists in a ScrollArea or pagination so every review/hunk is reachable; optionally add proposal-level accept/reject-all that deliberately includes hidden hunks with explicit counts.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:5480-5488 (git_relative_path)\", \"evidence\": \"git_relative_path does `file_path.strip_prefix(root)?.trim_start_matches(['/','\\\\\\\\'])` -- a raw string prefix strip with no component boundary check, so root `/repo` and file `/repo2/src/lib.rs` yields `2/src/lib.rs`, mis-associating hunks/blame across roots that share a prefix.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"After strip_prefix, require that the next char is a separator (or the remainder began with one) before accepting; e.g. only proceed if the stripped remainder is empty or starts with '/'/'\\\\\\\\', otherwise return None. Better: build Path::new(file).strip_prefix(Path::new(root)) on normalized paths and convert the relative component to a string.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:6009-6048 (checkpoint_rollback rendering)\", \"evidence\": \"`proposal_evidence_panel` and the cited file view/proposal_review.rs never existed (`git log -S proposal_evidence_panel` over all .rs returns nothing). The current checkpoint surface keys on `rollback.checkpoint.checkpoint_id`, not a `ProposalId(0)` sentinel, and there is no 'checkpoint timeline proposal=' render, so the fake proposal=0 association does not apply to this repo.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (no proposal evidence panel; cf. crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:3259-3303 render_proposal_cards)\", \"evidence\": \"The described evidence panel (proposal rows take(4) + verification rows take(6)) in view/proposal_review.rs never existed in git history. No such combined panel exists; the related verification surface (view.rs:7185-7191) actually does report an `omitted` count, contradicting the finding.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (no plan editor in legion-desktop)\", \"evidence\": \"`render_plan_editor` and view/plan_editor.rs never existed (`git log -S render_plan_editor` over all .rs and `git grep plan_editor` in legion-desktop return nothing). There is no draft-section reconciliation code in legion-desktop, so the stale-body defect does not apply here.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (no scope picker conversion in legion-desktop)\", \"evidence\": \"view/scope_picker.rs and any DesktopScopePickerViewModel->DelegatedTaskScope conversion never existed in legion-desktop (`git grep DelegatedTaskScope`/`target_path`/`ScopePicker` over crates/legion-desktop returns nothing). The placeholder 'file'/'module' summary and target_path:None path do not exist here.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"error\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (no sandbox panel in legion-desktop)\", \"evidence\": \"`host_profile_summary` and view/sandbox_panel.rs never existed (`git log -S host_profile_summary` over all .rs returns nothing; `git grep` for sandbox profile/compile/`/workspace/project` in crates/legion-desktop returns nothing). The hard-coded `/workspace/project` and `expect` panic live only in legion-remote/legion-sandbox, not in the reviewed desktop view.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:5862-5889 (privacy_inspector_projection rendering)\", \"evidence\": \"The header pushes aggregate counts for all records (`privacy.records.len(), denied_record_count, redacted_record_count, external_egress_record_count, high_risk_record_count`) at 5864-5871, then `privacy.records.iter().take(10)` at 5873 renders only the first 10 with no omitted-count and no prioritization, so denied/high-risk/external records beyond index 10 are invisible while the header still counts them. (Defect is real even though it lives in view.rs, not the cited privacy_inspector.rs.)\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Before truncating, sort/partition privacy.records so denied || high_risk || external_egress || redacted records come first, then take(N); and push an explicit omitted row (`records.len().saturating_sub(N)`) like the test-explorer surface already does (view.rs:7187), or add expansion/pagination so every exposure record is inspectable.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-1.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (assistant_rail.rs)\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/assistant_rail.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/assistant_rail.rs:57 and :130-138\", \"evidence\": \"`apply_as_proposal_available: proposal_id.is_some()` (line 57) and render_code_block (lines 130-138) show an 'Apply as proposal' button for every fenced block whenever any proposal_id exists, dispatching `DesktopAction::ApplyProposal { proposal_id }` without verifying the block corresponds to that proposal and without gating on `code_block.complete`; the click guard `code_block.apply_as_proposal_available` is itself just `proposal_id.is_some()`, so it is a no-op guard. Caveat: this module is NOT declared (view.rs only has `mod code_canvas_painter;`), so it is orphaned/uncompiled and `render_streaming_assistant_rows` is never called, making the review's 'current call sites pass first_proposal_id' claim inaccurate.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In assistant_rail.rs change `apply_as_proposal_available` to require `complete` plus a verified per-block proposal binding, and carry the matched ProposalId on each AssistantRailCodeBlockViewModel instead of sharing the snapshot-level proposal_id; in render_code_block only render the button when `code_block.complete && code_block.apply_as_proposal_available` and disable/hide for generic text. Also either wire the module (`pub mod assistant_rail;` + re-export in view.rs, which tests/assistant_rail.rs already imports) or delete the orphaned file and its test.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (cloud_lane.rs)\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/cloud_lane.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file absent from repo; never tracked in git history)\", \"evidence\": \"`crates/legion-desktop/src/view/cloud_lane.rs` does not exist (git ls-files lists only assistant_rail.rs and code_canvas_painter.rs under view/), and the cited string 'cancellation: mid-flight cancel is available' and any cloud-task cancellation-row rendering are absent from the consolidated view.rs (the only `cancel` affordances are CancelAssistInlinePrediction at line 2302 and CancelDirtyClose at 5166). No live equivalent of the described cloud-lane panel was found.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file/code does not exist in current source. If a cloud-task panel is re-introduced, only emit a cancellation-available row when runtime_enabled and at least one projected task is cancelable; otherwise show a disabled row explaining disabled/no-active/all-terminal.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (fleet_card.rs)\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/fleet_card.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:3259-3303 (fn render_proposal_cards)\", \"evidence\": \"Although fleet_card.rs / fleet_card_view_models / render_card no longer exist, the live equivalent `render_proposal_cards` iterates `snapshot.proposal_ledger_projection.rows.iter().take(4)` (line 3268) and unconditionally renders Approve/Review/Reject for every row using only row.title/payload_kind/risk_label (lines 3284-3299) with no lifecycle/action-readiness gating, while the empty state says 'No pending proposals' (line 3265). An approval-checklist projection carrying lifecycle_state/ready exists (view.rs:5972-5974) but is not consulted, so applied/rejected/terminal proposals still present active approve/reject controls.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In render_proposal_cards (view.rs:3259), filter rows to actionable/pending lifecycle states or disable Approve/Reject for terminal states, surface the lifecycle state on the card, and gate the Approve button on the approval-checklist readiness already available in the projection (lifecycle_state at view.rs:5972) rather than rendering controls for every ledger row.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2 (fleet_card.rs)\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/fleet_card.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:3268 (fn render_proposal_cards)\", \"evidence\": \"The live equivalent hard-limits proposal cards with `for row in snapshot.proposal_ledger_projection.rows.iter().take(4)` (line 3268) and renders no overflow indicator; any rows beyond the first four are silently hidden, matching the described defect.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"After the `.take(4)` loop in render_proposal_cards, when `snapshot.proposal_ledger_projection.rows.len() > 4` render an explicit overflow label, e.g. `theme::muted(format!(\\\"{} more proposals\\\", rows.len() - 4))`, or support paging/scrolling and honor the projection's omitted-row metadata.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (manifest_panel.rs)\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/manifest_panel.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file absent); closest live code crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:5818-5860 (fn trust_rows) and :2356-2362\", \"evidence\": \"`manifest_panel.rs` does not exist and the cited string 'no context items projected before invocation' is nowhere in source. The closest live manifest code (trust_rows, view.rs:5818) gates its summary on `!manifest.items.is_empty() || !manifest.permissions.is_empty()` and truncates items/permissions with `take(10)` and no overflow row, but it does not misreport 'no items projected' (it simply omits the line), so the specific described defect cannot be confirmed against current code.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate the cited panel: file absent. Separately, the live trust_rows item/permission `take(10)` (view.rs:5830,5850) lacks an overflow row; if addressing the spirit of the finding, add an 'N more items omitted from preview' row and include manifest-level omitted_item_count / risk fields even when items is empty.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (provider_setup.rs)\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/provider_setup.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file absent); closest live code crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:2409-2421 and :6141-6159\", \"evidence\": \"`provider_setup.rs` and `provider_policy_rows` do not exist anywhere in the repo. The live provider rendering displays provider_class alongside the authoritative projection fields (availability at 2395; class/risk/privacy/risk_budget at 2411-2420; refusal reason_code/label/risk_label at 6154-6159) and does NOT re-derive policy labels from hard-coded class strings or map Gateway->Unknown, so the described defect is not present in current code.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited function/file absent and live code already uses authoritative provider fields. If a provider policy panel is re-introduced, build rows from availability/refusal/risk_label/privacy_label/route-consent and treat Gateway/Unknown as denied unless explicit route consent is projected.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1 (worker_panel.rs)\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/worker_panel.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file absent); closest live code crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:6547-6567\", \"evidence\": \"`worker_panel.rs` does not exist; no code searches `display_safe_labels` for a `signoff:` prefix anywhere in the repo. In the live workflow rendering, `display_safe_labels` is only joined into a display string (view.rs:6565) and no sign-off recovery action is constructed, so the described label-derived recovery logic is absent from current code.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file/code absent. If workflow recovery actions are re-added, project sign-off identifiers explicitly (or add a dedicated recovery-action projection sourced from sign_off_records) rather than parsing generic display_safe_labels.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2 (worker_panel.rs)\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/src/view/worker_panel.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file absent); related guards in crates/legion-desktop/src/bridge.rs:2261-2312\", \"evidence\": \"`worker_panel.rs` does not exist; no view code constructs `LegionWorkflowVerificationGateId(gate_id)` or `LegionWorkflowConflictId(conflict_id)` from display label text (grep in view.rs finds none; the typed IDs appear only in bridge.rs action variants and in validation guards `with_known_legion_workflow_verification/conflict` at bridge.rs:2261-2312 that check IDs against known metadata). The described view-side ID-from-label transport defect is absent from current code.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file/code absent. If recovery actions are re-added in the view, carry stable gate_id/conflict_id in the projection/recovery view model and dispatch those typed IDs directly, keeping display labels for UI text only.\", \"review_file\": \"desktop-views-part-2.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs:2421-2424\", \"evidence\": \"read_until_correlated_response has `if id != target_json_rpc_id { // Skip notification-shaped or out-of-order responses. continue; }`, so a response carrying another pending json_rpc_id is dropped without being correlated or buffered, leaving that request stranded in pending_by_json_rpc_id.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In read_until_correlated_response, when `id` is present, always call self.client.correlate_response(envelope) and store/queue completed LspCorrelatedResponse by request id in a new map on LspStdioSession; return immediately if it matches expected_request_id, otherwise stash it. Have read_response_for first check that stash before reading new frames. Alternatively serialize one in-flight request at a time.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs:2325-2330, 2393-2429\", \"evidence\": \"read_response_for just calls read_until_correlated_response, which loops on self.process.read_envelope()? with no deadline; LspPendingRequest.timeout_ms and LspClient::resolve_timeout (lib.rs:882) are never consulted on this path.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a deadline derived from pending.timeout_ms around the read loop (e.g. a nonblocking/timed read or watchdog thread on the LspStdioProcess). On expiry call self.client.resolve_timeout(pending.request_id, elapsed_ms), optionally emit $/cancelRequest, and return the Timeout-status LspCorrelatedResponse instead of blocking until EOF.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs:834-835\", \"evidence\": \"prepare_request does `self.next_json_rpc_id = self.next_json_rpc_id.saturating_add(1);`, so once it reaches u64::MAX every later request reuses MAX and overwrites pending_by_json_rpc_id / json_rpc_id_by_request_id entries.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change prepare_request to use checked_add(1) and return an explicit exhaustion LspRuntimeError (or change prepare_request signature to LspRuntimeResult), so id reuse cannot silently corrupt correlation tables.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/lib.rs:1106\", \"evidence\": \"completion_projection_for_item computes `score_basis_points: 10_000u16.saturating_sub((index as u16).saturating_mul(100))`; for index >= 65536 the `index as u16` cast wraps (e.g. 65536 -> 0 -> score 10000) before the multiply, so far-down completions regain top scores.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Compute the penalty in usize/u32: `let penalty = (index as u32).saturating_mul(100); score = 10_000u32.saturating_sub(penalty)` then cast the clamped result to u16.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/bin/mock_lsp_server.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/bin/mock_lsp_server.rs:291-303\", \"evidence\": \"read_frame parses Content-Length and then does `let mut payload = vec![0u8; length];` with no maximum bound, unlike the production read_lsp_frame which checks LspFramer::MAX_FRAME_PAYLOAD_BYTES.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"After parsing `length`, reject `length > LspFramer::MAX_FRAME_PAYLOAD_BYTES` (or a small mock-specific constant) returning MockIoError::Protocol before allocating the payload buffer.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/bin/mock_lsp_server.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-lsp/src/bin/mock_lsp_server.rs:100-101, 220-228\", \"evidence\": \"`id` is Option<u64>; the `other =>` arm always emits `\\\"error\\\": ...` with `\\\"id\\\": id`, which serializes to `\\\"id\\\": null` for notifications (no id), violating the JSON-RPC rule that notifications get no response.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In the unknown-method (`other`) arm, if `id` is None return None (no response). More generally, gate response emission on `id.is_some()` for request-only methods and only handle true notifications when id is absent.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs:797-836, 994-1002, 1205-1213\", \"evidence\": \"handle_transport_envelope dedups/audits on envelope.operation_id and passes it to handlers, but handle_filesystem_operation only checks `operation.operation_id.0 == 0` and handle_process_descriptor only checks `descriptor.operation_id.0 == 0`; validate_envelope (918) never compares the payload's embedded operation_id to envelope.operation_id.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In validate_envelope or each handler, require `operation.operation_id == envelope.operation_id` (and apply the same session/principal/correlation/causality consistency checks) before dispatching; return RemoteRuntimeError::InvalidOperation on mismatch.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs:1177-1193\", \"evidence\": \"validate_mutation_gate only checks proposal_id present, preconditions.has_required_write_guards() (which merely requires granted+nonzero decision_id and a non-empty principal, protocol lib.rs:2330-2339) and workspace_generation; it never calls validate_capability for \\\"remote.fs.write\\\" nor compares preconditions.principal_id to the session/envelope principal.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In validate_mutation_gate, call validate_capability(&preconditions.capability_decision, \\\"remote.fs.write\\\") and return denied on error; compare preconditions.principal_id against the active session/envelope principal; and bind preconditions.correlation_id/causality_id to the operation envelope, denying on mismatch.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs:1089-1095\", \"evidence\": \"create_file builds `content = format!(\\\"remote-created-by-proposal:{}\\\", proposal_id.0)` but stores `fingerprint: metadata_fingerprint(\\\"remote-created-by-proposal\\\")`, fingerprinting the constant string rather than the actual content.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Set `fingerprint: metadata_fingerprint(&content)` after building `content`, matching seed_file (lib.rs:774) and write_file (lib.rs:1064).\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs:1063, 1094, 1166-1170\", \"evidence\": \"write_file sets `entry.snapshot_id = preconditions.snapshot_id`, create_file sets `snapshot_id: preconditions.snapshot_id`, and rename_file removes/reinserts the old entry unchanged, so no new post-mutation snapshot id is allocated.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Derive a fresh snapshot id per accepted mutation (e.g. like seed_file's `SnapshotId(stable_hash_u128(...) | 1)` combined with content_version/operation_id), assign it to the entry, and return it via with_snapshot/snapshot_for_path in write_file, create_file, and rename_file.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs:1670-1680\", \"evidence\": \"common_headers wraps both AUTHORIZATION and X-Legion-Client-Identity in `if let Ok(header_value) = HeaderValue::from_str(...)`, silently dropping the header when the configured token/identity is invalid, producing an unauthenticated/misattributed request.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Make common_headers return Result<HeaderMap, RemoteRuntimeError>; map HeaderValue::from_str errors to RemoteRuntimeError::InvalidOperation/Transport and propagate through send_with_body callers instead of dropping headers.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote/src/lib.rs:340-347, 1749, 1765, 1775, 1785\", \"evidence\": \"validate_cloud_task_id only rejects empty/whitespace ids; the HTTP transport methods format `task_id.0` straight into paths like `/v1/cloud/tasks/{}/events`, so ids containing `/`, `?`, `#` alter the endpoint path.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Percent-encode task_id.0 as a single path segment (e.g. via a NON_ALPHANUMERIC/path encoder) before formatting URLs, and tighten validate_cloud_task_id to reject ids containing path/query/control characters.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote-transport/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote-transport/src/lib.rs:731-737\", \"evidence\": \"On accept, seen_operations.insert and inflight_operations.insert grow per operation while only accepted_sequences is trimmed to replay_window_size (lines 734-736); seen_operations is never evicted, and replay_window reports accepted_operation_count = seen_operations.len() (line 909).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Track operation ids together with their sequence and evict seen_operations entries whose sequence falls below the lowest retained accepted_sequence when the replay window slides; keep inflight_operations separate (already removed on ack) and base replay-window counts on the bounded set.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote-transport/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote-transport/src/lib.rs:762-779\", \"evidence\": \"checkpoint only validates session match, event_sequence != 0, and that last_operation_id is in seen_operations; it never checks checkpoint.event_sequence against self.last_sequence or the accepted replay window before storing last_checkpoint.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In checkpoint, reject when `checkpoint.event_sequence.0 > self.last_sequence.0` or when it is below the lowest retained accepted_sequence (outside the replay window) with RemoteTransportCoreError::ReplayRejected before assigning self.last_checkpoint.\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote-transport/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote-transport/src/lib.rs:268-281, legion-protocol/src/lib.rs:22085-22086\", \"evidence\": \"connect_inner calls validate_remote_transport_connection_attempt before the addition, and that validator rejects `attempt.timeout_ms == 0 || attempt.timeout_ms > 120_000`, so `Instant::now() + Duration::from_millis(timeout_ms)` is bounded to <=120s and cannot overflow.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"lsp-&-remote.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs:1713-1717 (metadata_hash), 1590-1595 (metadata_fingerprint)\", \"evidence\": \"metadata_hash builds the digest with `let mut hasher = DefaultHasher::new(); value.hash(&mut hasher); format!(\\\"{:016x}\\\", hasher.finish())` and metadata_fingerprint stores that 64-bit non-cryptographic value into FileFingerprint while labeling algorithm with domain strings like \\\"assisted-ai-provider\\\"/\\\"assisted-ai-request\\\" (lines 672-700). The same hash also backs path/command/policy/title fields (937, 985, 1562, 1580).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace DefaultHasher in metadata_hash with a stable cryptographic digest (sha2::Sha256 or blake3) emitting full hex; have metadata_fingerprint set FileFingerprint.algorithm to the actual digest name plus the domain-separation label, and add golden/stability tests asserting fixed digest output across runs.\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs:1761-1796\", \"evidence\": \"In the MetadataOnly/None branch, scalar strings pass through verbatim (`is_metadata_value` returns true for Value::String at 1791-1796) unless the key hits the small denylist in `is_sensitive_key` (text/source/secret/token/password/payload at 1781-1789). Keys like summary, reason, message, diagnostics, path, command retain raw strings.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Convert the redaction in the MetadataOnly branch to allowlist-based: only pass through known-safe keys verbatim; for any other free-form string emit a hash+length summary (reuse metadata_hash + .len()) instead of the raw value, and add denied-marker scanning via contains_forbidden_assisted_ai_marker.\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs:1719-1727 (assert_core_ids); callers at 602,733,815,859,891,1026,1048,1068,1114,1249,1269,1368,1398,1432,1489,1553\", \"evidence\": \"assert_core_ids uses `assert_ne!` on nil causality, zero correlation, and zero sequence (1724-1726), and ~16 public `fn ... -> EventEnvelope` helpers (e.g. save_denied_event at 1018-1038) call it directly, so externally supplied invalid ids panic the caller rather than returning an error.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change the public envelope helpers that validate externally supplied ids to return Result<EventEnvelope, ObservabilityError>, replacing assert_core_ids with a validating function that returns InvalidCausalityId/InvalidCorrelationId/InvalidSequence errors (mirroring validate_envelope); keep assert-based panics only for internal invariants.\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs:577-594\", \"evidence\": \"proposal_audit_record sets proposal_id from `proposal.proposal_id` while copying lifecycle_state/timestamp/principal/capability/correlation_id/causality_id from `transition`, but never compares `transition.proposal_id` (which exists, legion-protocol/src/lib.rs:4859) against `proposal.proposal_id`.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change proposal_audit_record to return Result<ProposalAuditRecord, ObservabilityError>; at the top return an error if `transition.proposal_id != proposal.proposal_id`. Add a test passing mismatched ids and asserting rejection.\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/lib.rs:559-573 (schema_version hardcoded at line 572)\", \"evidence\": \"event_metadata_record copies envelope fields but sets `schema_version: 1` as a literal instead of `envelope.schema_version`, so a bumped envelope schema yields a metadata record reporting stale version 1.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Set `schema_version: envelope.schema_version` in event_metadata_record, or add a distinctly-named metadata-record schema field documented as independent from the envelope schema; add a test bumping envelope.schema_version and asserting propagation.\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/telemetry.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"The cited file crates/legion-observability/src/telemetry.rs does not exist (the crate has only src/lib.rs) and `suggestion_metadata_summary` appears in no source file (grep matches only the review docs). The referenced code cannot be located in the current tree.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/minidump.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/minidump.rs does not exist and no `crash_reports_enabled`/`symbol_upload`/`symbolicated` consent-gating code exists in legion-observability/src/lib.rs or any source crate. The cited code is absent from the current workspace.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/minidump.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"No minidump.rs file and no crash-summary envelope code (`crash_id`, `metadata_summary`, `symbol_upload_target`) exist anywhere in the current source crates; the referenced helper is not present to validate.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/minidump.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"minidump.rs does not exist and no `symbolicated` / `symbol_upload_state` field assignment exists in any source file; the described code cannot be located in the current tree.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/training.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/training.rs does not exist and `consented_training_candidate_from_records` appears only in review docs, not in any source file. The cited training-candidate code is absent.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/training.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"training.rs does not exist; no AssistedAiConsentState::NotRequired training-gate logic exists in any source crate. The referenced code cannot be located.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-observability/src/training.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"training.rs does not exist and no ProposalLifecycleState::Approved -> Accepted training-label mapping code is present in any source file; the described logic is absent from the current workspace.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-debug/src/evidence.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"The entire legion-debug crate does not exist (no crates/legion-debug directory, not referenced in any Cargo.toml) and `debug_adapter_audit_evidence`/`test_run_summary_evidence`/the `fingerprint` helper appear only in review docs. The cited fake-sha256 code is not in the current tree.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"observability-&-debug.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs:1003-1019\", \"evidence\": \"`NativeProcessService::execute` calls `command.output()` (blocking until the child exits) at line 1003, then only checks `if elapsed > timeout` at lines 1012-1014; the timeout is never enforced while the child runs.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In `execute`, replace `command.output()` with `command.stdout(Stdio::piped()).stderr(Stdio::piped()).spawn()`, then loop on `child.try_wait()` against `request.timeout` (sleeping briefly between polls), and on timeout call `child.kill()`/`child.wait()` (plus process-group kill on Unix) before returning `PlatformError::Timeout`. Drain piped stdout/stderr after exit.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs:1108\", \"evidence\": \"In the Unix `spawn_native_pty`, after `command.env_clear()` the loop is `for (key, value) in child_environment_vars(&[])`, passing an empty slice and ignoring `request.env`.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change `child_environment_vars(&[])` to `child_environment_vars(&request.env)` at line 1108 to mirror the non-PTY `execute` path, and add a test asserting an injected env var is visible to the PTY child.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs:1800,1834-1840\", \"evidence\": \"`close_pty` calls `self.kill_pty(session_id, PtyKillMode::Terminate)` (line 1800); in `kill_pty` the target for Terminate is `Pid::from_raw(pid)` (positive PID) since only `Interrupt | KillTree` use `-pid` (lines 1835-1839), so only the session leader receives SIGTERM and grandchildren survive.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a close/terminate path that signals the process group `Pid::from_raw(-pid)` (the child is the session leader via `setsid`), escalate to SIGKILL after the 500ms wait, and reap the leader before removing the session entry. Either add a dedicated mode or include `Terminate` in the negative-pid branch.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-platform/src/lib.rs:974\", \"evidence\": \"`list_directory` builds entries with `.filter_map(|entry| entry.ok())`, silently dropping any `read_dir` entry whose result is an `Err`.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace `filter_map(|entry| entry.ok())` with explicit error propagation (collect into `Result<Vec<_>, _>` mapping errors via `PlatformError::from_io_error`), or accumulate omitted-entry diagnostics in a structured partial result if partial listings are intended.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs:279-286\", \"evidence\": \"`fn stable_hash` uses `std::collections::hash_map::DefaultHasher` and is consumed for supposedly stable ids: `WorkspaceId(stable_hash(...))` (455), hunk id (1790), and content-version digest `(size ^ ts.0).wrapping_add(stable_hash(hash) as u64)` (3447); DefaultHasher is not a stable cross-version contract.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the DefaultHasher body in `stable_hash` with a fixed algorithm (FNV-1a, xxHash with fixed seed, or truncated SHA-256), and embed an algorithm version tag in any persisted/protocol-facing ids (WorkspaceId, hunk ids, content-version digest).\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs:1582-1586,1592-1637\", \"evidence\": \"`git_status_entries_gix` does `let debug = format!(\\\"{item:?}\\\")` then scrapes paths via `extract_gix_status_path` (searching `path: \\\"`) and status via `extract_gix_status_code` (substring match on `untracked`/`modified`/etc.), relying on the unstable gix Debug format.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the Debug-scraping with typed `gix` status item accessors for path and status kind (rename/copy/delete/untracked/modified), or keep the CLI porcelain parser as authoritative until typed gix mapping exists; add rename/copy/delete/untracked tests.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-project/src/lib.rs:3120,4730\", \"evidence\": \"Both workspace-search sites iterate `for (line_number, line) in text.split_inclusive('\\\\n').enumerate()` and set `line_number: line_number as u32` on `WorkspaceSearchHit`, so the first line reports 0 (zero-based).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"If `WorkspaceSearchHit::line_number` is user-facing, change both sites to `line_number: line_number.saturating_add(1) as u32`; otherwise document the field as zero-based and ensure all consumers apply the same convention.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:2462-2465,2508-2511,2528,2621-2623\", \"evidence\": \"`tree_sitter_supports_language` returns true when `plugin_tree_sitter_grammar_is_registered` (line 2623), but after that gate `parse` calls `parse_tree_sitter_rust(source)` (2528), `highlight_captures_from_text` calls `tree_sitter_highlight_captures` (2465), and `code_chunk_descriptors_from_text` calls `tree_sitter_code_chunk_descriptors` (2511) unconditionally as Rust.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Split bundled-Rust support from plugin registration: only invoke the Rust parser/highlight/chunk routines when language is `rust`/`rs`; route registered plugin grammars through a real loaded-grammar worker, and until that exists fall back to `LexicalFallbackParser` with a diagnostic for plugin languages.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:2658-2660,2682-2685,2690-2693\", \"evidence\": \"All accesses to the global `PLUGIN_TREE_SITTER_GRAMMAR_REGISTRY` mutex use `.lock().expect(\\\"plugin tree-sitter grammar registry should not be poisoned\\\")` in `register_plugin_tree_sitter_grammars`, `plugin_tree_sitter_grammar_is_registered`, and the reset helper.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace each `.expect(...)` with fallible handling: recover via `PoisonError::into_inner()` or treat a poisoned lock as `false`/0 with a diagnostic, so support checks and registration cannot panic the indexing process.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:5296-5313\", \"evidence\": \"`build_rename_preview_payload` builds `target_coverage` from a single `SymbolFileMapRecord` yet hardcodes `coverage_kind: ProposalTargetCoverageKind::Complete` and `omitted_target_count: 0`.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Set `coverage_kind` to a partial variant (and/or populate `omitted_target_count`/diagnostics) unless the `SymbolFileMapRecord` carries an explicit workspace-complete/freshness proof that cross-file references were searched.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-tracker/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-tracker/src/lib.rs:201-209\", \"evidence\": \"The Ready-state guard checks `verification_gate_ids.is_empty()`, `required_sign_off_count`, and `signed_off_count`, but the struct field `failed_verification_count` (declared line 122) is never validated, so a Ready record with failures passes `validate`.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add `|| self.failed_verification_count > 0` to the Ready-state condition at lines 201-204 (or a separate check) so a merge-ready record with failed verification gates is rejected; add a regression test.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-telemetry/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-telemetry/src/lib.rs:580-609,704\", \"evidence\": \"`pending_batch` takes `consent` and `endpoint` independently and stores both into the batch; `validate_hosted_telemetry_export_batch` (legion-protocol:22534) checks `endpoint.allowlisted` and consent fields but never compares `batch.endpoint` to `batch.consent.endpoint`, and `export_once` uploads to `batch.endpoint` (line 704-705).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In `pending_batch`/`export_once`, reject when the passed `endpoint` does not match `consent.endpoint` (compare endpoint_id, label, region, schema_version), or derive the upload endpoint solely from `consent.endpoint`. Optionally add the equality check inside `validate_hosted_telemetry_export_batch`.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-telemetry/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-telemetry/src/lib.rs:534-555\", \"evidence\": \"`FileBackedTelemetrySpool::open` does `serde_json::from_str(&text)` into `PersistedTelemetrySpool` with no validation of `schema_version`, `records.len()` vs `config.max_records`, or per-record `validate_hosted_telemetry_spool_record`.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"After decoding in `open`, verify `state.schema_version` is supported, cap/reject when `state.records.len() > config.max_records`, and run `validate_hosted_telemetry_spool_record` on each decoded record; quarantine or return a clear `TelemetrySpoolError` for invalid/corrupt files.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-vscode-compat/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-vscode-compat/src/lib.rs:148-160,508-518\", \"evidence\": \"`parse_manifest` (lines 148-160) never reads `main`/`browser`; `required_tier` (508-518) computes the tier only from activation event/contribution tiers, so an extension with executable `main` but declarative contributions and no activation events stays `Tier0Declarative` -> `NoneRequired`/`Supported`.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Parse `package_json.get(\\\"main\\\")`/`get(\\\"browser\\\")` in `parse_manifest`, and when an executable entrypoint is present raise `required_tier` to at least the extension-host-sidecar tier and adjust `aggregate_status`/`requested_capabilities` to require a host policy decision even without activation events.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-vscode-compat/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-vscode-compat/src/lib.rs:257-261\", \"evidence\": \"`required_string` does `optional_string(...).filter(|s| !s.trim().is_empty())` but returns the original untrimmed string; publisher/name/version (148-150) feed `VsCodeExtensionId(format!(\\\"{publisher}.{name}\\\"))` (176), so whitespace yields malformed ids.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In `required_string`, return the trimmed value (e.g. `.map(|s| s.trim().to_string())`) or reject values where trimming changes them, ensuring publisher/name/version identity fields are normalized before building `extension_id`.\", \"review_file\": \"platform-&-misc-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs:160 and 195-197\", \"evidence\": \"The output quota check `if request.metadata_label.len() as u64 > plugin.manifest.quotas.max_output_bytes` (line 160) only compares the single call's label length; `output_bytes_used` is accumulated via `saturating_add` (lines 195-197) but never read to deny a subsequent call.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In dispatch_host_call, before accepting, compute `let next = plugin.output_bytes_used.saturating_add(request.metadata_label.len() as u64);` and deny with `PluginDenialReason::QuotaExceeded` when `next > plugin.manifest.quotas.max_output_bytes`; only then commit `output_bytes_used = next`. Also reset the counter at the invocation boundary if the quota is per-invocation.\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs:74 (doc), 85 (init), 153 (check), 194 (increment)\", \"evidence\": \"`host_calls_used` is documented as \\\"Host calls consumed during the active invocation\\\" (line 73-74), initialized to 0 only in `LoadedPlugin::new` (line 85), incremented at line 194, and never reset; there is no invocation begin/end so it accumulates for the plugin's lifetime while being checked against per-invocation `max_host_calls`.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Introduce explicit invocation start/end methods on PluginRuntimeHost that reset `host_calls_used` (and `output_bytes_used`) at the invocation boundary, or rename/redefine the quota semantics to lifetime and update the doc comment and tests accordingly.\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/lib.rs:255-260\", \"evidence\": \"In `PluginRuntimePort::handle`, the `CommandDescriptor` and `Contribution` arms immediately return `Ok(PluginResponse::CommandRegistered(descriptor.command_id))` / `ContributionRegistered(descriptor.name)` with no check that a manifest was loaded, that the item belongs to a loaded plugin, or that its required capability was declared.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a plugin/capability lookup to those arms: require the descriptor to carry a PluginId, verify `host.plugins` contains it in a loaded/activated state, confirm the command/contribution exists in `manifest.contributions` and its `required_capability` is in `declared_capabilities`, and return a ProtocolError (or Denied response) otherwise before emitting Registered.\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/host.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-plugin/src/host.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"The file `host.rs` does not exist (git ls-files shows only Cargo.toml and lib.rs) and there is no `wasmtime` dependency anywhere in the workspace; the crate is metadata-only and executes no WASM, so the described Wasmtime quota-enforcement defect has no corresponding code.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/host.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-plugin/src/host.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"No `host.rs`, no `Linker`/`invoke`/`load_fixture` code, and no `env::host_log` import path exist in the current crate; the described host-interface inconsistency references code that is not present in the codebase.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/host.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-plugin/src/host.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"There is no `used_host_calls` accounting tied to guest instantiation in current source; `host.rs` and any Wasmtime invocation path do not exist (only lib.rs's metadata `host_calls_used` exists, covered by Finding 2).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/host.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-plugin/src/host.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"No `finish_trap`, audit-log scanning, or trap/instantiation state-machine code exists; `host.rs` is absent from the crate so the described Running/Crashed inconsistency has no corresponding code.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/manifest.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-plugin/src/manifest.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"`manifest.rs` does not exist and `permission_reason_for_capability` appears only in review docs (grep finds it only under .legion-review); the described per-capability permission-review row logic is not part of the codebase.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/registry.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-plugin/src/registry.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"`registry.rs` does not exist; `SignedExtensionRegistry` and `validate_installable` appear only in review documents, not in any source file, so the described missing-validation defect has no corresponding code.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/src/registry.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A - crates/legion-plugin/src/registry.rs does not exist\", \"evidence\": \"No `registry.rs` and no signature/trust-acceptance logic exist in the crate (grep for SignedExtensionRegistry hits only .legion-review docs); the described forged-signature acceptance path is not present in current source.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"plugin-system.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/lib.rs:287-322\", \"evidence\": \"path_is_within_scope now calls resolve_for_scope_check (lines 301-322) which canonicalizes the longest existing ancestor via std::fs::canonicalize (following symlinks) before the starts_with prefix check, and the doc comment explicitly addresses the symlink-escape concern; lexical normalize_path is only a fallback when no ancestor exists.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/lib.rs:151-167\", \"evidence\": \"ActivatedSandbox::activate still returns `Self` (not Result) and unconditionally pushes a SandboxAuditEvent with allowed:true and reason \\\"sandbox activated\\\" with no backend/platform compatibility validation; SandboxError::{UnsupportedBackend,DocumentedFallbackRequired} (lines 248-258) are never used by activation.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Change `activate` signature to `-> Result<Self, SandboxError>`; validate platform/backend pairing (Seatbelt=>MacOS, BubblewrapLandlock=>Linux, RestrictedToken/AppContainer=>Windows) returning SandboxError::UnsupportedBackend on mismatch; only push the allowed Activate audit event after the OS backend is confirmed installed, and require explicit policy acceptance before constructing DocumentedFallback.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/landlock.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/landlock.rs does not exist on disk or in git history (git log --all returns nothing), and LandlockProfile appears only in the .legion-review markdown files; yet lib.rs:11 declares `pub mod landlock;` (a dangling module). Note legion-sandbox has no Cargo.toml and is not a workspace member, so it is not compiled.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited source file and LandlockProfile::compile are absent from the repository. Locate or recreate the module before assessing; separately, the dangling `pub mod landlock;` in lib.rs:11 would prevent compilation if the crate were built.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/seatbelt.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/seatbelt.rs does not exist on disk or in git history; SeatbeltProfile appears only in review markdown. lib.rs:13 declares `pub mod seatbelt;` referencing a nonexistent file. The crate is not a workspace member.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file and SeatbeltProfile::compile are absent. Locate/recreate the module before assessing; the dangling `pub mod seatbelt;` in lib.rs:13 is itself broken.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/windows.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/windows.rs does not exist on disk or in git history; WindowsProfile appears only in review markdown. lib.rs:14 declares `pub mod windows;` referencing a nonexistent file. The crate is not a workspace member.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file and WindowsProfile::compile are absent. Locate/recreate the module before assessing; the dangling `pub mod windows;` in lib.rs:14 is itself broken.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/windows.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"windows.rs and its `documented_fallback` field do not exist in the repository or git history; only referenced in review markdown.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file is absent. Locate/recreate the module before assessing.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/network.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-sandbox/src/network.rs:56-71\", \"evidence\": \"allowlist_matches_target returns true via `allowlisted_port.is_none() && allowlisted_host == target_host && target_port.is_some()` (line 70), so a host-only entry like \\\"localhost\\\" matches \\\"localhost:2375\\\" or any port; the crate test at lib.rs even relies on \\\"localhost\\\" matching \\\"localhost:8080\\\".\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Remove the port-broadening clause at network.rs:70 so only exact host:port (or exact authority) entries match, or add an explicit `allow_any_port` flag to SandboxScope and only broaden when set; optionally define safe default ports per scheme so non-default ports require explicit allowlisting.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs:133-148, 183-192\", \"evidence\": \"NormalizedPolicyPath::starts_with only enforces prefix equality when root.prefix is Some (line 134); the default PathPolicy roots are \\\"./\\\" (lines 186-187) which parse to {prefix:None, segments:[]}, so starts_with skips the prefix check and zips empty segments (`.all` on empty == true), making `can_access(\\\"/tmp/file\\\", Read)` return true under the default policy.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In NormalizedPolicyPath::starts_with, fail closed when root has no prefix and no segments (e.g. `if root.prefix.is_none() && root.segments.is_empty() { return false; }`), and resolve relative roots like \\\"./\\\" against a trusted canonical workspace root inside PathPolicy::can_access (or store an absolute workspace root in PathPolicy::default) so an empty relative root cannot match absolute candidates.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs:1852-1890\", \"evidence\": \"In the `fs.` branch, fs.write with no target_path falls through to `SecurityDecision::allow()` (line 1885), and every non-write fs.* capability returns `SecurityDecision::allow()` (lines 1887-1889) without consulting PathPolicy/readable/blocked roots.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Require target_path for all disk-touching fs.* capabilities: replace the no-path `allow()` at 1885 with a deny when path is None, and replace the non-write `else { allow() }` at 1887-1889 with PathPolicy::can_access using PathAccess::Read for fs.read and PathAccess::List for fs.list (deny when path missing); keep only genuinely pathless fs capabilities explicitly allowlisted.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs:1402-1414\", \"evidence\": \"remote.fs.read/remote.fs.write only check runtime_sessions_enabled && filesystem_enabled, and write additionally calls write_size_decision; the path is never required and PathPolicy::can_access is never invoked, so enabling remote filesystem bypasses read/write/blocked-root restrictions.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In the `remote.fs.read | remote.fs.write` arm, require a canonical remote target path from context, apply self.policy.path_policy.can_access with PathAccess::Read/Write and the blocked-root checks used for local fs.*, and deny when path context is missing.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs:389, 406-415, 1909-1921, 1948-1958\", \"evidence\": \"CommandTaxonomy maps `git` => CommandClass::Read (line 389) and classify() keys only on the first whitespace token (lines 406-415), so `git push` is Read; terminal.launch only denies CommandClass::Network (lines 1913-1920), permitting shells/mutating tools; cmd.* only denies Mutate/Terminal/Network for untrusted (lines 1950-1955), so `git push` (Read) is allowed even untrusted.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Classify by verb+subcommand (parse `git push|clean|checkout|fetch` as Mutate/Network) rather than first token; in terminal.launch deny CommandClass::{Mutate,Terminal,Network,Unknown} (not just Network) unless allowlisted; treat Unknown commands as deny-by-default for untrusted workspaces in both the cmd.* arm and requires_trusted_workspace_for_request.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs:459-475, 1925-1933\", \"evidence\": \"The `lsp.` decision arm only checks require_trusted_workspace then returns SecurityDecision::allow() for `launch` and for any other subcommand (lines 1930-1933); LspLaunchPolicy.allowed_binaries and deny_network_refresh (lines 463-465) are never read in the decision path.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In the lsp. arm require context.command_binary for lsp.launch, reject when the resolved binary is not in lsp_policy.allowed_binaries, deny network-refresh-style commands when deny_network_refresh is set, and change the catch-all `_ => allow()` to deny unknown lsp.* subcommands.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs:2052-2053\", \"evidence\": \"CapabilityBrokerPort::handle returns `CapabilityRequest::Grant(grant) => Ok(CapabilityResponse::Granted(grant))` and `Deny(deny) => Ok(CapabilityResponse::Denied(deny))` directly, with no namespace/policy/trust/principal validation, so any caller submitting a Grant gets a granted response without going through decide_with_request_context.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Do not echo Grant/Deny payloads back as authoritative responses: either reject Grant/Deny at this boundary (treat all external input as Request), or validate the grant/deny against a trusted/signed decision store before returning Granted/Denied.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-security/src/lib.rs:2017, 2047-2048\", \"evidence\": \"handle clones the broker (`let mut owned = self.clone();`, line 2017) and increments owned.counter; the clone is dropped at return so self.counter never advances, and `decision_id.unwrap_or(CapabilityDecisionId(owned.counter))` (line 2048) yields the same generated id across repeated calls when callers omit decision_id.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Store the counter behind interior mutability (AtomicU64 or Mutex) and increment on &self so generated CapabilityDecisionIds are monotonic for the real instance, or require caller-provided decision_id at the protocol boundary and reject missing ids.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/policy.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-security/src/policy.rs does not exist on disk or in git history; `allows_rule_ids` is absent from lib.rs (the only security source). lib.rs:24 declares `pub mod policy;` and lib.rs:25 re-exports ProposalAutoApprovalPolicy from it, so the module is referenced but its file is missing (build would not compile).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file and ProposalAutoApprovalPolicy::allows_rule_ids cannot be located. Recreate/locate the policy module first; if the described `.all()` on empty rule_ids exists, add `!rule_ids.is_empty()` guard before accepting.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/risk.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-security/src/risk.rs does not exist on disk or in git history; `is_dependency_or_lockfile` is absent from lib.rs. lib.rs:26 declares `pub mod risk;` referencing a nonexistent file.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file and is_dependency_or_lockfile cannot be located. Recreate/locate the risk module first, then ensure manifests (Cargo.toml, package.json, etc.) are covered.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-security/src/risk.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-security/src/risk.rs does not exist on disk or in git history; the path-scope rule and workspace_root handling described cannot be located in lib.rs. The `risk` module is declared at lib.rs:26 but has no file.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file and the path-scope risk rule cannot be located. Recreate/locate the risk module first, then make absent workspace_root a non-low/deny finding for auto-approval.\", \"review_file\": \"sandbox-&-security.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs:499-539 (PersistedState), 541-572 (From<&InMemoryStorage>), 742-753 (From<PersistedState>)\", \"evidence\": \"PersistedState (499-539) has no protocol_workspace_configs/protocol_file_metadata/protocol_sessions/protocol_trust fields, From<&InMemoryStorage> (541-572) never copies them, and From<PersistedState> reinitializes all four to HashMap::new() at lines 750-753, so file-backed save responses succeed but the records are lost on reopen.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add the four maps to PersistedState with #[serde(default)] (mirroring the other protocol_* fields at 508-534), copy them in From<&InMemoryStorage> (around 550), and restore from value.* in From<PersistedState> instead of HashMap::new() at 750-753; add a flush/reopen regression test exercising SaveWorkspaceConfig/SaveFileMetadata/SaveSessionRecord/SaveTrustRecord.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs:673-682 (record_event)\", \"evidence\": \"record_event emits first (let emitted = self.event_sink.emit(...); line 678) then stores metadata (line 679) and only checks emitted? at 680, so emit-success/store-failure leaks an event with no audit metadata, and store-success/emit-failure returns Err despite a persisted record.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Reorder in record_event to persist+validate metadata first (call self.handle(SaveEventMetadata...) and propagate its error), and only after success call event_sink.emit; if emit fails after a successful store, record/return an explicit partial-failure state rather than discarding the persisted record.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs:491-496 (stable_storage_sum), used at 390 and 419\", \"evidence\": \"stable_storage_sum folds bytes with wrapping_add and appends len ('sum:{sum}:len:{}'), and recover_from_backup verifies integrity solely via this sum at line 419, so byte permutations/swaps preserving sum+len pass checksum verification.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace stable_storage_sum body with a SHA-256 digest (e.g. via the sha2 crate already used elsewhere), set STORAGE_CHECKSUM_ALGORITHM accordingly, and keep an explicit legacy branch in recover_from_backup keyed on backup.checksum.algorithm for old 'sum:len' markers if backward compatibility is required.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/lib.rs:786-795 (FileBackedStorage::open)\", \"evidence\": \"In the corrupt-parse branch the rename result is discarded (line 790: let _ = fs::rename(&path, &quarantine);) yet StorageError::Corrupt is returned with quarantine_path regardless, so a failed rename leaves the corrupt primary in place while reporting it was quarantined.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In open(), capture fs::rename's Result; on Err either return StorageError::Failed describing the quarantine failure, or fall back to copy-then-remove and only populate quarantine_path after the move actually succeeds.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/secrets.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file and symbols absent)\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/secrets.rs does not exist (only lib.rs is present), and InMemorySecretStore/SecretStoreError appear nowhere in the workspace source (only in .legion-review docs); git history shows the file was never committed.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/secrets.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file and symbols absent)\", \"evidence\": \"provider_secret_reference and the format!(\\\"{provider_id}:{secret_name}\\\") keyring-account construction do not exist anywhere in the current workspace source; the cited secrets.rs file is absent.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-storage/src/secrets.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file and symbols absent)\", \"evidence\": \"The 'not found' string-matching keyring classification described lives in the non-existent secrets.rs; the only keyring usage in the repo is legion-retention's keyring_error (lib.rs:1457) which formats the error rather than string-matching, so the cited code cannot be located.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs:432-437 (capture_descriptor) and 594 (capture_bundle)\", \"evidence\": \"Both lease constructors set expires_at to TimestampMillis(self.policy.ttl_ms) (the map_or arms at 435-436 are identical and meaningless; capture_bundle line 594 does the same), treating a duration as an absolute epoch ms and ignoring grant.expires_at, so a 60_000ms TTL yields expiry at 1970-01-01T00:01:00Z and purge_expired (1196) deletes it immediately under wall-clock now.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Supply a clock to the capture path and set expires_at = TimestampMillis(min(now_ms + self.policy.ttl_ms, grant.consent.expires_at.0)) in both capture_descriptor and capture_bundle; update purge tests (e.g. purge_expired_only_deletes_bundles_past_recorded_lease_expiry) to use absolute expiry rather than TTL literals.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs:1217-1240 (pack_files); capture_bundle checks at 567 and 624\", \"evidence\": \"pack_files appends every file's bytes (1234-1237) with no cumulative-byte check against request.max_bytes, and capture_bundle only rejects empty/over-config.max_bundle_bytes payloads (567, 624); request.max_bytes is used solely as descriptor metadata, so a caller can exceed the consent-bound budget up to the vault config limit.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In pack_files, accumulate packed.len() (or raw file byte total) and return RawSourceVaultError::Denied once it would exceed request.max_bytes, before returning; optionally also assert sealed.encrypted_byte_len <= request.max_bytes (or document tag/header overhead) in capture_bundle.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs:1246-1252 (flush_index)\", \"evidence\": \"flush_index serializes the index and writes it with plain fs::write(self.root.join(\\\"index.json\\\"), text) (line 1251), with no temp-file/fsync/rename, so an interrupted or disk-full write can truncate index.json and lose all bundle metadata.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the fs::write in flush_index with an atomic write: create a temp file in self.root, write+sync_all, rename over index.json, and sync the parent dir (mirroring legion-storage's write_file_atomically); add corrupt-index recovery/quarantine on open.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs:629-647 (capture_bundle)\", \"evidence\": \"capture_bundle writes ciphertext via fs::write at line 629 before inserting index entries (642-646) and flush_index() at 647; if flush_index fails the function returns Err but the .vault file remains on disk unreferenced by the persisted index, and a later same-id capture can overwrite it (the contains_key guard at 576 only checks in-memory index).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Write ciphertext to a temp path, stage the index mutations, call flush_index, and only on success rename temp->bundle_path; on flush_index error remove the temp/ciphertext file and revert the in-memory index inserts.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-retention/src/lib.rs:1174 (delete_bundle) and 1211 (purge_expired)\", \"evidence\": \"delete_bundle calls fs::remove_file(...).map_err(io_error)? at line 1174 before touching index state, so a missing ciphertext returns an Err and leaves the descriptor; purge_expired invokes self.delete_bundle(tombstone)? at 1211, aborting the entire purge on the first missing file.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In delete_bundle, treat NotFound from fs::remove_file as recoverable (log/record a tombstone, proceed to remove index entries) rather than returning Err; in purge_expired, accumulate per-bundle failures into a report and continue the loop instead of propagating with ?.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs:244-260 (from_snapshot)\", \"evidence\": \"from_snapshot builds the service from snapshot.retained/workflow_retained/trace_retained and validates only individual records (250-258); snapshot.schema_version (field at line 167) is never read, so version 0 or future-unsupported snapshots are accepted.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"At the top of from_snapshot, reject snapshot.schema_version == 0 and any version above the supported max (return a MemoryError variant), or route unsupported-but-known versions through a migration before constructing Self.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs:467-483 (validate_memory_candidate)\", \"evidence\": \"validate_memory_candidate only wraps the id into audit_id: format!(\\\"memory:{}\\\", candidate.candidate_id) (469) and delegates to validate_phase4_runtime_audit_record, whose validate_assisted_ai_audit_string (legion-protocol lib.rs:11524-11535) checks only forbidden markers, not emptiness, so an empty candidate_id (audit_id \\\"memory:\\\") passes; note validate_legion_workflow_candidate at line 706 already has the missing trim().is_empty() check.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add an explicit `if candidate.candidate_id.trim().is_empty() { return Err(MemoryError::InvalidMetadata(...)) }` at the start of validate_memory_candidate (mirroring line 706), plus a unit test rejecting empty candidate ids.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs:300-307 (retain), 332-340 (retain_legion_workflow_candidate), 367-372 (retain_trace_record); deletes at 310-314, 345-349, 377-381\", \"evidence\": \"All three retain methods just push onto the Vec without checking for an existing candidate_id/trace_id (e.g. self.retained.push(candidate) at 305), while the corresponding delete methods filter out every matching id (313, 348, 380), so duplicates can accumulate and make delete counts/exports ambiguous.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"On each retain path, reject or replace when an entry with the same candidate_id/trace_id already exists (or migrate the Vecs to keyed HashMaps), and add tests asserting a repeated retain does not duplicate; keep delete semantics consistent with the chosen uniqueness rule.\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-memory/src/lib.rs:694 (from_session_metadata)\", \"evidence\": \"from_session_metadata derives correlation_id/causality_id from the session but hard-codes event_sequence: EventSequence(13) at line 694 for every generated candidate, so candidates from different sessions/snapshots share the same synthetic sequence.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Derive the sequence from session metadata (e.g. a session event counter) or add an event_sequence parameter to from_session_metadata supplied by the caller's sequencing source, instead of the literal EventSequence(13).\", \"review_file\": \"storage,-retention-&-memory.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs:553-559 (spawn_pty), :521-527 (RuntimeSession)\", \"evidence\": \"launch() always spawns with `cwd: None` in PtyRequest (line 558) and RuntimeSession {platform_session_id, next_sequence, correlation_id, causality_id} stores no cwd or deadline, while validate_launch_policy only checks cwd_policy/timeout_seconds for nonzero/format. No timeout is ever passed to the PTY or polled.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add `cwd: Option<String>` and `deadline`/`timeout_seconds` fields to RuntimeSession; in launch() derive a policy-approved cwd from policy.cwd_policy and pass it into PtyRequest.cwd; store the deadline and enforce it in poll_output/cleanup or in the PtyService. If cwd_policy is only descriptive, rename it to make non-enforcement explicit.\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs:563-567 (launch), :712-723 (poll_output), :968-991 (validate_launch_policy)\", \"evidence\": \"validate_launch_policy only checks `output_byte_limit <= max_output_bytes`; RuntimeSession never stores output_byte_limit, and both launch (lines 563,567) and poll_output (lines 715,722,723) use self.config.max_output_bytes for redaction/byte_count/truncation, so a smaller per-launch limit is ignored.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Store policy.output_byte_limit in RuntimeSession at launch; compute an effective limit = min(session_limit, config.max_output_bytes) and use it in redact_terminal_projection, byte_count, read_pty max bytes, and TerminalOutputChunk.truncated for launch and poll_output.\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs:1011-1035 (redact_terminal_projection)\", \"evidence\": \"The function does literal `projected.replace(needle, replacement)` for prefixes like \\\"Authorization: Bearer\\\"->\\\"Authorization: [redacted]\\\", \\\"ghp_\\\"->\\\"[redacted]\\\", \\\"sk-\\\"->\\\"[redacted]\\\"; the credential value following the prefix (e.g. the bearer token after the marker) is left intact in the output.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the literal substring list with regex/token-aware redaction that consumes the whole credential value up to a delimiter (whitespace/newline/quote), case-insensitive for headers and ENV=value assignments; redact full token shapes (ghp_/gho_/xoxb-/sk- followed by [A-Za-z0-9_-]+). Add tests for bearer headers, ENV assignments, and mixed-case headers.\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs:243-318 (DapAdapterFixtureRuntime::step); legion-protocol DapClientState\", \"evidence\": \"No `DapClientRuntime` type or `client()`/`client_mut()` accessors exist anywhere in the repo (grep finds them only in the review). The actual DapAdapterFixtureRuntime::step validates session_id and returns DapAdapterFixtureError::Denied for empty input with no panic, and DapClientState methods (prepare_launch/prepare_threads) return Results, verified by test dap_client_state_machine_rejects_lifecycle_mistakes asserting .is_err().\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs:729-734 (poll_output), :783-788 (close), :824-829 (kill) vs :677,:684-689 (resize next_sequence)\", \"evidence\": \"poll_output, close, and kill pass request.event_sequence/request.correlation_id/request.causality_id directly into audit_record, whereas resize uses session_for_lifecycle()->next_sequence() and the session-owned correlation/causality; input also uses next_sequence() for the sequence.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In poll_output/close/kill, obtain the event_sequence (and session-owned correlation/causality) via session_for_lifecycle/next_sequence() instead of trusting the request fields; treat caller correlation_id only as validated request metadata, or document why externally supplied identity is authoritative.\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-terminal/src/lib.rs:776-782 (close), :802-816 (kill), :914-940 (platform_session_id/remove_session)\", \"evidence\": \"close()/kill() call platform_session_id() (locks, clones id, drops lock), then run the backend op, then remove_session() reacquires the lock; with &self methods a concurrent input() can fetch the same platform id between the backend op and removal. No Closing/Killing state guards the window.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Hold the registry lock across the lifecycle transition or add a per-session state (Closing/Killing) set under the lock before the backend call so concurrent input/resize/poll return a stable structured error; remove/mark the session atomically before irreversible terminate.\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs:5236-5287 (parse_terminal_shell_output), :6039-6071 (push_terminal_output)\", \"evidence\": \"No `TerminalSessionMetadata::apply_shell_projection` exists. Current code parses exit_code into a fresh local TerminalShellOutputProjection per chunk and only emits a 'command block finished' row when exit_code is present and a command is active (lines 6056-6070); exit_code is never persisted as session metadata, so there is no stale-exit-code retention.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs:5243-5280 (parse_terminal_shell_output inner loop)\", \"evidence\": \"On encountering ESC ] the loop scans for BEL/ST; if none is found cursor advances to bytes.len() and the remainder is taken as `sequence` (line 5256) and never appended to visible_output, so an unterminated/split OSC drops all trailing bytes; the parser is stateless across calls.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"When no terminator is found, either emit the unterminated bytes (from ESC]) back into visible_output, or make the parser hold a per-session carry-over buffer that prepends leftover bytes to the next chunk so split OSC sequences complete. Add tests for unterminated OSC and terminator-in-next-chunk.\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/src/lib.rs:5289-5294 (terminal_shell_cwd_from_osc)\", \"evidence\": \"The helper strips \\\"file://\\\", takes everything after the first '/' (split_once('/').1) and returns format!(\\\"/{}\\\", ...) with no percent-decoding; `file:///C:/Users` becomes \\\"/C:/Users\\\" (mangled drive) and `My%20Project` stays encoded.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Parse the OSC 7 value with a URL-aware approach: handle the host segment, percent-decode each path segment, and special-case Windows drive letters (file:///C:/...) and UNC (file://server/share) paths. Add Windows-path tests.\", \"review_file\": \"terminal.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/apply_activation.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file does not exist)\", \"evidence\": \"Glob of crates/legion-app/tests/*.rs does not list apply_activation.rs and `git log --all -- crates/legion-app/tests/apply_activation.rs` returns nothing; the file never existed in this repo.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_contracts.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_contracts.rs:264-298\", \"evidence\": \"The predicate `token.end_col <= rust_slashes || token.start_col > rust_slashes` (lines 272-273, mirrored at 294-295) is satisfied by a comment token starting at the second slash (start_col = rust_slashes+1 > rust_slashes), so a bogus comment marking string content still passes.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In daily_editing_contracts_*_string_delimiter_not_comment, replace the per-token predicate with an overlap rejection over the full delimiter span: for Rust assert no Comment token where `token.start_col < rust_slashes + 2 && token.end_col > rust_slashes`; for TOML use `token.start_col <= toml_hash && token.end_col > toml_hash`.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_contracts.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_contracts.rs:17-28, 301\", \"evidence\": \"`create_root()` returns a bare PathBuf and each test ends with `let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root);` (e.g. line 301); a panic before that line leaks the temp workspace, and there is no Drop guard.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Introduce a `TempWorkspace` struct wrapping the PathBuf with a `Drop` impl that does a prefix-checked `remove_dir_all` (matching daily_editing_search.rs), have create_root return it, and drop the manual remove_dir_all calls.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_search.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/daily_editing_search.rs:237-242\", \"evidence\": \"`std::process::Command::new(\\\"git\\\").arg(\\\"init\\\")...status().expect(\\\"git init should run\\\")` only verifies the process spawned; the returned ExitStatus is discarded so a failed `git init` lets the test continue in a non-repo.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Bind the status (`let status = ...output()`), assert `status.status.success()` including stdout/stderr in the message, or skip the test with an explicit precondition when git is unavailable.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/delegated_task_integration.rs\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/delegated_task_integration.rs:56-79\", \"evidence\": \"acp_host_command is now `#[cfg(windows)]` returning powershell (line 57-67) and `#[cfg(not(windows))]` returning `/bin/sh` (line 69-79); /bin/sh is platform-gated, not hard-coded for all targets.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/delegated_task_integration.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/delegated_task_integration.rs:81-88\", \"evidence\": \"`temp_workspace` returns a bare PathBuf with no Drop guard; tests at lines 113 (waiting-plan) and 207 (approved-plan) never call remove_dir_all, so they leak even on success (the review's claim that only ACP-host cleans up is now partly stale since hunk/chat also remove at 436/491).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Return a Drop-guarded temp directory (or tempfile::TempDir) from temp_workspace so all paths clean up uniformly, removing the ad-hoc remove_dir_all calls.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/git_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/git_workflow.rs:23-41, 69-83\", \"evidence\": \"TempGitRepo::new() unconditionally runs `run_git(&root, [\\\"init\\\"])` etc., and run_git does `.expect(\\\"git command should run\\\")`; there is no `git --version` precondition or skip path, so a missing git binary surfaces as a product test failure.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a once-checked helper (e.g. a lazy `git_available()` running `git --version`) and either `eprintln!` + early-return-skip or panic with an explicit environment diagnostic before TempGitRepo::new spawns git.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/git_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/git_workflow.rs:320-324 (and 426, 576, 688, 812)\", \"evidence\": \"Each conflict setup does `let _ = Command::new(\\\"git\\\").args([\\\"merge\\\",\\\"feature\\\"]).output().expect(\\\"git merge command should run\\\");` \\u2014 the ExitStatus and stdout/stderr are discarded; only a later app-level `!projection.conflicts.is_empty()` assertion runs.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Capture the merge Output, assert `!output.status.success()` (merge should fail with conflicts) and/or that `git diff --name-only --diff-filter=U` lists the target file, including stdout/stderr in the assertion message, before opening the app.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/language_terminal_integration.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/language_terminal_integration.rs:219-237\", \"evidence\": \"The test sends TerminalInput, does a single TerminalOutputPoll, then asserts `!terminal.output_rows.is_empty()` (line 237); the fixture uses a real PTY (`TerminalRuntime::new(..., NativePtyService)` at lib.rs:5363) so output is genuinely asynchronous and one poll can race on a slow host.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the single poll with a bounded poll loop (a shared poll_until helper) that re-dispatches TerminalOutputPoll until output_rows contains the expected row or a generous deadline elapses, emitting the final projection on timeout.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/language_tooling_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/language_tooling_workflow.rs:110-150, 228-306\", \"evidence\": \"No test writes a `traversal_target` outside the workspace; grep for traversal/outside/`../`/parent() returns no matches, and the cited tests write only `root.join(\\\"lib.rs\\\")` / `root.join(\\\"main.rs\\\")` inside the workspace root.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/legion_workflow_integration.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/legion_workflow_integration.rs:265-275\", \"evidence\": \"`temp_workspace` builds `current_dir()/target/legion-workflow-integration/{label}-{id}` and returns a bare PathBuf; cleanup is manual `let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(root);` only at lines 503/790/917, so panics or other callers leak under the crate target dir.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Root the fixture in std::env::temp_dir() and return a Drop-guarded wrapper (or tempfile::TempDir) that removes the specific generated workspace, decoupling from process current_dir.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/palette.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/palette.rs:528-532\", \"evidence\": \"Coverage is computed as `(resolved_cases as f32 / 13.0) * 100.0` with the failure message also hard-coding `/13`; the denominator is a literal matching the manually maintained 13-element `cases` array, not the registered command catalog.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Use `cases.len()` as the denominator and additionally derive the expected set from the registered command catalog, asserting every registered command kind has a corresponding case and emitting a catalog-vs-cases diff on failure.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/plugin_grammar.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/plugin_grammar.rs:37-43\", \"evidence\": \"The manifest declares `artifact_uri: \\\"file:///tmp/rust-plugin-grammar.wasm\\\"` but the test only asserts tree_sitter_supports_language and that parsing succeeds; the .wasm artifact is never created or validated for existence/loadability.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Either write a real fixture artifact and assert the loader validates/loads it, or rename the test to make clear it only checks metadata registration and add a separate artifact-validation test.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/terminal_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/terminal_workflow.rs:140-160 (and 231-247)\", \"evidence\": \"The poll loop is `for _ in 0..20 { ...; std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(25)); }`, a fixed ~500ms ceiling; although it breaks on the condition, the deadline is short and can be exceeded by real PTY startup on loaded CI.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Extract a reusable poll_until helper with a generous deadline (e.g. several seconds) that re-polls until the exact condition holds and reports the last terminal projection on timeout; replace both fixed 0..20 loops with it.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/terminal_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/terminal_workflow.rs:75 (test body)\", \"evidence\": \"Grep for `eprintln`/`println!` across terminal_workflow.rs returns no matches; the diagnostic print in terminal_fixture_lifecycle_projects_status has been removed.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/terminal_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/terminal_workflow.rs:9-17, 70-71\", \"evidence\": \"`create_root()` returns a bare PathBuf and tests clean up with `std::fs::remove_dir_all(&root).ok();` (lines 70-71) with no Drop guard and no prefix/pid safety check before deletion, so panics leak temp roots.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Wrap the root in a Drop-guard struct that performs a prefix-checked (legion-terminal-workflow- + pid) remove_dir_all on drop, and remove the manual cleanup calls.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/workspace_vfs_integration.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/workspace_vfs_integration.rs:2375-2377, 3028-3030\", \"evidence\": \"Off-workspace fixtures use `format!(\\\"legion-escape-{}.txt\\\", TEMP_ROOT_COUNTER.load(Ordering::Relaxed))` / `legion-outside-{}` placed in `root.parent()` (the shared temp_dir); `.load` does not increment and the name omits pid/timestamp, so parallel processes or reruns can collide in the shared parent.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Build the off-workspace name from the same unique suffix as the root (pid + timestamp + `TEMP_ROOT_COUNTER.fetch_add`) or a fresh UUID, and manage the outside fixture with a Drop cleanup guard instead of `.load` + manual remove_file.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/tests/tools_schema.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file does not exist)\", \"evidence\": \"legion-agent contains only Cargo.toml and src/lib.rs (no tests/ dir); grep for tools_schema/registry/schema tests in legion-agent/src/lib.rs returns nothing and git log shows no such test file ever existed.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 19\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-agent/tests/worktree_sandbox.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file does not exist)\", \"evidence\": \"No crates/legion-agent/tests/ directory exists and grep for worktree_sandbox/source_root returns no matches in legion-agent; the sandbox logic lives only in src/lib.rs with an inline test, not the cited file.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"tests---app-&-agent.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/beta_acceptance_e2e.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/beta_acceptance_e2e.rs:280-364\", \"evidence\": \"Sections 2/5/6/7 instantiate local fixture structs (approved_vsix_manifest() L89, proposal_context_manifest_fixture() L137, proposal_diff_fixture() L148, test_verification_run_fixture() L166) and assert on their own field values (L282-364) rather than driving any plugin/proposal/verification surface; only debug (L377) and collaboration (L466) sections drive the runtime.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add workflow-level coverage: load the VSIX manifest fixture through the production plugin/runtime path (e.g. runtime.load_plugin_manifest / install bridge) and assert projected install state; open proposal context manifest and diff via the bridge/view model from a real proposal; record a verification run through the app/runtime path. Keep the struct-shape asserts as separate fixture tests.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/beta_acceptance_e2e.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/beta_acceptance_e2e.rs:245-248,520-527\", \"evidence\": \"No-bypass checks are pure substring tests: `!report.proposal_status.contains(\\\"apply\\\")` (L246) and `!report.proposal_status.contains(\\\"autonomous\\\")` (L525), against a human-readable status string.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add structured fields to the beta report (e.g. proposal lifecycle enum, allowed-action set, approval-gate state) and assert those instead of/in addition to status text; assert the projected command/action model contains no autonomous-apply command rather than matching substrings on prose.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/beta_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/beta_workflow.rs:91-100,117,139-142\", \"evidence\": \"Key assertions are substring checks: edit_save_status.contains(\\\"saved\\\") L91, terminal_status.contains(\\\"denied\\\") L92, proposal_status.contains(\\\"preview\\\") L93, error.contains(\\\"blocked\\\") L117, error.contains(\\\"failed\\\")/\\\"status: failed\\\" L139-141.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Expose typed enums/fields in BetaWorkflowReport (save outcome, terminal policy decision, proposal mode) and typed error variants for blocked/failed, and assert those; retain text asserts only for the markdown evidence formatting after structured state is verified.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/breakpoint_hit.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/breakpoint_hit.rs:49\", \"evidence\": \"After creating a Cargo crate, the test calls `runtime.enable_debug_fixture_for_tests()` (L49) then asserts fixture-projected Paused status (L90-91), breakpoints, frames, variables and console rows (L94-141); no real DAP/cargo launch is exercised.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Keep this fixture test for UI projection, and add a separate gated integration test using a protocol-level fake DAP server (or real adapter) that verifies launch request, breakpoint binding, stopped event, stack frame, and variables derived from actual protocol events.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/collaboration_gui.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/collaboration_gui.rs:334-385\", \"evidence\": \"Test calls `runtime.enable_local_collaboration_runtime()` (L345-347) and asserts Joined/PresencePublished status transitions and projected session rows (L353-385); no real transport, remote peer update, or conflict payload is exercised.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a loopback/fake collaboration transport test that feeds remote presence/conflict/proposal events through the production ingestion path and asserts projected rows plus local buffer immutability.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/control_trust_bridge.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/control_trust_bridge.rs:330-343\", \"evidence\": \"desktop_control_trust_bridge_preserves_projection_only_boundary reads src/bridge.rs and src/view.rs as text (L332-334) and asserts raw `!source.contains(\\\"WorkspaceProposal\\\"/\\\"ProviderRouter\\\"/\\\"WorkspaceActor\\\"/\\\"EditorEngine\\\")` (L337-340).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace source-text scan with dependency-level enforcement (cargo metadata/guppy check that bridge/view modules do not depend on the forbidden crates/modules) or a Rust-token-aware lint; if scans remain, centralize a tokenizing deny-list helper.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/debug_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/debug_workflow.rs:49\", \"evidence\": \"Writes a Cargo project then calls `runtime.enable_debug_fixture_for_tests()` (L49) before refresh/launch/step/evaluate, asserting fixture-projected Paused status and debug rows (L86-148); real DAP lifecycle is not exercised.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Keep as a projection smoke test; add a real-or-fake-DAP integration test validating launch, breakpoint, stopped event, step, evaluate, and error propagation from the protocol layer.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/diagnostics_harness.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"No file crates/legion-desktop/tests/diagnostics_harness.rs exists in the worktree or in git history (`git log -- diagnostics_harness.rs` empty; Glob finds nothing), and no buffer_id/URI diagnostics happy-path harness test was found elsewhere in legion-desktop/tests.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Locate the current diagnostics harness (the cited file no longer exists); if diagnostics-ingestion tests exist under another name, add negative cases (mismatched URI/buffer, invalid ranges, missing fields, sensitive text) and assert rejection/sanitization and that unrelated buffers are not cleared.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/headless_input.rs\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/headless_input.rs:34-41\", \"evidence\": \"headless_input_test_guard now matches on lock() and recovers poisoning: `Err(poisoned) => poisoned.into_inner()` (L39), with a comment explaining it prevents cascade failures; no `lock().unwrap()` remains.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/intent_bridge.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/intent_bridge.rs:1012-1020\", \"evidence\": \"intent_bridge_preserves_app_boundary reads src/bridge.rs (L1014) and asserts raw `!source.contains(\\\"AppComposition\\\"/\\\"WorkspaceActor\\\"/\\\"EditorEngine\\\")` (L1017-1019).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace with dependency-level enforcement (cargo metadata/guppy) or a Rust-aware lint forbidding legion_app/app-authority symbols in the bridge module instead of raw substring scanning.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/language_terminal_workflow.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/language_terminal_workflow.rs:224-233\", \"evidence\": \"Reads src/bridge.rs and src/view.rs (L225-228) and asserts raw `!source.contains(\\\"AppComposition\\\"/\\\"legion_terminal\\\"/\\\"TerminalRuntime<\\\")` (L230-232).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Enforce the boundary via dependency-graph/cargo metadata checks or a token-aware lint; keep this workflow test focused on observable bridge outputs and projection state.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/palette.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-app/tests/palette.rs:462-531\", \"evidence\": \"The cited desktop file palette_coverage.rs does not exist; the actual coverage test lives in crates/legion-app/tests/palette.rs which increments `resolved_cases` over a fixed `cases` array (L379,L462-525) and computes `(resolved_cases as f32 / 13.0) * 100.0` with a hard-coded denominator (L528,L531).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Derive the denominator and expected cases from the real command catalog/registry, or iterate the catalog and assert every command appears in the test-case table; remove the hard-coded 13.0. Note: file path in the finding is wrong (it is in legion-app, not legion-desktop).\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/platform_smoke.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/platform_smoke.rs:135-164\", \"evidence\": \"platform_smoke_report_writes_evidence_file builds a temp dir named only by process id `legion_desktop_platform_smoke_{process::id()}` (L137-140) and cleans up manually at the end (L156-163) with no nanos/counter and no Drop guard, so a panic before L156 leaves stale state.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Use the nanos+counter temp naming pattern used by other tests and a Drop-guard (or tempfile) for cleanup so cleanup runs even on panic and names cannot collide across runs in the same process-id namespace.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/platform_smoke.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/platform_smoke.rs:229-233\", \"evidence\": \"platform_smoke_adapter_paths_route_without_metrics_payloads reads src/metrics.rs (L229) and asserts the broad raw substrings `!source.contains(\\\"pub payload\\\")`, `\\\"pub text\\\"`, and `\\\"String,\\\"` (L231-233), which is not tied to any metrics payload API.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Assert against the exported metrics/report struct definitions or a serialized-evidence schema snapshot; if specific payload fields must be forbidden use a Rust-aware structural check rather than the `String,` raw substring.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/plugin_management.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/plugin_management.rs:79-257\", \"evidence\": \"plugin_management.rs contains no signed-extension/grammar test and no `file:///tmp/rust-plugin-grammar.wasm` URI (grep empty; tests are command-routing/quota at L133-257). The hard-coded grammar URI lives in crates/legion-app/tests/plugin_grammar.rs:40, but that test actually drives the real load+parse path (AppComposition::load_plugin_manifest then TreeSitterParser::parse, L85-104), contradicting the 'only assert rendered row strings' claim.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/projection_rendering.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/projection_rendering.rs:1579-1584\", \"evidence\": \"projection_rendering_tests_preserve_app_boundary reads src/view.rs (L1580) and asserts raw `!source.contains(\\\"legion_app\\\")` and `!source.contains(\\\"AppComposition\\\")` (L1583-1584).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Enforce the renderer dependency boundary with cargo metadata/guppy or a Rust-aware lint; reserve this test file for rendering/projection behavior assertions.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/remote_workspace_gui.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/remote_workspace_gui.rs:327-383\", \"evidence\": \"remote_workspace_gui_workflow_reports_connect_without_local_mutation calls `runtime.enable_remote_development_runtime()` (L339-341) then asserts a Connected projection and descriptor row labels (L348-371); no real transport handshake, reconnect/offline, or proposal sync is driven.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a loopback/fake remote backend test driving connect, reconnect/offline, terminal descriptor, LSP descriptor, and remote proposal events through the production ingestion path, then assert GUI rows and local buffer immutability.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/save_all_conflict.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-desktop/tests/save_all_conflict.rs:273-278\", \"evidence\": \"save_all_conflict_desktop_save_paths_dispatch_ui_intent uses `include_str!(\\\"../src/workflow.rs\\\")` and asserts the source `contains(\\\"dispatch_ui_intent\\\")` and `!contains(\\\"save_file_with_proposal\\\")` (L275-277).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace with a behavior test that injects a spy/mock app authority and asserts save/close/save-all commands always dispatch UI intents (and never a proposal-apply save), or enforce the forbidden call with a Rust-aware lint.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---desktop.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/smoke.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file absent)\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/ contains only mcp_ga_conformance.rs and prompt_stability.rs; smoke.rs does not exist anywhere in the repo and has no git history on this branch. No hosted-Anthropic smoke test could be located.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cited file is not present in the current tree, so the described defect cannot be confirmed. If a hosted live-smoke test is reintroduced, gate it behind an explicit live-only/ignored target that fails when credentials are expected but missing.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/mcp_ga_conformance.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/mcp_ga_conformance.rs:235-285, 444-446\", \"evidence\": \"spawn_http_fixture spawns a thread with `for _ in 0..4 { listener.accept().expect(...) }` and read_http_request_json loops on stream.read with no read/accept timeout; the test unconditionally calls handle.join() at line 444. Fewer than four client requests or an early client failure leaves accept()/read blocked forever and hangs join().\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In spawn_http_fixture set listener and per-stream read timeouts (listener.set_nonblocking or stream.set_read_timeout) and/or return a shutdown channel; replace the fixed `for _ in 0..4` with accept-until-closed bounded by a timeout, and make join() time-bounded so an early client failure surfaces as an assertion rather than a hang.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/mcp_ga_conformance.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ai-providers/tests/mcp_ga_conformance.rs:167 and 588\", \"evidence\": \"stdio_transport (line 167) and stdio_pid_transport (line 588) both construct StdioMcpTransportConfig { command: \\\"python3\\\".to_string(), ... }, hard-coding python3 as an external runtime dependency for these tests.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the python3 fixture with a Cargo-built Rust fixture binary referenced via env!(\\\"CARGO_BIN_EXE_...\\\"), or discover the interpreter through a workspace toolchain variable and skip with an explicit diagnostic in a clearly optional smoke test.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-lsp/tests/stdio_transport_contract.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-lsp/tests/stdio_transport_contract.rs:399-410\", \"evidence\": \"rust_analyzer_initializes_against_legion_repo_when_opted_in returns early (eprintln + return) when LEGION_RUN_RUST_ANALYZER_SMOKE != \\\"1\\\" (line 401-404) and again returns when `rust-analyzer --version` is unavailable (line 407-410), so the real-server launch path is never exercised in default CI.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Convert to an `#[ignore]` live-smoke target run by a dedicated CI job that sets LEGION_RUN_RUST_ANALYZER_SMOKE=1 and treats a missing rust-analyzer binary as a hard failure rather than a silent return.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-lsp/tests/stdio_transport_contract.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-lsp/tests/stdio_transport_contract.rs:544-705\", \"evidence\": \"Inside the rust-analyzer smoke, projected responses are bound to unused underscore vars with no assertions: _completion_rows (544), _hover (554), _definitions (566), _references (578), _locations (590,602,614), _signature_help (626), _outline (637), _workspace_symbols (648), _hints (672), _lenses (683), _folding_ranges (694), _semantic_tokens (705). The test only proves requests do not error.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add non-empty/key-field assertions for each projected surface (e.g. assert completion contains an Alpha entry, hover label non-empty, definition/reference ranges resolve to lib.rs), or narrow the test to the surfaces that can be validated deterministically.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/tests/hostile.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file absent)\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-plugin has no tests/ directory at all (only Cargo.toml and src/); hostile.rs and its compile_fixture helper do not exist anywhere in the repo and have no git history on this branch.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cited file is not present, so the leak cannot be confirmed. If hostile-plugin tests are reintroduced, have compile_fixture return a tempfile::TempDir-owned path so the wasm artifact is deleted on drop.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-plugin/tests/quotas.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A (file absent)\", \"evidence\": \"crates/legion-plugin has no tests/ directory; quotas.rs and its write_fixture_wasm helper do not exist in the repo and have no git history on this branch.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cited file is not present, so the leak cannot be confirmed. If quota tests are reintroduced, use an RAII temp dir/named temp file retained only while WasmPluginHost::load_fixture needs the path.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs:345-416\", \"evidence\": \"The cited large_file_streaming.rs no longer exists, but large_file_100mb_degraded_mode_measurement (line 345 `#[test]`, no `#[ignore]`) sets `let size = 100 * 1024 * 1024;` and builds deterministic_large_text(size) on every default run, so an ordinary `cargo test` allocates and opens 100 MiB.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add `#[ignore = \\\"performance suite: 100MB\\\"]` to large_file_100mb_degraded_mode_measurement (and any sibling 100MiB cases) so the heavy allocation only runs in a dedicated perf job, keeping a smaller deterministic default test for degraded-mode behavior.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs:346-416\", \"evidence\": \"large_file_100mb_degraded_mode_measurement computes p50/p95 (lines 398-399) and eprintln!s open/viewport/edit latencies (405-411) but its only assertions are mode==DegradedLargeFile, payload_bytes < budget/32, and chunks.len()>1 (413-415); no latency budget is asserted, so perf regressions pass.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add explicit budget assertions for open_elapsed, viewport_elapsed and edit p50/p95 in this test, or rename/split it into a report-only measurement excluded from the pass/fail suite.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-editor/tests/performance_suite.rs:683-685, 720-722\", \"evidence\": \"undo_redo_latency_under_edit_burst carries `#[ignore = \\\"performance suite: undo/redo latency\\\"]` (line 684) and snapshot_retention_and_release carries `#[ignore = \\\"performance suite: snapshot retention\\\"]` (line 721), so default CI never exercises these latency/retention checks.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Schedule these in a named performance CI job (cargo test -- --ignored) or add smaller deterministic non-ignored variants for default runs while keeping the heavy benchmarks ignored.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-project/tests/search_workspace.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-project/tests/search_workspace.rs:155-159\", \"evidence\": \"indexed_workspace_search_refreshes_after_file_changes overwrites the file then does `sleep(Duration::from_millis(120))` (line 156) before poll_watcher_events; the fixed sleep is timing-sensitive and can flake on slow runners or pass spuriously on fast ones.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Replace the fixed sleep with a bounded retry loop polling poll_watcher_events until the modification/invalidation is observed (with an overall timeout), or expose a deterministic watcher-flush synchronization point on WorkspaceActor.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-project/tests/search_workspace.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-project/tests/search_workspace.rs:168-170\", \"evidence\": \"indexed_workspace_search_benchmark_large_fixture is annotated `#[ignore]` (line 169) and writes 500 files; default test runs do not validate large-workspace indexed search.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Run the ignored benchmark in a named perf job, or add a smaller non-ignored coverage test (e.g. a few dozen files) validating indexed vs live equivalence for larger fixtures.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-project/tests/watcher_recovery.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-project/tests/watcher_recovery.rs:120\", \"evidence\": \"watcher_recovery_overflow_then_rescan_emits_recovery_event uses the deterministic OverflowThenOkWatcher mock yet calls `std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(80))` (line 120) between the overflow poll and the recovery poll.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Remove the 80 ms sleep if recovery is synchronous after poll, or replace it with a bounded poll loop that retries poll_watcher_events until the Modified recovery event appears.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-project/tests/path_boundary.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-project/tests/path_boundary.rs:163, 276/345/367/383/433/470/507/537/563/583/608-609\", \"evidence\": \"create_temp_workspace returns a bare PathBuf (line 163) and each test ends with `let _ = std::fs::remove_dir_all(root);` (and at line 608 also removes the outside symlink target). A panic before these lines leaks the temp dir and the outside fixture; there is no Drop guard.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Introduce an RAII TempWorkspace struct owning the root (and any outside fixture paths) whose Drop calls remove_dir_all/remove_file, replacing create_temp_workspace() -> PathBuf and the manual cleanup lines.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote/tests/cloud_lane_http_transport.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote/tests/cloud_lane_http_transport.rs:135-144\", \"evidence\": \"serve_one's thread does a single `let mut buf = [0u8; 4096]; let n = stream.read(&mut buf)` (lines 137-138) then treats buf[..n] as the whole request; TCP can split larger/segmented requests across reads, truncating before the header/body assertions.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In serve_one read until the \\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n header terminator, parse Content-Length, then read the full body (mirroring read_http_request_json in mcp_ga_conformance.rs), with a read timeout to avoid hangs.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-remote/tests/cloud_lane_http_transport.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-remote/tests/cloud_lane_http_transport.rs:129-146, 293-344\", \"evidence\": \"serve_one returns only a URL String (no join/shutdown handle) and spawns a thread blocking in listener.accept(); the before-network rejection tests (http_transport_disabled_policy_rejects_before_network l.294, forbidden_upload l.314, cost_cap l.329) all call serve_one with a panic handler, leaving the listener thread stuck in accept() until process exit.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"For before-network rejection tests do not spawn a listener at all (use an invalid base_url or a transport mock recording whether it was called). Where a listener is genuinely needed, change serve_one to return a join handle plus shutdown signal and shut it down deterministically.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/tests/docs_hygiene.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/tests/docs_hygiene.rs:44-49\", \"evidence\": \"placeholder_docs_hygiene_test_file_compiles only does `repo.write(\\\"README.md\\\", ...)` then `assert!(repo.path(\\\"README.md\\\").exists())`; it never calls run_docs_hygiene, so it exercises no docs-hygiene logic.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Delete the placeholder test, or replace its body with a real run_docs_hygiene(&repo.root, &DocsHygieneConfig::default()) assertion.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"error\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/tests/docs_hygiene.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/tests/docs_hygiene.rs:302-318\", \"evidence\": \"docs_hygiene_checks_untracked_markdown_in_git_repo runs `Command::new(\\\"git\\\").arg(\\\"init\\\")...output().expect(\\\"git init should run\\\")` (302-306) and the git add (312-318) but never checks output.status.success(); if git fails the test proceeds against a non-git directory and no longer validates untracked-file detection.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Capture each Command output and assert output.status.success(), printing stdout/stderr on failure (as other git fixture helpers do) before asserting the untracked NEW.md violation.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 19\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"stub\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/tests/perf_harness.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/tests/perf_harness.rs:148-182\", \"evidence\": \"perf_harness_unreachable_budget_marks_measurement_failed sets budget_millis=0 and only asserts `assert_ne!(measurement.status, SkeletonStatus::Failed)` (line 162); perf_harness_tight_budget_classifies_measurement_failed also sets budget 0, asserts status==Skipped (179) and merely references `let _ = SkeletonStatus::Failed;` (181). Neither asserts a Failed measurement, so the failure-classification path is untested despite the names.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a deterministic helper/fixture that produces a measurement whose elapsed exceeds its budget (e.g. inject a recorded elapsed time) and assert measurement.status == SkeletonStatus::Failed plus the expected failure message, instead of asserting Skipped.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 20\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/tests/perf_harness.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/tests/perf_harness.rs:184-209\", \"evidence\": \"perf_harness_fail_on_budget_env_overrides_descriptor_budget mutates process-global env via `unsafe { std::env::set_var(FAIL_ON_BUDGET_ENV, \\\"0\\\") }` (192-194) and restore set_var/remove_var (202-207) with only a comment claiming single-thread safety; cargo runs integration tests concurrently, so another test reading FAIL_ON_BUDGET_ENV can race this mutation.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Serialize env-mutating tests with a global Mutex or the serial_test attribute, or refactor apply_fail_on_budget_override to accept an injected env value so the test sets no process-global variable.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 21\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/tests/release_pipeline.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/tests/release_pipeline.rs:19-24\", \"evidence\": \"TempRepo::new builds its root from `name` plus `SystemTime::now()...as_nanos()` only (lines 20-24); there is no process id or atomic counter, so parallel/rapid same-name construction can collide when clock granularity is coarser than nanoseconds.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Include std::process::id() and a static AtomicU64 counter (as docs_hygiene/path_boundary fixtures do) in the temp dir name to guarantee uniqueness.\", \"review_file\": \"tests---remaining-crates.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/projection.rs\", \"verdict\": \"UNCERTAIN\", \"current_location\": \"N/A\", \"evidence\": \"The cited file crates/legion-ui/src/projection.rs does not exist (legion-ui has only lib.rs and ui.rs), and the function legion_workflow_fleet_card_projections appears nowhere in the source tree nor in git history. The actual proposal-card rendering (render_proposal_cards in crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs:3259) does not attach any per-proposal verification/test_status label at all.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Cannot validate: cited file and function do not exist in the current tree or git history. If a per-proposal verification status feature is later added, ensure verification rows are joined to their owning proposal id rather than projecting a single global aggregate onto every card.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs:3367-3414\", \"evidence\": \"Shell::render starts with print!(\\\"\\\\x1b[2J\\\\x1b[H\\\") then emits untrusted content verbatim: println!(\\\"{}\\\", text) for buffer text, println!(\\\"{}\\\", slice.visible_text) per viewport line, println!(\\\"Path: {}\\\", path), tab titles, prompts, debug frames, etc., with zero control-character escaping.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a sanitization helper (strip/escape C0/C1 control chars and ESC sequences, e.g. replace bytes < 0x20 except newline/tab and 0x7f-0x9f) and route every untrusted projection string (visible_text, file_path, tab titles, prompt.message, debug labels, terminal rows) through it before println!. Add tests feeding ANSI/control payloads in buffer text and paths.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs:4731-4742\", \"evidence\": \"In parse_pos the viewport branch accumulates current_offset from slice.visible_text.len()+1 starting at 0, compares against byte_offset, and returns protocol_text_coordinate(line, character, Some(byte_offset as u64)); it never consults slice.byte_range.start, so the returned byte offset is viewport-relative rather than absolute.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In the viewport loop, when the target slice is found compute the absolute offset as slice.byte_range.start + (byte_offset - current_offset), validate it lies within [slice.byte_range.start, slice.byte_range.end], and return that as byte_offset; reject offsets that fall outside any visible slice instead of falling through to (0,0).\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs:4719-4728\", \"evidence\": \"parse_pos small-buffer branch uses text.as_bytes().get(..byte_offset) and on None does unwrap_or_else(|| protocol_text_coordinate(0,0,Some(0))); a byte_offset past end silently coerces to file start. (Note: byte-slice get does not reject mid-codepoint offsets, so the char-boundary case is silently mis-counted rather than fallback.)\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Before slicing, validate byte_offset <= text.len() and text.is_char_boundary(byte_offset); if either fails, return a command/validation error (or Noop) rather than coercing to (0,0,0). Add the same char-boundary guard to the viewport branch.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs:5070-5074\", \"evidence\": \"parse_proposal_id parses u64 and maps to ProposalId with no zero filter, unlike parse_buffer_id (line 4760) which uses .filter(|value| *value != 0). ProposalId(0) is used as a sentinel in empty_approval_checklist_projection (4945) and empty_checkpoint_rollback_projection (4980), so :proposal-approve 0 emits a sentinel-id intent.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add .filter(|value| *value != 0) to parse_proposal_id between parse and map(ProposalId), mirroring parse_buffer_id. Add tests asserting zero/empty proposal ids yield None/Noop.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs:3023-3036, 3005\", \"evidence\": \"toast_id(severity, message) is a pure FNV hash over only the severity byte and message bytes, and ToastProjection::from_status_message sets id: toast_id(message.severity, &message.message); two identical status messages produce identical ids, so dismissing one dismisses all and duplicates collapse.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Incorporate a per-message discriminator (status message index/sequence, timestamp, or source id) into ToastProjection::id while keeping deterministic ids only where dedup is explicitly intended; thread that value through from_status_messages_with_verbosity into from_status_message.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs:1151-1163 (with prepare_batch_edit_plan at 1312-1320)\", \"evidence\": \"prepare_batch_edit_plan sorts ascending then reverses (applied descending); in apply_edits each delta records ByteRange::new(prepared.start, changed_end) using the original/high offset before lower-offset edits are applied, then deltas.reverse(); lower edits that change length shift the higher delta's final position but the recorded range is never adjusted.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Track a running cumulative length delta from already-applied (lower-processed) edits, or recompute each ChangedDelta's byte_range/utf16_range against the final staged_buffer after the loop completes; alternatively accumulate edits ascending and offset previously-recorded ranges by each edit's (new_text.len() - (end-start)).\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs:1866-1891\", \"evidence\": \"set_cursors and set_selections only look up the buffer state then assign state.cursors = cursors / state.selections = selections with no position validation; viewport_projection later calls protocol_range(&state.buffer, selection.range) and state.buffer.try_byte_offset(cursor)? (lines 1044-1046) which return Err for invalid positions, making projection fallible for stored state.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In set_cursors/set_selections, validate every Cursor.position and Selection.range via buffer.try_byte_offset (and start<=end) before storing, returning EditorError on invalid input so only valid editor state is ever persisted.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs:2368-2383\", \"evidence\": \"EditorRequest::ApplyTransaction fetches buffer_metadata, checks workspace_id/file_id match, then returns Ok(EditorResponse::Transaction(descriptor)) with no buffer mutation, no transaction-log append, and no event emission; callers get a success for an unapplied transaction.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Either route this through real mutation (resolve the descriptor's edits/preconditions and call apply_edits with transaction/event recording) or return ProtocolError::unsupported when no mutation occurs; do not return EditorResponse::Transaction for a pure identity check.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs:2424-2426\", \"evidence\": \"EditorRequest::Overlay(overlay) => Ok(EditorResponse::OverlayApplied(overlay.overlay_id)) returns success without ever calling engine.set_overlays (defined at 1894) or otherwise updating any buffer's state.overlays.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add/resolve a buffer id on the overlay request and call engine.set_overlays(buffer_id, ...) (or merge into the target buffer's overlay list) before returning OverlayApplied; if overlays are projection-only, return ProtocolError::unsupported instead.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-editor/src/lib.rs:1671-1677 (error defined at 77, never returned)\", \"evidence\": \"request_save matches try_full_text() and on Err(FullCacheBudgetExceeded) calls snapshot.materialize_full_text_from_chunks()? to build a whole-file String on the interactive path; EditorError::DegradedSaveUnavailable is defined but grep shows it is never returned anywhere, contradicting the viewport message that 'Phase 1 saves fail closed'.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Pick one contract: to fail closed, return EditorError::DegradedSaveUnavailable(buffer_id) in the FullCacheBudgetExceeded arm instead of materializing; to support degraded saves, stream chunks through the save payload without a single String and update the large-file status/error text accordingly.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs:815-825\", \"evidence\": \"LineIndex::visible_line_slices only checks start_line > end_line_exclusive, then does Vec::with_capacity(end_line_exclusive.saturating_sub(start_line)) before the loop where line_slice(line,..)? performs the first bounds check; a huge end_line_exclusive forces a massive allocation before any out-of-bounds error.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Before allocating, validate end_line_exclusive <= self.line_count() (return TextError::LineOutOfBounds or InvalidRange), and/or cap the requested count to a bounded viewport limit; only then Vec::with_capacity over the clamped range.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs:733-745 (caller try_replace_range at 1290-1299)\", \"evidence\": \"rebuild_from_simple_edit only shifts chunk.end_byte/byte_len and recomputes the edited chunk hash, with no comparison against DEFAULT_CHUNK_FORCE_MAX_BYTES (96 KiB) and no split/rebalance; repeated same-line edits can grow a chunk past the advertised bound while staying on the simple-edit fast path.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"After shifting the edited chunk in rebuild_from_simple_edit, if chunk.byte_len > DEFAULT_CHUNK_FORCE_MAX_BYTES return None so try_replace_range falls back to refresh_cache_and_index(rebuild_chunk_index) / rebuild_from_chunk, restoring the bounded-chunk invariant.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-text/src/lib.rs:354-358 and 1108-1112\", \"evidence\": \"TextSnapshot::text() and TextBuffer::text() both call self.try_full_text().expect(\\\"full text cache unavailable; ...\\\"), panicking whenever the bounded full-text cache is absent (large/degraded buffers), despite documentation.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Prefer try_full_text() in production paths; consider renaming the panicking methods (e.g. text_or_panic / #[cfg(test)] gating) or returning Cow via a fallible API so callers must handle the degraded case instead of crashing.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"critical\", \"category\": \"error\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs:419-440 (auth at 579-588)\", \"evidence\": \"handle_transport_envelope only checks sender_participant_id.0 == 0 then forwards CollaborationTransportPayload::Operation(operation) to submit_operation; validate_operation_shape authorizes via self.participant(operation.author_participant_id) and its PublishOperation permission, never comparing envelope.sender_participant_id to operation.author_participant_id (or to projection.participant_id for presence).\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In handle_transport_envelope, for Operation payloads require envelope.sender_participant_id == operation.author_participant_id and for Presence require envelope.sender_participant_id == projection.participant_id, returning InvalidOperation on mismatch before dispatch; add negative tests for sender/payload spoofing.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs:142-161\", \"evidence\": \"The bounds check at line 142 uses participants.len() (pre-dedup), then the loop does participant_map.insert(participant.participant_id, participant) at line 160 with no duplicate detection, so a duplicate id silently overwrites the earlier descriptor including principal/permissions.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In the loop, check participant_map.insert(...).is_some() (or a seen HashSet) and return CollaborationRuntimeError::InvalidParticipant on a duplicate id; after building, assert participant_map.len() == submitted count and apply the max_participants bound to the deduplicated map.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs:267-306 (ordering at 739-773)\", \"evidence\": \"submit_operation only computes expected_sequence from participant_sequences for the author and gaps on that alone; it never validates operation.preconditions.base_vector against accepted sequences. dependencies_satisfied iterates only over `remaining` ops, so a base-vector dependency on another participant's never-accepted sequence is not detected and the op is accepted.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Before acceptance, iterate operation.preconditions.base_vector.entries and for each require self.participant_sequences.get(entry.participant_id) >= entry.sequence; otherwise emit a CollaborationCausalGap / GapDetected (or ResyncRequired) acknowledgement instead of pushing and replaying the operation.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 18\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs:721-817\", \"evidence\": \"deterministic_order only reorders operations and replay_operations/apply_operation apply each operation's original byte_range via replace_range with no transform against prior concurrent inserts/deletes; replace_range only rejects out-of-document ranges (Conflict), so concurrent ops from the same base hit wrong bytes deterministically.\", \"effort\": \"L\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Introduce an OT/CRDT transform step that adjusts each operation's byte range against previously-applied concurrent operations during replay, or constrain acceptance to a strictly linear base version/vector so raw byte ranges remain valid; emit ResyncRequired when a range cannot be safely transformed.\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 19\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs\", \"verdict\": \"ALREADY_FIXED\", \"current_location\": \"crates/legion-collaboration/src/lib.rs:313-322\", \"evidence\": \"In the accepted branch participant_sequences.insert(author_participant_id, participant_sequence) (lines 314-317) runs BEFORE self.acknowledge(...Accepted) (line 318); acknowledge builds observed_vector from self.participant_sequences (662-672), so the Accepted ack already includes the just-accepted sequence.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"ui,-editor-&-collaboration.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/main.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/main.rs:516-520, 527-531, 542-544, 551-553\", \"evidence\": \"All four subcommands declare `#[arg(long, default_value_t = true)] strict: bool` and the doc comments say `Set --no-strict` (e.g. lines 517-520), but no field/action defines `--no-strict`, so strict cannot be turned off.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a negated flag: keep `strict` but add `#[arg(long = \\\"no-strict\\\", action = clap::ArgAction::SetFalse)]` semantics, e.g. `#[arg(long = \\\"strict\\\", overrides_with = \\\"no_strict\\\")] strict: bool` plus `#[arg(long = \\\"no-strict\\\")] no_strict: bool`, then resolve `strict = strict && !no_strict` in main. Add CLI tests for each subcommand.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 2\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/main.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/main.rs:735-789 (run_verify_release_pipeline_command), const at line 32\", \"evidence\": \"VerifyReleasePipeline takes only `out`; the verify command always loads `DEFAULT_RELEASE_PIPELINE_CONFIG_PATH` = `xtask/release-pipeline.example.toml` (line 743) and re-plans, so a custom `--config` used for release-pipeline cannot be verified.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Add a `--config` arg to the VerifyReleasePipeline variant matching ReleasePipeline and thread it into run_verify_release_pipeline_command, OR persist the config path/identity into VersionStamp during write_descriptors and read it back in verify so the plan is reconstructed from the same config.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 3\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/main.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/main.rs:2771-2778 (markdown_section)\", \"evidence\": \"`let start = source.find(heading)?;` matches the heading substring anywhere (prose, code blocks), and termination uses `body.find(\\\"\\\\n## \\\")` ignoring the matched heading's actual level.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Rewrite markdown_section to iterate `source.lines()`, require a line that is an ATX heading (after trim_start starts with '#'+space) whose label equals `heading`, capture its hash-count level, and terminate at the next heading line with level <= matched level.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 4\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs:226-228 (check_markdown_links)\", \"evidence\": \"`let file_relative = file.parent()...join; let root_relative = root.join; if !file_relative.exists() && !root_relative.exists()` accepts a link if it resolves against EITHER the file's parent or the repo root, so a nested broken `README.md` passes because root has README.md.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Resolve normal relative links only against `file.parent()`; drop the `root.join(&normalized)` fallback (the leading-`/` case at line 223 already handles root-relative). If root-relative is desired, require explicit `/`-prefixed syntax.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs:97-99 (run_docs_hygiene loop)\", \"evidence\": \"`let Ok(text) = fs::read_to_string(&path) else { continue; };` silently skips any unreadable tracked markdown file, so the gate fails open.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"On read error, push a new DocsHygieneViolationKind (e.g. UnreadableFile) or accumulate a separate I/O error list and surface it so the command exits non-zero instead of `continue`.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/docs_hygiene.rs:263-269 (is_allowlisted), 275-277 (normalize_allowlist_prefix)\", \"evidence\": \"`rel.starts_with(&prefix)` with normalize that only trims/replaces backslashes means allowlist `docs/foo` also matches `docs/foo-old.md`.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Match on path boundaries: accept only when `rel == prefix` or `rel.starts_with(&format!(\\\"{}/\\\", prefix.trim_end_matches('/')))`.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 7\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/kanban_backlog.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/kanban_backlog.rs:43-44 (#[serde(default)] dependencies), 198 (check_required_fields)\", \"evidence\": \"`dependencies` is `#[serde(default)] pub dependencies: Vec<String>` and check_required_fields returns `\\\"dependencies\\\" => true` (line 198) with comment 'presence of the field is sufficient', so an omitted field passes the required-field gate.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Deserialize `dependencies` (and other required-present fields) without `#[serde(default)]` or as `Option<Vec<String>>`; then in check_required_fields require `task.dependencies.is_some()` to distinguish omitted from empty.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 8\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/legion_bench.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/legion_bench.rs:241-286 (verify_legion_bench_report)\", \"evidence\": \"The verify loop only checks `expected.id != result.task.id` (lines 277-284) and summary.failed/regressed (271-275); it never compares full task equality nor recomputes summary.passed/scores from report.tasks, so tampered scores, summary counts, or non-fingerprinted task fields verify clean.\", \"effort\": \"M\", \"fix_recipe\": \"In the zip loop compare `expected != &result.task` for full equality and reject mismatches; recompute the summary (passed/failed/regressed/scores) from report.tasks statuses and reject if it differs from report.summary.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 9\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"error\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/legion_bench.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/legion_bench.rs:149-192 (plan_default_legion_bench_suite)\", \"evidence\": \"The file is only 474 lines (cited 538-581 do not exist); plan_default_legion_bench_suite builds the suite entirely from hardcoded `fixture_repos`/`kinds` constants with no file/TOML manifest loading and no unwrap/expect, so there is no panic-on-missing-fixture path.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 10\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/legion_bench.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/legion_bench.rs:351-355 (score_task)\", \"evidence\": \"`let tests_passed = budget.require_tests_pass;` then `let passed = tests_passed && ...` means a task with `require_tests_pass = false` forces tests_passed=false and can never pass (the cited `&& exfiltration_blocked` term is gone, but the gating defect remains).\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Compute a separate gate: `let tests_gate = !budget.require_tests_pass || tests_passed_actual;` and use `tests_gate` in the `passed` expression, while still reporting the raw `tests_passed` field if needed.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 11\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/no_egui_textedit.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/no_egui_textedit.rs:75-77 (run_no_egui_textedit loop)\", \"evidence\": \"`let Ok(text) = fs::read_to_string(&path) else { continue; };` silently skips unreadable scanned files, making the forbidden-token gate fail open.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"On read error for a scanned (non-allowlisted) file, push a violation/command error rather than `continue`, so unreadable files cause a non-zero exit.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 12\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/no_egui_textedit.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/no_egui_textedit.rs:237-243 (is_scanned), 245-251 (is_allowlisted), 253-255 (normalize_prefix)\", \"evidence\": \"Both is_scanned and is_allowlisted use `rel.starts_with(&prefix)` with normalize_prefix that only trims/strips `./` and replaces backslashes, so a configured prefix matches sibling paths sharing the byte prefix.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Require boundary match: accept only when `rel == prefix` or `rel.starts_with(&format!(\\\"{}/\\\", prefix.trim_end_matches('/')))` in both is_scanned and is_allowlisted.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 13\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/perf_harness.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/perf_harness.rs:271-415 (plan_perf_harness and workloads)\", \"evidence\": \"The current module (713 lines) has only InputToPaint, LineGalley, RendererBacked, and MemoryCeiling skeletons; there is no large-fixture search benchmark, no scan_limit, and no `module_49999`/`module_99999` queries anywhere, so the described bounded no-hit scan does not exist.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 14\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/perf_harness.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/perf_harness.rs:345-415 (run_input_to_paint / run_line_galley)\", \"evidence\": \"The startup/input-to-paint/scroll workloads are fully synthetic (`vec![b'a'; fixture_bytes]`, generated lines via `format!`); they never read real workspace files, so there is no silent fallback-to-tiny-string behavior to fix.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 15\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/perf_harness.rs\", \"verdict\": \"FALSE_POSITIVE\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/perf_harness.rs:130-187 (descriptor constructors), 821-825 (main.rs hardcoded descriptors)\", \"evidence\": \"Descriptors are built only via hardcoded constructors (m0/m1/m2) with positive sample_counts and are not deserialized from any fixture manifest, so the `sample_count = 0` manifest path is unreachable. A latent gap remains that plan_perf_harness returns Passed for empty samples, but the described loaded-descriptor defect does not apply.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 16\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"bug\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/release_pipeline.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/release_pipeline.rs:189-200 (plan_release_pipeline), 414-417 (build_version_stamp)\", \"evidence\": \"Preview sets descriptor `version = format!(\\\"{workspace_version}-preview\\\")` (line 191, used at 209) but build_version_stamp is called with `&workspace_version` (line 196), so version_stamp.package_version stays the unsuffixed version, mismatching the descriptor version.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Pass the channel-adjusted `&version` (instead of `&workspace_version`) into build_version_stamp at line 196, or add a distinct base-version field if both are needed.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}, {\"finding_id\": \"Finding 17\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"category\": \"failure-point\", \"source_file\": \"xtask/src/release_pipeline.rs\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"current_location\": \"xtask/src/release_pipeline.rs:498-508 (descriptor_file_stem), 255-270 (write_descriptors)\", \"evidence\": \"descriptor_file_stem maps every non-alphanumeric/`-`/`_` char to `-`, so `linux x64` and `linux-x64` both become `linux-x64`; write_descriptors writes `{stem}.toml` (line 256) with no duplicate detection, silently overwriting.\", \"effort\": \"S\", \"fix_recipe\": \"Before writing in write_descriptors, collect computed stems into a HashSet and return an explicit configuration error on collision, or append a stable disambiguator (e.g. index or target) to the filename.\", \"review_file\": \"xtask.md\"}]}\n.\\plans\\evidence\\p0-governance-mutation-path-audit.md:13:- ADR-0015 streaming constraints remain in force: full-source UI projection is limited to explicitly bounded small-buffer mode, and large/degraded buffers use viewport projections.\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-roadmap-v0.1.md:98:**Phase 1 entry criteria:** this phase can begin without waiting for ADR-0013 and ADR-0014 acceptance, but downstream implementation in phases that mutate files/workspace/trust must not start until those ADRs are accepted.\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-roadmap-v0.1.md:139:**Phase 3 entry criteria:** ADR-0013 and ADR-0014 are accepted before persistence-sensitive VFS/tree/watcher semantics are finalized.\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-roadmap-v0.1.md:219:| `legion-lsp` | ADR-0011 accepted before implementation; server lifecycle, transport, supervision, restart policy | trusted workspace can start LSP, untrusted cannot |\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-roadmap-v0.1.md:256:**Phase 10 entry criteria:** ADR-0012 acceptance is required before finalizing plugin runtime crate and plugin capability enforcement.\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-roadmap-v0.1.md:302:- **Path-policy failures [Owner: Platform + Security]:** ADR-0013/ADR-0014 canonicalization and watcher identity regression suites.\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-roadmap-v0.1.md:309:- **Air-gap/network-policy bypass risk [Owner: Security]:** ADR-0010 command and network policy checks integrated by early policy phases.\r\n.\\plans\\foundational-core-ide-platform-roadmap-v0.1.md:337:- **Phase 10:** plugin manifest validation and ADR-0012-driven grants/denials.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:30:The current runnable product is `legion-app`, a CLI shell proof. `crates/legion-app/src/main.rs` opens the current directory as a trusted workspace, accepts an optional file path, and supports only `:w` and `:q` in the interactive loop. This is useful as a composition proof but is not a renderer-backed desktop IDE.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:36:The root workspace has no active `legion-desktop` member and no GUI renderer dependency. The product gap is therefore a desktop adapter and renderer integration, not a rebuild of editor, workspace, save, proposal, policy, telemetry, or provider runtime substrates.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:49:ADR-0002 is accepted with reservations. It points at a native Rust GPU path as the primary direction but still requires renderer-backed p50/p95 input-to-paint, IME, clipboard, focus, and accessibility evidence. SPIKE-001A validated projection-only shell behavior and text-model boundaries, not a real desktop renderer.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:51:There is no `legion-desktop` crate yet. The planned adapter must consume `ShellProjectionSnapshot`, own only renderer/window/native input resources, and route user actions back into app-owned command handling. It must never make renderer state authoritative for editor text, dirty state, proposal lifecycle, workspace persistence, provider execution, retention, telemetry, or plugin/collaboration/remote authority.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:55:`plans/dependency-policy.md` currently describes `legion-ui` as a projection-only crate and forbids hard edges from `legion-ui` to app/editor/project/storage. It does not yet define `legion-desktop`, authorized renderer dependency categories, or a renderer-specific `xtask` gate.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:57:Phase 1 therefore needs a policy and `xtask` update before Phase 2 can add any renderer dependency or desktop crate. The policy must authorize renderer dependencies only in the planned adapter, while `legion-ui` and core crates continue to fail closed if they gain renderer/windowing dependencies or forbidden internal edges.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:61:- ADR-0002 names the accepted renderer path, fallback triggers, and required proof obligations.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:62:- ADR-0030 defines `legion-desktop` as an adapter boundary that may depend on app/UI/protocol and approved renderer crates while core crates do not depend on it.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:63:- `plans/dependency-policy.md` documents the desktop adapter rule and conservative renderer dependency denial for `legion-ui`.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\gui-productization-baseline.md:64:- `xtask` includes a renderer dependency gate preserving the projection boundary.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\p2-1-viewport-non-regression-harness.md:5:Scope: P2.1 only. This note records non-regression coverage for ADR-0015 viewport-first rendering and text snapshot bounded access. It does not mark a broader phase accepted.\r\n.\\plans\\ide-core-architecture-spec-v0.1.md:170:| `legion-lsp` | LSP server lifecycle, JSON-RPC transport, document synchronization, language feature normalization. | ADR-0011 |\r\n.\\plans\\ide-core-architecture-spec-v0.1.md:171:| `legion-plugin` | Plugin registry, manifests, activation events, contribution points, sandboxed runtime adapters. | ADR-0012 |\r\n.\\plans\\ide-core-architecture-spec-v0.1.md:966:| ADR-0011 | Select LSP architecture, transport, process supervision, and document sync policy. |\r\n.\\plans\\ide-core-architecture-spec-v0.1.md:967:| ADR-0012 | Select plugin runtime model, manifest schema, contribution points, and sandbox roadmap. |\r\n.\\plans\\ide-core-architecture-spec-v0.1.md:968:| ADR-0013 | Define file system abstraction, atomic save, conflict detection, and path policy. |\r\n.\\plans\\ide-core-architecture-spec-v0.1.md:969:| ADR-0014 | Define workspace state model, trust policy, watcher behavior, and file identity strategy. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:7:Phase 1 is accepted for starting Phase 2 renderer-backed foundation work. The phase reconciled accepted Phase 8 substrate evidence, selected a Windows-first renderer proof path, documented the desktop adapter ownership boundary, and added dependency-policy plus `xtask` enforcement so renderer dependencies stay out of every workspace package except `legion-desktop`.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:14:| `plans/evidence/gui-productization/gui-productization-baseline.md` | Accepted | Documents current CLI shell proof, projection-only UI, proposal-mediated saves, metadata-only defaults, renderer gap, and Phase 2 entry criteria. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:15:| `plans/evidence/gui-productization/renderer-decision-matrix.md` | Accepted | Compares GPUI, custom Rust-native GPU, egui/eframe, Slint, and Tauri/WRY using official documentation and repository constraints. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:16:| `plans/adrs/ADR-0002-ui-editor-rendering.md` | Accepted with Phase 1 update | Selects `eframe`/`egui` for Phase 2 foundation proof in `legion-desktop` only. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:19:| `plans/dependency-policy.md` | Accepted | Adds adapter-only renderer dependency policy and a conservative non-adapter renderer deny list. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:20:| `xtask/src/main.rs` | Accepted | Adds `renderer_dependency_gate_preserves_projection_boundary` and runtime `check-deps` validation across non-adapter workspace packages. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:25:- Phase 2 uses `legion-desktop` as the renderer-backed adapter crate name.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:26:- `eframe`/`egui` is the accepted Phase 2 foundation renderer proof path because it is Rust-first, Windows-capable, and has an AccessKit accessibility path.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:28:- Slint is the fallback if Phase 2 evidence shows egui cannot satisfy IME, clipboard, focus, accessibility, or high-DPI obligations.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:39:- `cargo test -p xtask renderer_dependency_gate_preserves_projection_boundary -- --exact: passed`\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:47:- [x] `legion-ui` remains projection-only and no non-adapter workspace package may depend on renderer/windowing crates.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:49:- [x] Dependency policy and `xtask` fail closed for renderer-boundary drift.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-1-renderer-readiness.md:54:- `eframe`/`egui` is accepted only for the Phase 2 foundation proof. It is not yet accepted as the final daily-driver editor renderer.\r\n.\\plans\\implementation-plan.md:138:1. Create [`plans/adrs/ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md) before implementation. It must decide lifecycle states, approval model, multi-file atomicity, rollback limits, partial-failure records, payload redaction, and ownership boundaries.\r\n.\\plans\\implementation-plan.md:197:1. Land ADR and evidence scaffolding: [`plans/adrs/ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md) and [`plans/evidence/phase-2/proposal-mutation-substrate.md`](plans/evidence/phase-2/proposal-mutation-substrate.md).\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\platform-parity\\P8-F5-T3-platform-parity-report.md:18:- `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test input_conformance clipboard_input_routes_to_the_buffer_through_the_egui_context -- --nocapture` — passed\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\platform-parity\\P8-F5-T3-platform-parity-report.md:27:- Clipboard: `input_conformance` routes paste text through the egui context and keeps clipboard payloads intact.\r\n.\\plans\\kanban\\legion-ga-backlog.toml:217:    verification = [\"cargo test -p legion-desktop --test headless_input\", \"cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit\"]\r\n.\\plans\\kanban\\legion-ga-backlog.toml:225:    title = \"Add a headless egui/eframe test harness seam without giving renderer product authority\"\r\n.\\plans\\kanban\\legion-ga-backlog.toml:230:    verification = [\"cargo test -p legion-desktop\", \"cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit\"]\r\n.\\plans\\kanban\\legion-ga-backlog.toml:286:    verification = [\"cargo test -p legion-desktop\", \"cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit\"]\r\n.\\plans\\kanban\\legion-ga-backlog.toml:288:    stop_condition = \"Do not introduce egui::TextEdit in the code canvas.\"\r\n.\\plans\\kanban\\legion-ga-backlog.toml:324:    title = \"Preserve/