are not user workflow proof. Product gates still require renderer-backed UX, real language/debug flows, extension-host cut lines, and installability evidence. |\r\n.\\plans\\product-readiness-ledger.md:42:| WS-P0 Phase 0 truth-repair closure (`evidence/production/WS-P0/phase-0-truth-repair-closure.md`; supersedes the interim `evidence/production/WS-P0/phase-0-gate-baseline.md` run) | Full standing gate set (check-deps, docs-hygiene, claim-audit, no-egui-textedit, verify-kanban-backlog, kanban_backlog tests, fmt, workspace check, full workspace test suite, clippy `-D warnings`, cargo-deny, evals/training pytest) re-run green on commit `fd715c5` (1522 tests passing, 0 failed). Task-to-commit table for Phase 0 Tasks 1-10 recorded there. | All rows below that cite `cargo test --workspace`/`cargo deny check`/`cargo clippy` pass counts | Some Readiness Matrix rows below still cite older raw pass counts (e.g. \"909 pass\") from earlier evidence captures; those counts are stale relative to the current workspace-wide total in the WS-P0 closure file, but the underlying targeted-test evidence each row cites remains current unless that row's own evidence file says otherwise. Treat the WS-P0 closure file as the current whole-workspace gate baseline; per-row promotion still requires each row's own named evidence. |\r\n.\\plans\\product-readiness-ledger.md:49:| Performance, UI, accessibility | PR-UI-001 renderer latency and input accessibility | p50/p95 input-to-paint budgets, IME, clipboard, focus, high contrast, screen-reader projection, font sizing, keyboard remapping, floating windows, and multi-monitor restore are tested against renderer-backed workflows. | Substrate validated | Whole-workspace pass counts: see WS-P0 closure (`plans/evidence/production/WS-P0/phase-0-truth-repair-closure.md`) rather than frozen historical totals. Targeted tests: `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test projection_rendering` (9 pass); `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test daily_editing_controls` (4 pass); `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test beta_workflow` (5 pass); `cargo test -p legion-app --test daily_editing_contracts` (7 pass); `plans/evidence/production/M5/WS18-T3-platform-parity-matrix.md`. WS-MANUAL-01 adds renderer-backed Manual input-to-paint perf evidence, input/focus/IME/clipboard tests, font/wrapping/degraded-mode renderer evidence, deterministic editor evidence, and an app-level Manual zero-egress smoke under `plans/evidence/production/WS-MANUAL-01/`. Promotion beyond substrate validated still requires current native platform accessibility/focus evidence across supported OSes. **Tier 1 progress (2026-07-21):** Backspace/Delete/Enter buffer mutation and OS clipboard write for copy/cut landed in `legion-desktop`/`legion-app` (see `plans/evidence/production/WS-P0/T1-A1-A2-editor-keys-clipboard.md`); tree depth cap raised 2→32. Status remains substrate validated pending broader a11y/focus/cross-OS product workflow evidence. GP-1 smoke (`cargo run -p xtask -- golden-path-1`) passed all 7 steps locally on Windows (single-OS; 3-OS CI pending via `legion-smoke.yml`), exercising AppComposition workspace open, product edit path, workspace search, terminal cargo-test gate, and git workflow. |\r\n.\\plans\\product-readiness-ledger.md:51:| Language, debug, test, SCM | PR-LANG-001 Rust language workflow | Rust LSP supervision covers completion, hover, diagnostics, rename, format, code actions, semantic tokens, folding, project-wide errors, and structural search through protocol DTOs. | Substrate validated | `cargo test -p legion-app --test structural_search_workflow` (1 pass); `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test language_terminal_workflow` (3 pass); `cargo test -p legion-app --test language_tooling_workflow` (5 pass). Full LSP completion/diagnostics product UX path is not yet validated. WS-LANG-01 adds: mock-gate tests across all four tiers — `cargo test -p legion-lsp` (lifecycle, transport, pump, discovery, read/write side contracts); `cargo test -p legion-protocol` (LSP health record, 6 pass); `cargo test -p legion-app` (rust_analyzer_download_policy 4 pass, rust_analyzer_session_handshake 3 pass, rust_analyzer_doc_sync 3 pass, rust_analyzer_read_requests 4 pass, language_stale_snapshot 4 pass, language_edit_proposal_routing 5 pass, language_restart_policy 3 pass); `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test language_health_view` (6 pass). Real rust-analyzer 1.95.0 single-OS smoke: `cargo run -p xtask -- rust-analyzer-smoke` passes both `--ignored` tests (lsp: initialize Fresh + ≥1 diagnostic via pump; app: completion/hover/definition/references/formatting/rename all well-formed JSON; restart policy exercised). Status is substrate-validated plus real single-OS (Windows) rust-analyzer smoke evidence available. 3-OS hosted CI smoke is deferred pending CI infrastructure, consistent with PR-REL-001 posture. See `plans/evidence/production/WS-LANG-01/WS-LANG-01-evidence.md`. PKT-LSP-B (branch `m8/lsp-read-ui`, commits 400396c..d678395) adds desktop product UI path: `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test completion_popup` (8 pass — CompletionDismiss, CompletionNext/Prev wrap, CompletionAccept via editor authority, stale popup on tab switch); `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test hover_definition` (7 pass — HoverDismiss, hover auto-show, last_hover_id pre-sync, tab-switch dismiss, GoToDefinition/NavigateToDefinition dispatch); T8 product composition smoke `rust_analyzer_product_composition_smoke` added to `rust_analyzer_workflow` suite (`#[ignore]` gated, exercises AppComposition startup → drain → health → problems → completion dispatch → stale discard). Promotion to product-workflow-validated is deferred until 3-OS real-server smoke and renderer-backed diagnostics panel UX evidence exists. Write-side (rename/code-action/format UI) is explicitly out of scope for this branch (P2.F1.T5). See `plans/evidence/production/M8/WS-LANG-01-product-ui-evidence.md`. GP-1 smoke (`cargo run -p xtask -- golden-path-1`) passed all 7 steps locally on Windows (single-OS; 3-OS CI pending via `legion-smoke.yml`): s2 LSP init 48ms, s3 diagnostic introduce/detect/fix/clear 2735ms, s5 terminal cargo-test exit-0 380ms, s6 git edit-stage-commit 974ms. PKT-LSP-C (branch `m8/lsp-write-side`, commits 87dd2e5..1192454) adds: lazy session start (T1, 6 tests), WorkspaceEdit → proposal translation (T2, 8 tests), circuit-breaker backoff UX with `LspSessionStatusProjection` countdown (T3, 5 tests), and stderr ring buffer as `LspSessionLogProjection` redacted projection (T4, 9 tests). All 16 standing gates passed on Windows. Status unchanged (substrate validated, single-OS). See `plans/evidence/production/M8/WS-LANG-01-write-side-evidence.md`. |\r\n.\\plans\\phase-status-ledger.md:21:| Phase 8 — Hardening | **Substrate accepted** | [`plans/evidence/phase-8/`](evidence/phase-8/) | Phase 8 runtime-hardening substrate acceptance: Accepted. The accepted substrate evidence includes `phase-8-architecture-map.md`, `platform-matrix-evidence.txt`, and `release-readiness-review.md`. This acceptance covers the runtime-hardening substrate (production remote transport, standalone local terminal, hosted telemetry/egress, raw-source retention, operational hardening) and is **not** a product GA or release-readiness sign-off. Product GA / release readiness is a separate, post-substrate track that requires additional GUI productization evidence (renderer-backed latency, IME, clipboard, focus, and accessibility), packaging/signing/auto-update decisions, and collaboration/admin/runtime-extension surface decisions; none of those reopen accepted Phase 8 substrate hardening. |\r\n.\\plans\\phase-status-ledger.md:38:| ADR-0010 — Air-gap mode | Accepted for Phase 4 provider policy | Air-gap and local-provider-only policy denies hosted providers, hosted telemetry, hosted embeddings, gateways, and unapproved outbound access. |\r\n.\\plans\\phase-status-ledger.md:39:| ADR-0015 — Streaming text viewport | Accepted | — |\r\n.\\plans\\phase-status-ledger.md:40:| ADR-0016 — Generalized proposal service | Accepted | Phase 2 accepted for save, text edit, closed-file, workspace-edit, edit-only code-action, and reversible batch proposal routes. Future runtime apply surfaces remain separately gated. |\r\n.\\plans\\phase-status-ledger.md:41:| ADR-0017 — Semantic fabric indexing | Accepted | Phase 3 evidence accepts the bounded semantic fabric runtime; vector indexing remains deferred. |\r\n.\\plans\\phase-status-ledger.md:42:| ADR-0018 — LSP runtime supervision | Accepted | Phase 3 evidence accepts metadata-only LSP supervision contracts and proposal-routed edit outputs; command/process/runtime expansion remains separately gated. |\r\n.\\plans\\phase-status-ledger.md:43:| ADR-0019 — WASM plugin runtime boundary | Accepted | Phase 5 evidence accepts the isolated plugin boundary for manifest validation, host-call capability checks, quotas, plugin storage, metadata-only observability, app-owned command invocation, and projection-only UI contributions. |\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md:51:- Current app architecture: `legion-protocol` contracts, `legion-app` authority/composition, `legion-ui` projection-only UI model, `legion-desktop` egui renderer, and subsystem crates for editor/text/project/LSP/terminal/AI/agent/plugin/remote/collaboration/security/storage/telemetry/retention.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md:185:- `legion-desktop`: renderer/adapter edge, no product authority.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md:283:2. MANUAL.02 Extend `xtask perf-harness` from skeleton to renderer-backed input-to-paint measurement.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md:284:3. MANUAL.03 Verify egui custom editor path avoids `TextEdit` regressions under `xtask no-egui-textedit`.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md:292:11. MANUAL.11 Add deterministic screenshot or textual renderer evidence for core editor states.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md:306:- `PR-UI-001` can move from substrate-validated toward product-workflow validated only after real renderer-backed input, focus, accessibility, and platform evidence exist.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md:894:cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.2.md:1034:| PR-UI-001 renderer latency/accessibility | Substrate validated | M8/M12 |\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:18:Legion IDE today is a **validated substrate, not a product**. Substrate phases 0–8 (and 13) are accepted with evidence: ~156K lines of Rust across 26 crates implement a disciplined control-first architecture — proposal-mediated mutation, projection-only UI, metadata-first observability, fail-closed saves, capability-brokered policy, phase-gated runtime activation. The protocol layer, editor/text substrate, workspace VFS + watcher, git CLI integration, provider routing (Ollama / llama.cpp / OpenAI-compatible), MCP client (stdio + streamable HTTP), agent state machine with worktree sandboxing, multi-worker DAG coordinator, encrypted secret storage, TLS transport, and an egui/eframe renderer are real and tested.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:55:4. **Invariant preservation.** Every workstream was checked against the authority boundaries in `docs/ARCHITECTURE_AUTHORITY_BOUNDARIES.md` and the dependency policy in `plans/dependency-policy.md`. No task in this plan requires `legion-ui` to take renderer dependencies, lets providers/workers mutate the workspace outside proposals, or persists raw payloads without consent.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:89:- **Renderer** (`legion-desktop`): real egui/eframe window, event loop, projection rendering for shell/panels/code canvas with a theme/token system, smoke + beta modes with evidence export. GUI rebuild phases 1–2 (foundation + editor syntax interactions) recently merged.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:118:Gold (production-shaped): `legion-protocol`, `legion-text`, `legion-editor`, `legion-security`, `legion-storage`, `legion-observability`, `legion-retention`, `legion-remote-transport`, `legion-agent`, `legion-platform`, `legion-tracker`, `legion-ui`, `legion-desktop` (renderer shell).\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:126:PR-UI-001/002 (renderer latency/accessibility product UX, 100MB streaming), PR-LANG-001/002 (LSP + DAP/test/SCM product UX), PR-AI-001/002 (context-manifest UX, real adversarial evals), PR-VSC-002 (runtime extension host — deferred cut line), PR-ENT-001/002 (remote transport, collaboration/admin — deferred cut lines), PR-REL-001 (signed installers, auto-update/rollback, crash reporting — in progress). Known limitations ledger additionally records: Windows-only GUI evidence, no signed installer, hosted-provider activation unsupported, native PTY hardening incomplete, autonomous apply unsupported.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:160:| Cross-platform parity + accessibility | 🟡 Windows evidence only; AccessKit via egui available | Extend (WS-18) |\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:234:| ADR-0032 | **Editor render path** | (a) custom egui widget (own line shaping/`Galley` cache, `show_rows` virtualization, never `TextEdit`); (b) migrate renderer to GPUI; (c) Slint fallback per ADR-0030 | **(a)**, with the renderer kept behind the existing projection boundary so GPUI remains a live fallback re-evaluated every 6 months. egui+AccessKit is currently *ahead* of GPUI/Floem on accessibility, which Legion needs for PR-UI-001. Codify \"no `egui::TextEdit` in the code canvas\" as a check-deps-style gate. | WS-01, WS-18 |\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:236:| ADR-0034 | **LSP client architecture** | (a) hand-rolled stdio JSON-RPC client à la Helix/Zed with per-language adapter registry; (b) async-lsp framework; (c) tower-lsp | **(a) with `lsp-types`**, matching how every shipping Rust editor did it and fitting Legion's actor-supervision contracts (ADR-0018). async-lsp acceptable if hand-rolling stalls. rust-analyzer protocol extensions (flycheck, runnables, inlay hints) are in-scope for the flagship language. | WS-03 |\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:237:| ADR-0035 | **Terminal stack** | (a) `alacritty_terminal` VTE grid + `legion-platform` PTY; (b) `alacritty_terminal` + `portable-pty`; (c) wezterm-term | **(a)**: keep the existing audited PTY layer (it already passes policy gates), add `alacritty_terminal` for terminal state, custom egui renderer. Structured terminal output feeds the agent harness — a real differentiator. | WS-05, WS-12 |\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:239:| ADR-0037 | **Semantic retrieval** | (a) tree-sitter AST-aware chunking + local embeddings (Ollama/llama.cpp-served) + embedded vector store (LanceDB or sqlite-vec) + Aider-style PageRank repo map, with **agentic search as the default** and the index as enhancement; (b) embeddings-first | **(a)**. Resolves the ADR-0005/ADR-0017 vector deferral. Store model name+version per index; lazy re-embed; repo map is the always-available deterministic fallback. Vector store choice (LanceDB vs sqlite-vec) decided by a 1-week spike. | WS-10 |\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:258:- 🔴 WS01.T1 **Codify the custom-widget boundary.** Audit `legion-desktop` view/bridge code; remove/forbid any `egui::TextEdit` use in the code canvas; define a `CodeCanvasPainter` seam (paint lines + handle input) so the editor core stays renderer-portable per ADR-0032. Add an xtask lint denying `TextEdit` in `legion-desktop` editor modules. *Accept:* gate exists and passes; canvas renders via custom painter only.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:262:- 🔴 WS01.T5 **IME + CJK correctness.** Wire egui IME events end-to-end (composition region rendering, candidate-window positioning); bundle/fallback fonts with CJK coverage; known egui IME issues (e.g., Tab consumed during composition) tracked with upstream links and local workarounds. *Accept:* manual IME test script on all 3 OSes recorded as evidence; automated composition-event tests.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:280:**Objective:** real language servers, supervised under the existing ADR-0018 contracts, with rust-analyzer as the flagship; stale LSP responses must never mutate buffers or workspaces. **Current state:** complete DTO surface + supervision contracts; no process ever launched. **Depends:** ADR-0034; WS-05.T1 (process plumbing shared); proposal routes (done). **Exit:** PR-LANG-001 product-validated; GP-1.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:285:- 🔴 WS03.T4 **Write-side features through proposals.** Rename, code actions, formatting (`textDocument/formatting` + range), organize imports — all materialize as workspace-edit proposals through the accepted Phase 2 routes (ADR-0016/0018 already gate this). *Accept:* rename across files lands as one reviewable, reversible proposal; audit-before-success verified.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:306:- 🔴 WS05.T2 **Terminal renderer.** Custom egui grid renderer (cells, styles, cursor, selection/copy, scrollback, URL detection), 12px terminal type per design tokens. *Accept:* vttest-subset conformance; TUI apps (htop-class) render usably.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:410:**Objective:** activate Phase 5's plugin boundary with a real VM, scoped to the Zed-validated launch set: grammars, themes, language-server adapters. **Current state:** manifest validation, capability gates, quotas — no VM. **Depends:** ADR-0019 (accepted), WS-02.T4. **Exit:** plugin-delivered grammar + theme + LSP adapter in production.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:487:3. **ADR-first for boundary changes.** Tree-sitter/syntax crate placement, sandbox layer, WASM VM, ACP host, and any new renderer dependency all require dependency-policy updates + ADR acceptance *before* code merges (per `plans/dependency-policy.md`).\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:490:6. **Upstream hygiene.** egui/AccessKit/tree-sitter/alacritty_terminal issues encountered get tracked links in-repo; budget ~10% time for upstream fixes rather than local forks.\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:510:| R1 | **egui can't hit editor feel/IME bar** even with custom widget | Med | High | ADR-0032 keeps renderer behind projection boundary; GPUI fallback re-evaluated semi-annually; IME issues tracked upstream with workarounds; accessibility currently *favors* egui |\r\n.\\plans\\legion-production-master-plan-v0.1.md:609:Technology stack (primary sources verified 2026-06-09): boringcactus.com 2025 Rust GUI survey; egui issues #3086/#7485 + AccessKit integration; zed.dev blogs (Rope & SumTree, CRDTs, extensions/WIT, GPUI README); lapce/floem; loro.dev + diamond-types; tree-sitter; rust-analyzer book; async-lsp/tower-lsp crates; helix LSP architecture; alacritty_terminal + portable-pty crates; BurntSushi ripgrep-as-library discussion #2509; tantivy; LanceDB/sqlite-vec materials; aider repo-map; modelcontextprotocol.io spec (2025-11-25) + transport-futures blog + rust-sdk (rmcp); platform.claude.com docs (pricing, prompt caching, structured outputs, count_tokens, batch); OpenAI Responses migration guide; Codex sandboxing internals (Landlock/seccomp/Seatbelt); gitoxide README (write-path gaps); jj-vcs/jj; rcodesign distribution guide; cargo-dist; velopack; Embark crash-handler/minidumper + sentry-rust-minidump; Mozilla rust-minidump.\r\n.\\plans\\remaining-implementation-tasks-plan-v0.1.md:29:| Editor and text substrate | Phase 1 evidence records degraded large-file mode, viewport projection, chunk descriptors, and non-blocking fake consumers in [`plans/evidence/phase-1/editor-text-substrate.md`](plans/evidence/phase-1/editor-text-substrate.md:7). | Phase 1 is accepted enough to unblock proposal and semantic work; renderer-backed UI measurements remain follow-up evidence, not a blocker. |\r\n.\\plans\\remaining-implementation-tasks-plan-v0.1.md:60:2. Update [`plans/adrs/ADR-0002-ui-editor-rendering.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0002-ui-editor-rendering.md:3) from provisional to accepted with reservations or explicitly supersede it with a renderer integration ADR, because Spike 1A is now accepted with reservations in [`plans/spikes/SPIKE-001A-result.md`](plans/spikes/SPIKE-001A-result.md:60).\r\n.\\plans\\remaining-implementation-tasks-plan-v0.1.md:63:5. Reconcile old required ADR identifiers in [`plans/ide-core-architecture-spec-v0.1.md`](plans/ide-core-architecture-spec-v0.1.md:960) with newer ADRs such as [`plans/adrs/ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md:1), [`plans/adrs/ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md:1), and [`plans/adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:1).\r\n.\\plans\\proposal-execution-lsp-runtime-gating-plan-v0.1.md:20:- Capture LSP runtime gating requirements from [`ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md`](adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:1).\r\n.\\plans\\proposal-execution-lsp-runtime-gating-plan-v0.1.md:36:6. [`ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md`](adrs/ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md:1) accepts the generalized proposal service direction, including universal lifecycle states, batch atomicity, rollback limits, deny-by-default validation, audit-before-success, metadata-only persistence, and projection-only UI constraints.\r\n.\\plans\\proposal-execution-lsp-runtime-gating-plan-v0.1.md:119:- [`ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md`](adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:13) is accepted for governance and implementation gating, not as proof that runtime behavior exists.\r\n.\\plans\\proposal-execution-lsp-runtime-gating-plan-v0.1.md:124:- LSP ownership stays outside UI, editor text ownership, and workspace VFS authority as specified by [`ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md`](adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:17).\r\n.\\plans\\proposal-execution-lsp-runtime-gating-plan-v0.1.md:130:- Every request must carry workspace identity, file identity, buffer identity when open, snapshot identity, buffer version, language id, timeout budget, correlation, causality, and cancellation token per [`ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md`](adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:25).\r\n.\\plans\\proposal-execution-lsp-runtime-gating-plan-v0.1.md:136:- Request queues must be bounded per server, workspace, and feature class as required by [`ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md`](adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:41).\r\n.\\plans\\proposal-execution-lsp-runtime-gating-plan-v0.1.md:138:- Timeouts must produce typed timeout, stale, degraded, unavailable, or cancelled outcomes rather than panics or blocking retries, consistent with [`ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md`](adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:49).\r\n.\\plans\\proposal-execution-lsp-runtime-gating-plan-v0.1.md:146:- If LSP output cannot be represented safely as proposal DTOs with target coverage, version preconditions, capability requirements, rollback expectations, preview summaries, and privacy metadata, it must be denied with metadata-only diagnostics per [`ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md`](adrs/ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:63).\r\n.\\plans\\semantic-index-boundary-remediation-plan-v0.1.md:18:| Repository discovery authority | [`RepositoryScanConfig`](crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:694) owns a live root path, bounds, and ignore patterns, while [`RepositoryScanner`](crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:776) canonicalizes the root with [`fs::canonicalize`](crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:794), reads ignore files with [`read_gitignore_patterns()`](crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:799), walks directories with [`fs::read_dir`](crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:843), reads file contents with [`fs::read`](crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:902), and mints [`FileId`](crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:910). | [`legion-index`](crates/legion-index/src/lib.rs:1) is acting as filesystem discovery authority instead of consuming workspace-authoritative discovery metadata. This conflicts with [`ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md:36), which requires metadata-first discovery and workspace-discovered ignore decisions. |\r\n.\\plans\\semantic-index-boundary-remediation-plan-v0.1.md:31:5. Vector indexing remains deferred exactly as stated in [`ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md`](plans/adrs/ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md:82) and [`predictive-semantic-fabric.md`](plans/evidence/phase-3/predictive-semantic-fabric.md:82).\r\n.\\plans\\SPIKE-000-platform-boundary-proof.md:61:| `shell_title` | Legacy static spike label | Window ownership, renderer state, shell model |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\phase-5\\plugin-architecture-map.md:20:- ADR: `plans/adrs/ADR-0019-wasm-plugin-runtime.md`\r\n.\\plans\\spikes\\SPIKE-001A-result.md:36:- p50: the current accepted non-ignored harness does not emit p50 in captured output; this is a reporting reservation for the renderer-backed harness.\r\n.\\plans\\spikes\\SPIKE-001A-result.md:44:- GPU utilization, compositor frame variance, native IME, native clipboard, native focus, and accessibility tree validation are renderer-integration follow-ups.\r\n.\\plans\\spikes\\SPIKE-001A-result.md:49:- If renderer-backed p95 input-to-paint exceeds the accepted budget, keep UI projection-only and defer renderer expansion until a bounded draw pipeline is proven.\r\n.\\plans\\spikes\\SPIKE-001A-result.md:55:- UI/runtime owner: accepted with renderer reservations.\r\n.\\plans\\SPIKE-001A-native-shell-proof.md:26:| Frame variance | No compositor-backed renderer is present; projection-only shell tests completed without state instability | Accepted with renderer reservation |\r\n.\\plans\\SPIKE-001A-native-shell-proof.md:28:| GPU utilization | GPU renderer path is not exercised because UI is projection-only in this phase | Accepted with renderer reservation |\r\n.\\plans\\SPIKE-001A-native-shell-proof.md:30:| IME | Native IME path is reserved for renderer integration; command intent boundaries are now renderer-independent | Accepted with renderer reservation |\r\n.\\plans\\SPIKE-001A-native-shell-proof.md:31:| Clipboard | Clipboard path is reserved for renderer integration; command intent boundaries are now renderer-independent | Accepted with renderer reservation |\r\n.\\plans\\SPIKE-001A-native-shell-proof.md:32:| Focus | Focus path is reserved for renderer integration; shell state no longer owns editor session state | Accepted with renderer reservation |\r\n.\\plans\\SPIKE-001A-native-shell-proof.md:34:| Accessibility | Accessibility tree generation is reserved for renderer integration; projection snapshots provide deterministic source data | Accepted with renderer reservation |\r\n.\\plans\\SPIKE-001A-native-shell-proof.md:35:| Platform notes | Windows 11 validation passed; macOS/Linux parity remains part of later renderer validation | Accepted with parity reservation |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\phase-0\\native-shell-proof-summary.md:25:| p50 latency | Current accepted harness does not emit a p50 value in captured CI output | Accepted as a reporting gap, not a failing gate | Add p50 emission when the renderer-backed measurement harness lands |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\phase-0\\native-shell-proof-summary.md:26:| p95 latency | Current accepted harness asserts p95 below 250ms | Accepted | Use renderer-backed p95 once native painting is integrated |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\phase-0\\native-shell-proof-summary.md:29:| GPU utilization | The current shell proof exercises projection-only state and no GPU renderer | Accepted with reservations | GPU utilization is reserved for the native renderer integration proof |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\phase-0\\native-shell-proof-summary.md:31:| IME | UI command dispatch is projection-only and does not own editor state | Accepted with reservations | Native IME event-loop validation remains a renderer integration follow-up |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\phase-0\\native-shell-proof-summary.md:32:| Clipboard | UI command parsing and dispatch intent paths compile and test cleanly | Accepted with reservations | Native clipboard API proof remains a renderer integration follow-up |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\phase-0\\native-shell-proof-summary.md:33:| Focus | Shell state is projection-only and receives snapshots rather than owning editor sessions | Accepted with reservations | Native window focus measurement remains a renderer integration follow-up |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\phase-0\\native-shell-proof-summary.md:35:| Accessibility | Projection snapshots are deterministic and renderer-independent | Accepted with reservations | Native accessibility tree integration remains a renderer integration follow-up |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-5-control-trust-assisted-ai.md:39:| R-013 Performance and reliability evidence | The final full gates below, existing Phase 2-4 evidence, and Phase 5 safety evidence prove the GUI track preserves dependency policy, formatting, compile health, workspace tests, clippy policy, save conflict/dirty text preservation, projection-only UI/desktop boundaries, and metadata-only trust surfaces. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-3-daily-editing-mvp.md:9:Phase 3 is accepted for the Daily Editing MVP scope. The accepted scope is local daily editing in the renderer-backed desktop adapter: tabs, explorer controls, cursor/selection/scrolling, undo/redo routing, save all, dirty-close prompts, bounded active-file/workspace search, metadata-only session restore, visible conflict preservation, and large-file degraded guardrails.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-3-daily-editing-mvp.md:27:- `legion-ui` remains projection-only. The live boundary check for `legion-app`, `legion-editor`, `legion-project`, `legion-storage`, `legion-desktop`, `eframe`, and `egui` references in `crates/legion-ui/Cargo.toml` and `crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs` returned no matches.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-smoke.md:12:`cargo run -p legion-desktop -- --smoke --workspace . --file Cargo.toml --duration-ms 1500 --evidence plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-smoke.md`\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:3:## Phase 2 renderer foundation: Accepted\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:7:Phase 2 is accepted for renderer-backed foundation mode. The accepted scope is a real desktop adapter that launches a native eframe window, renders current `legion-ui` shell projections, translates renderer actions into app-owned commands or app requests, and records bounded renderer smoke evidence. This is not acceptance of the daily editing MVP, full native platform integration, or accessibility proof; those remain Phase 3 and Phase 6 obligations.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:13:| `.planning/phases/01-baseline-reconciliation-and-renderer-decision/01-05-RESULT.md` | Complete | Phase 1 readiness accepted for Phase 2; dependency, format, workspace check, UI/app check, and renderer-gate evidence recorded. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:14:| `.planning/phases/02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode/02-01-RESULT.md` | Complete | `legion-desktop` workspace crate added with renderer dependencies limited to the desktop adapter and verified by `xtask check-deps`. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:15:| `.planning/phases/02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode/02-02-RESULT.md` | Complete | Projection renderer panels implemented and covered by projection rendering tests. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:16:| `.planning/phases/02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode/02-03-RESULT.md` | Complete | Desktop action bridge implemented with no app/editor/workspace internals in the bridge. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:17:| `.planning/phases/02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode/02-04-RESULT.md` | Complete | `DesktopRuntime` routes open/edit/save/rejection/quit through `AppComposition` and app-owned command dispatch. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:18:| `.planning/phases/02-renderer-backed-foundation-mode/02-05-RESULT.md` | Complete | Timed renderer smoke harness and platform smoke evidence recorded. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:19:| `plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-smoke.md` | Present | Smoke status passed with timing and platform fields. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:23:- `crates/legion-desktop/Cargo.toml` is the only crate manifest in the accepted Phase 2 surface that declares `eframe` and `egui`.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:24:- `plans/dependency-policy.md` explicitly authorizes renderer/windowing dependencies only for `legion-desktop` and forbids renderer/windowing crates in `legion-ui` and core crates.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:25:- `xtask/src/main.rs` enforces the renderer dependency gate; the live `cargo run -p xtask -- check-deps` gate passed.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:29:- `deny.toml` now documents the reviewed Phase 2 renderer transitive license set. `cargo deny check` exits 0 after that policy remediation, with duplicate-crate warnings still reported at warning level.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:34:- Smoke launch path: `cargo run -p legion-desktop -- --smoke --workspace . --file Cargo.toml --duration-ms 1500 --evidence plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-smoke.md`.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:41:Source: `plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-smoke.md`.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:83:| `cargo deny check` | passed with warnings | Advisories, bans, licenses, and sources ok; duplicate-crate warnings remain warning-level for the renderer/winit graph. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:84:| `cargo run -p legion-desktop -- --smoke --workspace . --file Cargo.toml --duration-ms 1500 --evidence plans/evidence/gui-productization/phase-2-renderer-smoke.md` | passed | Recorded in Plan 02-05 smoke evidence; not rerun in 02-06 because the committed smoke evidence was present and complete. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-2-renderer-foundation.md:102:- `cargo deny check` exits 0 but still reports duplicate-crate warnings in the renderer/windowing/transitive graph. This is policy-permitted today and should be monitored as renderer dependencies evolve.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-6-input-conformance.md:54:- The runtime font fallback now searches common host OS CJK font locations and appends the first match to egui's proportional and monospace font families.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-6-input-conformance.md:55:- The tab-suppression workaround is intentionally local and documented against upstream egui IME issues so it can be removed when the backend behavior fully stabilizes.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0019-wasm-plugin-runtime.md:1:# ADR-0019: WASM Plugin Runtime Boundary\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:1:# ADR-0018: LSP Runtime Supervision\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0018-lsp-runtime-supervision.md:11:The proposal substrate accepted in [`ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md`](ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md:1) is the only allowed route for mutations produced by LSP features. The streaming text substrate accepted in [`ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md`](ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md:1) supplies snapshot descriptors, chunk leases, and non-blocking event fanout. LSP supervision must consume those contracts without blocking editor input or saves.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md:1:# ADR-0017: Semantic Fabric Indexing\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md:11:This activation depends on the Phase 1 streaming text substrate in [`ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md`](ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md:1) and the Phase 2 proposal substrate in [`ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md`](ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md:1). The index must consume text snapshots, file identities, and event metadata without reintroducing full-source UI projection or direct workspace mutation.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0017-semantic-fabric-indexing.md:25:- Any mutation suggested by semantic analysis, refactoring preview, LSP rename, formatting, or code actions must route through [`WorkspaceProposal`](../../crates/legion-protocol/src/lib.rs:1343) and the generalized proposal lifecycle accepted in [`ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md`](ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md:15).\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0016-generalized-proposal-service.md:1:# ADR-0016: Generalized Proposal Service\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md:1:# ADR-0015: Streaming Text, Chunked Snapshots, and Viewport Projection\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md:40:Projection consumers may request a new viewport, scroll anchor, or command dispatch intent, but projection consumers do not mutate text, own editor sessions, own workspace actors, or persist files. [`Shell`](crates/legion-ui/src/ui.rs:228) remains a projection renderer and command-intent surface.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0015-streaming-text-viewport.md:113:- **Positive**: UI remains a projection-only renderer and can explain degraded mode without owning text or persistence.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0010-air-gap-mode.md:1:# ADR-0010: Define Air-Gap Mode and Outbound Network Enforcement Model\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:9:Phase 1 established that the existing product substrate is accepted through Phase 8 and that GUI productization is a new renderer-backed track. `legion-app` remains the app authority and current CLI proof. `legion-ui` remains projection-only: it accepts snapshots and emits `CommandDispatchIntent` values without mutating editor or workspace state.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:11:ADR-0002 now selects `eframe`/`egui` for the Phase 2 Windows-first desktop foundation proof. The renderer decision does not authorize renderer dependencies in `legion-ui` or core crates.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:15:Introduce a planned desktop adapter crate named `legion-desktop` in Phase 2.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:17:`legion-desktop` is an adapter, not a new authority layer. It may own the process entry point, native window, renderer resources, frame timing instrumentation, native input translation, clipboard bridge, file-dialog request forwarding, focus/IME integration, and accessibility tree publication. It must consume app/UI projections and route user actions back to app-owned command handling.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:28:- Renderer crates authorized by ADR-0002 and `plans/dependency-policy.md`, initially `eframe` and `egui` for the Phase 2 foundation proof.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:30:Core crates must not depend on `legion-desktop`. `legion-ui` must not depend on `legion-desktop`, `legion-app`, renderer/windowing crates, editor, project, storage, provider, telemetry, terminal, remote, retention, plugin, collaboration, or AI runtime crates.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:41:The adapter is a trust-boundary surface because it bridges native OS input, clipboard, IME, file dialogs, accessibility publication, and renderer callbacks into app-owned commands. Every action that can mutate files, buffers, terminal state, provider state, plugin state, collaboration state, or remote state must cross an app/protocol boundary with non-zero correlation and causality metadata where applicable.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:49:- `xtask` and dependency policy can fail closed if `legion-ui` or core crates gain renderer dependencies.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:55:- `plans/dependency-policy.md` documents the `legion-desktop` boundary and renderer dependency gate.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:56:- `xtask/src/main.rs` includes `renderer_dependency_gate_preserves_projection_boundary`.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0030-desktop-adapter-boundary.md:57:- Phase 2 must prove p50/p95 input-to-paint, IME, clipboard, focus, high-DPI, and accessibility behavior before claiming renderer-backed GUI acceptance.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:8:(option (a), custom egui code-canvas widget with the renderer kept behind the\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:9:existing projection boundary). The renderer boundary is enforced by the\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:10:`cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit` gate, which is recorded in\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:12:`xtask/tests/no_egui_textedit.rs`. No amendments to the master-plan\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:18:The Production Master Plan defines WS-01 as the first critical-path workstream for a credible manual editor. The current renderer is an egui/eframe projection shell with theme/token plumbing, but the code canvas must not regress into an `egui::TextEdit`-owned editor because that would violate the projection-only UI boundary and make editor portability, virtualization, IME handling, and large-file safety harder to enforce.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:20:ADR-0030 keeps the desktop adapter behind a projection boundary. This ADR chooses the concrete render-path strategy for M1 while preserving the ability to re-evaluate GPUI or another renderer later.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:24:Legion will continue with a custom egui code-canvas widget for M1. The code canvas owns painting and input translation only: shaped visible lines, gutters, selections, cursors, decorations, IME composition, and command intents. It does not own editor sessions, workspace state, save authority, or mutation authority.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:26:`egui::TextEdit` is forbidden in the desktop code-canvas/editor render path. A repository gate (`cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit`) enforces this boundary for the current code-canvas module (`crates/legion-desktop/src/view.rs`) and can expand as that surface is split into dedicated painter modules.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:28:The custom painter should introduce a `CodeCanvasPainter` seam so the editor remains renderer-portable. GPUI remains a live fallback to re-evaluate after M1 evidence, not a dependency to add during M0.\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:38:- `cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit`\r\n.\\plans\\adrs\\ADR-0032-editor-render-path.md:39:- `cargo test -p xtask --test no_egui_textedit`\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:4:Scope: Manual editor feel, rendering, input, focus, font, wrapping, degraded-mode messaging, deterministic renderer evidence, and zero-egress smoke.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:19:| MANUAL.02 renderer-backed input-to-paint | `target/perf-harness/perf_report.toml`; `cargo run -p xtask -- perf-harness`; `cargo run -p xtask -- verify-perf-harness`; `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test manual_perf` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:20:| MANUAL.03 custom editor path / no TextEdit | `cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit`; `cargo test -p xtask --test no_egui_textedit` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:25:| MANUAL.08 font fallback diagnostics | `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test manual_renderer_evidence font_fallback_diagnostics_are_projected_without_raw_font_paths -- --exact` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:26:| MANUAL.09 line wrapping policy | `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test manual_renderer_evidence line_wrapping_policy_keeps_viewport_math_stable -- --exact` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:28:| MANUAL.11 deterministic renderer evidence | `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test manual_renderer_evidence deterministic_renderer_evidence_covers_core_editor_states -- --exact` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:35:Rectangular selection is intentionally deferred out of the v1 product-workflow gate until the editor exposes a rectangular selection command with stable protocol DTOs, keyboard/mouse gestures, and renderer evidence. The Manual UI must not advertise rectangular selection as complete.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:43:| `rg -n \"TextEdit\\|CodeCanvas\\|manual editor\\|FrameTimingRecorder\\|perf-harness\\|zero-egress\\|egress\" crates xtask plans -g \"*.rs\" -g \"*.md\" -g \"*.toml\"` | Pass | Confirmed existing renderer/timing/gate/manual trust surfaces, including `CodeCanvasPainter`, `FrameTimingRecorder`, `xtask no-egui-textedit`, Manual mode projection rows, perf-harness evidence, and egress policy references. Zero-egress hits are plan/evidence targets until MANUAL.12 creates smoke evidence. Output also included expected incidental protocol `TextEdit` and historical evidence matches, so this ledger records the signal summary rather than the full search output. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:50:| `cargo run -p xtask -- perf-harness` | Pass | Generated `target/perf-harness/perf_report.toml` at git `04207b9db7f69bdccbc5ced0abd8d5416bb5b7f6`: 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; `manual.renderer_input_to_paint` p50 2077 us / p95 18223 us under the 32 ms budget. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:52:| `cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit` | Pass | Phase 10 rerun passed; custom Manual editor path still avoids `egui::TextEdit`. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:53:| `cargo test -p xtask --test no_egui_textedit` | Pass | Phase 10 rerun passed: 6 passed, 0 failed. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:56:| `cargo test -p legion-desktop --test manual_renderer_evidence` | Pass | Phase 10 rerun passed: 4 passed, 0 failed; covers MANUAL.08, MANUAL.09, MANUAL.11, and renderer zero-egress trust-boundary rows. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:70:`PR-UI-001` remains bounded by the evidence above. Do not mark it product-workflow validated unless all required Manual input, focus, accessibility, renderer-backed performance, platform, and zero-egress checks pass in the current tree.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\WS-MANUAL-01-evidence.md:76:- WS-MANUAL-02 owns full large-workspace and 100MB streaming performance; WS-MANUAL-01 only improves visible capability reduction and renderer/input evidence.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\manual-mode-zero-egress.md:13:Companion renderer-model check:\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\manual-mode-zero-egress.md:15:`cargo test -p legion-desktop --test manual_renderer_evidence manual_renderer_evidence_names_zero_egress_trust_boundary -- --exact`\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\manual-mode-zero-egress.md:22:- The desktop renderer evidence test must assert Manual trust-boundary rows that name no provider dispatch and no agent context.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\editor-latency-budgets.md:10:| Keypress to paint, normal buffer | p50 | <= 16 ms | `xtask perf-harness` renderer-backed Manual measurement | `target/perf-harness/perf_report.toml` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-MANUAL-01\\editor-latency-budgets.md:11:| Keypress to paint, normal buffer | p95 | <= 32 ms | `xtask perf-harness` renderer-backed Manual measurement | `target/perf-harness/perf_report.toml` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-P0\\WS-P0-rebaseline-evidence-refresh.md:34:| `cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit` | Pass | No egui::TextEdit in code canvas |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-P0\\T2-local-first-provider-preference.md:22:cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-P0\\T2-byok-ui-sandbox-enforcement.md:11:| **no-egui-textedit** | Interactive fields moved to `view/interactive_fields.rs` (outside canvas gate scan) — also relocates terminal input TextEdit that was violating the gate |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-P0\\T2-byok-ui-sandbox-enforcement.md:17:cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-P0\\phase-0-truth-repair-closure.md:27:| 4 | `cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit` | 03:26:01 | 03:26:04 | 0 | `no-egui-textedit checks passed` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-P0\\phase-0-gate-baseline.md:175:| 3 | `cargo run -p xtask -- no-egui-textedit` | repo root | 01:45:05 | 01:45:05 | 0 | `no-egui-textedit checks passed` |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\WS-P0\\campaign-closeout-2026-07-21.md:38:Local targeted suites exercised throughout the campaign (assist, control trust, delegated, debug, LSP read-side, desktop input/sandbox/provider keys, docs-hygiene, claim-audit, no-egui-textedit). Full standing 20-gate matrix remains the merge authority per `AGENT