nchanged)\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:1:# Renderer Decision Matrix\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:10:- egui README: https://github.com/emilk/egui\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:29:Phase 2 needs a Windows-first desktop shell that can open a real window, render current projection DTOs, route input to app-owned commands, and produce measurable renderer evidence without moving editor/workspace/proposal authority into UI.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:40:- The approach does not require webview or renderer state to own editor text, save state, proposal lifecycle, provider calls, telemetry storage, or workspace mutation.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:48:| egui/eframe | egui README says eframe supports Web, Linux, Mac, Windows, and Android; egui includes widgets, text editing, copy/paste, windows/panels, custom painting, and accessibility via AccessKit. eframe defaults include accesskit, winit, wgpu, x11/wayland, and clipboard/windowing integrations through the framework stack. | Good Phase 2 foundation fit: Rust-first, fast to integrate, native Windows path through eframe, easy projection rendering, custom painting hooks, AccessKit path, and no JavaScript state split. | Immediate-mode layout is not the final editor architecture; native look is a non-goal; deeper IME/editor text behavior must be proven before daily-driver claims. | Selected for Phase 2 foundation adapter proof, scoped to `legion-desktop` only. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:50:| Tauri/WRY | Tauri docs describe Rust plus HTML in a WebView with message passing; WRY supports Windows/macOS/Linux and uses WebView2 on Windows. | Mature desktop packaging and native bridge story; strong if a web UI already existed. | Reintroduces webview state split and browser/UI boundary for an IDE whose current architecture is Rust protocol projection plus app authority. Harder to preserve the no-renderer-ownership rule by default. | Reserved for auxiliary/non-core surfaces only. Not selected for editor shell. |\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:54:Phase 2 should implement the first renderer-backed desktop proof as a new `legion-desktop` adapter using `eframe`/`egui` plus the framework-provided native integration stack. This does not move `legion-ui` or core crates to egui. `legion-ui` remains projection-only, and `legion-desktop` consumes `ShellProjectionSnapshot` and emits `CommandDispatchIntent` through `legion-app`.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:60:Fallback from eframe/egui to Slint or a custom winit/wgpu/AccessKit adapter if any of the following cannot be proven in Phase 2:\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:68:- The adapter requires `legion-ui` or core crates to depend on renderer/windowing crates.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\renderer-decision-matrix.md:74:- Add `legion-desktop` as the only crate allowed to depend on `eframe`, `egui`, and renderer/windowing integration crates.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-8-advanced-surface-smoke.md:47:- `legion-desktop` owns renderer and smoke harness orchestration only.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\gui-productization\\phase-8-advanced-platform-gui-ga.md:13:The GUI track must preserve app/protocol/runtime authority boundaries. `legion-ui` remains projection-only, `legion-desktop` remains renderer and adapter-local state only, and mutation-capable plugin, collaboration, remote, delegated task, language, terminal, provider, storage, and security behavior remains proposal-mediated or policy-gated outside UI ownership.\r\n.\\plans\\evidence\\production\\M1\\M1-milestone-acceptance.md:25:| WS-05.T1–T3 | Done | Terminal PTY wiring, renderer, and terminal workflow coverage 